{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code","id":1154066,"title":"Hunter 2ED: The Code","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-29T23:44:48-07:00","id":1154066,"title":"Hunter 2ED: The Code","content":"Monica asked that all discussion on The Code be moved to a different thread, so I thought someone should create one. With that in mind here's what I'd like to see changed about the Code from the playtest draft.<br /> <br /> 1) No in setting universal morality. Simply put put it breaks my suspension of disbelief. If you want to have a default code that Compacts/Conspiracies modify I could see that working but please make it clear that it's a game mechanic and not something that exists inside the setting.<br /> <br /> 2) don't make &quot;monsters don't deserve to exist&quot; the default. There's definitely room for that, but looking at the corebook alone I don't think: the Long Night, Network Zero, Null Mysteries, the Loyalists of Thule, the Ascending Ones, or the Lucifuge will agree with that view. And the MM would make an exception for angels and god. That's over half the groups.<br /> <br /> More than that, in many respects Hunters are justified. Monsters do prey on humanity, standing up for the oppressed is laudable. So to say that standing up against monstrous oppression turns you into a Nazi-ish monster who dehumanises anyone with supernatural power is a message that alienates me.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying there's any moral obligation to avoid a problematic message. Fiction doesn't have to fit anyone's morality, least of all mine. (and there's definitely room for hunters like Chiron who are as bad or worse than their prey) All I'm saying is that this is the message the &quot;call a spade a spade&quot; sidebar is saying to me and since I doubt that's the intent perhaps it needs revising until the message matches the intent.<br /> <br /> 3) The code should be flexible enough to ensure behaving like a typical member of your organisation will not trigger Breaking Points. A Member of Les Mysteries should be able to create a Code that says they can: learn Rites, make bargains with spirits that involve acting against a human's interests, refuse to aid or oppose hunters who've hunting spirits, ignore monsters they consider outside their purvew, (and hunt spirits who're misbehaving) without a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that they have to be psychologically healthy. Someone who willingly let's spirits possess them is, at least by modern western standards, questionable at best. What I am saying is that breaking points are the wrong mechanic to represent the drawbacks of any kind of questionable behaviour that's encouraged by your Compact or Conspiracy. A Breaking Point should represent a significant moment in your charachter's charachter development. For business as normal, something like Tells or Vampires Banes would work better.<br /> <br /> (Building on from point 2. It should be possible to play that Les Mysteries as a Tier 1 independent Hunter. You could do it reasonably without access to an Endowment by using the Medium Merit from the Chronicle of Darkness core book.)<br /> <br /> 4) Building on from point 2. A bit more naunce in the social relationships between groups please. A VASCU hunter who barely has a Code and acts like a normal if psychic FBI agent should get a much friendlier reception from The Union that a surgically modified Cheriton Hunter even though both would have modified their code from the default. (Assuming there is still a default).<br /> <br /> And now I'm off to the airport <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll see if I'm able to reply from abroad or not.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-30-2017, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T01:29:46-07:00","id":1154072,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code\">What's wrong with the other thread?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T01:57:58-07:00","id":1154074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154072#post1154072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code\">What's wrong with the other thread?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>We were specifically asked to move the topic to a different thread so the original thread can focus on the intended topic of actually playing the playtest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T02:03:45-07:00","id":1154076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154074#post1154074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were specifically asked to move the topic to a different thread so the original thread can focus on the intended topic of actually playing the playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except the thread I linked wasn't the Hunter Playtest thread it was the old thread where the 2e Code was first revealed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T03:13:42-07:00","id":1154081,"title":"","content":"I agree with all <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> points. I just want to point my previous compromise idea - <b>Leave The Code the way it's in playtest now, but</b> <b>let each Hunter modify his own Code by changing default Breaking Points - let's say, up to 5 of BP. Each change of BP will alienate him a bit to other Hunters not sharing his own BP by -1 penalty to interactions. </b><br /> <br /> In that way, those 'we must save monsters' groups will be generally a bit alienated by rest of the Hunters Orgs - that is correct both in HtV 1E lore AND in TV series like <b>Supernatural </b>- where Sam is constantly nagged by Dean because 'they are to save humans, not monsters' - and still Sam is not going to Slasherdom only because he wants to <i>rescue</i> monsters too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T03:48:29-07:00","id":1154083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code#post1154066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) No in setting universal morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're good on this point. Because that's not what integrity is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T04:32:03-07:00","id":1154088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154083#post1154083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we're good on this point. Because that's not what integrity is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that is what The Code currently looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:18:02-07:00","id":1154093,"title":"","content":"No, it looks like a coping mechanism. Integrity 7+ talks about drawing &quot;a clear line between themselves and the monsters they despise&quot; but we all know that line <i>doesn't really exist.</i> <br /> <br /> Monsters have families, jobs, and all that. They're people, just like anyone else. Falling integrity happens in part when hunters <i>realise this</i>. It blurs the line. A low integrity hunter can <i>totally</i> protect an innocent psychic from a mundane killer. And they should. But at higher integrity this violates the lie they've told themselves to stay sane. That there's <i>us </i>and <i>them. </i>The code isn't a &quot;Universal Morality&quot;. If anything it's the opposite. A shield that lets hunters do what needs to be done, that their actual morality threatens to slowly weather away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:18:35-07:00","id":1154094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...except the thread I linked wasn't the Hunter Playtest thread it was the old thread where the 2e Code was first revealed? </div> </div> </div>.... Crap, there already was a thread for that? Sorry, Tasti. I had no idea. My guess is neither did Raven. I guess we'll have to decide if we keep going there or use that old thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) don't make &quot;monsters don't deserve to exist&quot; the default. There's definitely room for that, but looking at the corebook alone I don't think: the Long Night, Network Zero, Null Mysteries, the Loyalists of Thule, the Ascending Ones, or the Lucifuge will agree with that view. And the MM would make an exception for angels and god. That's over half the groups. </div> </div> </div>Raven, I agree with most of your points, but out of curiosity: why do you include the Long Night here? Aren't they a &quot;MONSTERS ARE ALL DEMONS AND MUST DIE!&quot; Kind of compact? Or did I get their section completely wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it looks like a coping mechanism. Integrity 7+ talks about drawing &quot;a clear line between themselves and the monsters they despise&quot; but we all know that line <i>doesn't really exist.</i><br /> <br /> Monsters have families, jobs, and all that. They're people, just like anyone else. Falling integrity happens in part when hunters <i>realise this</i>. It blurs the line. A low integrity hunter can <i>totally</i> protect an innocent psychic from a mundane killer. And they should. But at higher integrity this violates the lie they've told themselves to stay sane. That there's <i>us </i>and <i>them. </i>The code isn't a &quot;Universal Morality&quot;. If anything it's the opposite. A shield that lets hunters do what needs to be done, that their actual morality threatens to slowly weather away. </div> </div> </div>Fine, don't call it &quot;universal morality&quot; if you wish. But it's <i>still</i> problematic because there is still this basic idea all Hunters think the same and follow that same &quot;lie they've told themselves&quot; as you said, even though as mentioned several times before, it makes no sense they would <i>all</i> reason like this, given their diversity when it comes to motivations and methods. The Lucifuge know from day one that monsters are people too, because they see <i>themselves</i> as part of these monsters; that's a major part of their conspiracy: they are more forgiving toward monsters because their own existence proves them being a monsters doesn't prevent you from being a person with the choice to do good or evil. So unless you intend to have them <i>start out</i> at low Integrity, they would require an entirely different system.<br /> <br /> Moreover, feel free to correct me on this point if I am wrong, but isn't having a low Integrity considered a <i>disadvantage</i> in this game? I will admit I am not sure on that particular point, but it sure as hell is crippling to have a low Humanity in Vampires, a low Clarity in Changeling 2E or an unbalanced Harmony in Werewolf. So I assume having low Integrity comes with huge drawbacks as well. Meaning this Code would encourage you to act like a fanatic who doesn't see monsters as people, since doing otherwise would cause you drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-30-2017, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:41:06-07:00","id":1154102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154094#post1154094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raven, I agree with most of your points, but out of curiosity: why do you include the Long Night here? Aren't they a &quot;MONSTERS ARE ALL DEMONS AND MUST DIE!&quot; Kind of compact? Or did I get their section completely wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, they are semi-nice to Changelings and Mages so long as they renounce all their supernatural powers and become their definition of a &quot;good Christian&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:55:36-07:00","id":1154107,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the scaling Social penalties based on the degree to which one hunter's Code differs from another, but I think the penalty should go both ways. I also think the penalties should only come up if the hunters have actually come into conflict over said points. &quot;We need to help as many people as we can&quot; seems like a point two hunters could agree upon, up until the moment that Hunter A realizes that Hunter B considers changelings to be people instead of reserving the term for humans alone.<br /> <br /> As the Code stands now, I see several problems that would be encountered in my games. Namely, one of the major recurring themes in my games is that for all the power possessed by supernatural creatures, the greatest monsters are often human. As written, it seems like a vampire or Beast that preys upon child abusers (so that fulfilling their needs would make the world a better place) would still need to be the enemy of a hunter trying to protect their neighborhood. To keep from risking their Integrity, they'd need to save the abuser. &quot;Yeah, I saved you. You may have raped and murdered my daughter's best friend, but that's a police matter. Nobody, not even you, deserves to die at the fangs of some filthy vampire.&quot; That seems to be the &quot;stable&quot; hunter response. &quot;Yeah, you can have that one, but the second you lay a fang on an innocent I'll see to it that you're kissing sunshine,&quot; on the other hand, is the response of a hunter that's flirting with becoming a slasher. <br /> <br /> Another scenario: Hunter B's best friend escapes from Arcadia, and pours out the whole ordeal over a couple drinks. Hunter B gives a shoulder to cry on, and promises that he's not alone anymore. He even helps his changeling buddy to deal with that pesky Huntsman that just won't leave him alone. Then one day, he comes across another hunter that's beaten his changeling buddy to within an inch of his life. If his buddy manages to turn things around and takes out the guy, Hunter B will suffer a breaking point because a supernatural creature that he refused to harm ended up hurting someone. Perhaps I misunderstood, but it didn't sound like self defense was a valid justification.<br /> <br /> That is really where my main issue comes in. It's &quot;Us vs Them&quot;, where almost universally &quot;Us&quot; means &quot;Humans&quot; and &quot;Them&quot; means &quot;Anything with supernatural powers that don't come from a hunter Endowment.&quot; The most vile and despicable human with dreams of becoming the next Hitler still has more inherent worth than the werewolf that spends her every spare moment volunteering at the soup kitchen or the Sin-Eater that ensures everyone's last words reach their families. A veteran hunter with a &quot;Kill them all, let God sort them out,&quot; mentality can have hundreds of kills under his belt, but as long as he's cautious enough to avoid accidental human collateral damage, he's still less likely to snap and start slashing up everyone than a hunter with a &quot;Every life is sacred, even the monsters, so I better judge each on its own merits&quot; mentality.<br /> <br /> I know those are some extreme examples, but I think that they get my point across. When I've used Hunter, it's often a conflict about when one should act against a monster and when they shouldn't. They need to figure out who the real enemies are, and act accordingly. As written, it seems like &quot;Make sure you have the right weapon, make sure you have no witnesses, make sure it's really dead, make sure you leave no evidence,&quot; is always a safe approach to the Vigil, at least as far as Integrity is concerned. If you want to maintain a high Integrity on the Vigil, be a speciesist bastard and sentence everything touched by the supernatural to death regardless of actions or context. Except for those Lucifuge and Cheiron agents. They're freaks, too, but they're our freaks so they get a pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T06:20:45-07:00","id":1154111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154093#post1154093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it looks like a coping mechanism. Integrity 7+ talks about drawing &quot;a clear line between themselves and the monsters they despise&quot; but we all know that line <i>doesn't really exist.</i><br /> <br /> Monsters have families, jobs, and all that. They're people, just like anyone else. Falling integrity happens in part when hunters <i>realise this</i>. It blurs the line. A low integrity hunter can <i>totally</i> protect an innocent psychic from a mundane killer. And they should. But at higher integrity this violates the lie they've told themselves to stay sane. That there's <i>us </i>and <i>them. </i>The code isn't a &quot;Universal Morality&quot;. If anything it's the opposite. A shield that lets hunters do what needs to be done, that their actual morality threatens to slowly weather away.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Morality: Conformity to the rules of right(/moral/virtuous) conduct. The Code is a Rules of Conduct for Hunter - how should a Hunter behave when confronted with monsters or the supernatural. It currently applies to <i>all</i> Hunters, which makes it Universal.<br /> <br /> Now, judging by modern sensibilities, it is a <i>bad</i> moral system (namely, it is deemed morally inferior), but it is <u>a</u> moral system that universally applies to Hunters.<br /> <br /> A coping mechanism would be Integrity and customizing Breaking Points to remove triggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-30-2017, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T07:53:42-07:00","id":1154120,"title":"","content":"Except it's not. If you see a monster as harmless and let it go <i>nothing happens</i>, as long as you're <i>right.</i><br /> <br /> A low integrity hunter isn't necessarily <i>immoral</i>. Obsessed maybe, Jaded, perhaps. Probably a little insane. But Insanity is not a moral failing, nor is it caused by them. That's the very notion Integrity was created to dispel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T08:17:44-07:00","id":1154123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except it's not. If you see a monster as harmless and let it go <i>nothing happens</i>, as long as you're <i>right.</i> </div> </div> </div>What about the self-defense example with the changeling and hunter example above? Or the vampire/beast hunting serial killer one? In both cases the monster hurt humans. Does THAT trigger Breaking points despite the fact the humans were clearly the one in the wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A low integrity hunter isn't necessarily <i>immoral</i>. Obsessed maybe, Jaded, perhaps. Probably a little insane. But Insanity is not a moral failing, nor is it caused by them. That's the very notion Integrity was created to dispel. </div> </div> </div>Soooooo a hunter who sees monsters as mattering less than humans and sees nothing wrong with not treating them like persons as he takes them down will easily be able to maintain a high Integrity (a trait meant to represent mental health, mind you), while one who carefully checks if the supernaturals he meets actually are evil, treat them like persons rather than judging them on their monstruosity and defend them against humans who clearly are the real monsters will either be &quot;obsessed&quot;, &quot;jaded&quot;, or &quot;a little insane&quot; (and is somehow closer to become a slasher than case number 1). Am I the only one who feels this is a bit backward?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-30-2017, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T08:35:03-07:00","id":1154127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154123#post1154123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the self-defense example with the changeling and hunter example above? Or the vampire/beast hunting serial killer one? In both cases the monster hurt humans. Does THAT trigger Breaking points despite the fact the humans were clearly the one in the wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. Your confidence in the code would be shaken. You get breaking points for things other than breaking the rules of the code, you know. Getting tortured is one too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154123#post1154123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooooo a hunter who sees monsters as mattering less than humans and sees nothing wrong with not treating them like persons as he takes them down will easily be able to maintain a high Integrity (a trait meant to represent mental health, mind you), while one who carefully checks if the supernaturals he meets actually are evil, treat them like persons rather than judging them on their monstruosity and defend them against humans who clearly are the real monsters will either be &quot;obsessed&quot;, &quot;jaded&quot;, or &quot;a little insane&quot; (and is somehow closer to become a slasher than case number 1). Am I the only one who feels this is a bit backward?</div> </div> </div> </div>A hunter stares into the abyss. For them, high integrity is about compartmentalising. Separating the hunt form their everyday life. If you go empathising with the monsters then <i>of course</i> that's gonna make the two sides blur together. <br /> <br /> I mean look at how you phrased it. High integrity is just &quot;Bam, done, what's for lunch?&quot; whereas the other guy meticulously goes around background checking, probably staking them out or poking their nose in weird cults. Who's putting in more effort there? Whose sanity is more likely to crack? <br /> <br /> It looks backward form a distance, but get up close, think about what it involves and suddenly it <i>makes sense</i>. Just like with non-hunters, high integrity is born of looking at the shadows and <i>not thinking too hard about it. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T08:51:01-07:00","id":1154130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, yeah. Your confidence in the code would be shaken. You get breaking points for things other than breaking the rules of the code, you know. Getting tortured is one too. </div> </div> </div>Which brings us back to the fact not all hunters should even believe in that Code in the first place. I bring you back to my Lucifuge example above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A hunter stares into the abyss. For them, high integrity is about compartmentalising. Separating the hunt form their everyday life. If you go empathising with the monsters then <i>of course</i> that's gonna make the two sides blur together.<br /> <br /> I mean look at how you phrased it. High integrity is just &quot;Bam, done, what's for lunch?&quot; whereas the other guy meticulously goes around background checking, probably staking them out or poking their nose in weird cults. Who's putting in more effort there? Whose sanity is more likely to crack?<br /> <br /> It looks backward form a distance, but get up close, think about what it involves and suddenly it <i>makes sense</i>. Just like with non-hunters, high integrity is born of looking at the shadows and <i>not thinking too hard about it. </i> </div> </div> </div>I do see your point, and yeah, I did think about that. Except no. You are right that it'd make sense... from a certain point of view only. True, the second DOES risks his sanity... but that's from exposure to the supernatural and trying to understand things he can't, not directly because he tried to be nuanced. It's the consequences that cause this (which is already covered by other breaking points), NOT the act itself.<br /> <br /> Moreover, based on what I read is slashers, many hunters become slashers because they become too kill-happy and lose their ability to discern the guilties from the innocents. So.... yeah, by that logic, makes no sense that the high Integrity hunter mentioned above would be less likely to turn into a slasher than the more careful one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T10:28:33-07:00","id":1154160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154127#post1154127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah. Your confidence in the code would be shaken. You get breaking points for things other than breaking the rules of the code, you know. Getting tortured is one too. <br /> <br /> <br /> A hunter stares into the abyss. For them, high integrity is about compartmentalising. Separating the hunt form their everyday life. If you go empathising with the monsters then <i>of course</i> that's gonna make the two sides blur together. <br /> <br /> I mean look at how you phrased it. High integrity is just &amp;quot;Bam, done, what's for lunch?&amp;quot; whereas the other guy meticulously goes around background checking, probably staking them out or poking their nose in weird cults. Who's putting in more effort there? Whose sanity is more likely to crack? <br /> <br /> It looks backward form a distance, but get up close, think about what it involves and suddenly it <i>makes sense</i>. Just like with non-hunters, high integrity is born of looking at the shadows and <i>not thinking too hard about it. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except for the fact that Mr. Kill'em All may spend just as much time poking around the shadows as Ms. Compassion does, just with different motivations. However, as long Mr. K manages to avoid harming normal humans in the process, he can be as brutal and merciless as he likes without risking the Merciless Condition or eventual slasherhood. Ms. Compassion, on the other hand, will likely become Merciless if she continually attempts to use mercy.<br /> <br /> Mr. K: &quot;Yeah, it turns out that guy was limiting his molestation to the kids at this one school, right? Real asshole, and I figured that he was probably some kind of monster, maybe one of those damn nightmare critters. Good thing I did my homework, because it turned out that the little school was actually a front for a group of Cheiron group escapees. They were hiding their mutant children there in the hopes that they could pretend to have a normal life. This asshole turns out to just be human, and he only likes the freak kids, so way I figured it, I take out all those little monster children, he's no longer got anyone to prey on. Two birds, one stone. So, I slaughtered all 30 of the kids. If that guy turns his attention to normal kids, I'll call the cops, but since he wasn't targeting humans, I figure no harm done.&quot; Still maintains high Integrity and runs little risk of becoming slasher.<br /> <br /> Ms. Compassion: &quot;My best friend came back from the dead. She had a ghost riding with her behind her eyes, but it was still her. It was weird at first, but she's been a real help to me. She spoke to the ghosts and led us to the people that needed to be punished. I always dreamed of making the world a better place. I tried to see everyone as people. I tried to use mercy when possible. I was a fool. You can't help everyone. How many rapists and murderers ended up being thrown into prison just because some fucking Casper held a grudge? How many others were injured when they attacked my friend? How many hunters did we end up hurting together, just because I was trying to protect her from their attacks? I tried to avoid violence. That was a problem, and I failed. I tried to see everyone as a person, and largely succeeded. But that's the problem. Good and evil... That's a war that can't be won. You can't just focus on the bad guys. Mercy doesn't work. If you want to make the world a better place, you need to get rid of the people. All of them. Mr. K had the right idea, but his old prejudices get in the way. He seems pretty happy, dividing the world into monsters and humans, just like I did with good and evil once upon a time. He doesn't see the big picture. You can't divide the world, not by race, not by actions. You have to treat everyone equally. If you can't spare everyone, then everyone must die.&quot; The likely fate of anyone who tries to take a more merciful approach to the Vigil. Especially if you're a member of the Lucifuge or Cheiron Group and already traded out your one tenet for something besides the supernatural power source one.<br /> <br /> Once again, I use extreme examples, but it strikes me as odd that a vigilante hunter that allies with a vigilante vampire is going to have constant issues with his buddy's superpowers, but one that allies with a vigilante member of a Conspiracy like the Lucifuge would be cool with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T10:29:16-07:00","id":1154161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code#post1154066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monica asked that all discussion on The Code be moved to a different thread, so I thought someone should create one. With that in mind here's what I'd like to see changed about the Code from the playtest draft.<br /> 2) don't make &quot;monsters don't deserve to exist&quot; the default. There's definitely room for that, but looking at the corebook alone I don't think: the Long Night, Network Zero, Null Mysteries, the Loyalists of Thule, the Ascending Ones, or the Lucifuge will agree with that view. And the MM would make an exception for angels and god. That's over half the groups. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure MM wouldn't counter God and Angels as &quot;monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying that they have to be psychologically healthy. Someone who willingly let's spirits possess them is, at least by modern western standards, questionable at best. What I am saying is that breaking points are the wrong mechanic to represent the drawbacks of any kind of questionable behaviour that's encouraged by your Compact or Conspiracy. A Breaking Point should represent a significant moment in your charachter's charachter development. For business as normal, something like Tells or Vampires Banes would work better. </div> </div> </div>I haven't really seen them used like that, I think you are giving too much weight to Breaking Points. Especially for mortals-seeing a supernatural power is a breaking point. Getting hit by a super natural power is a breaking point. Killing someone is a breaking point. A Mortal Investigator would be getting at least three breaking points from a fight with any kind of supernatural creature without any sort of character development, possibly more if he sees the state its victims are in. A Hunter under the 2E code would be getting less breaking points for the same actions, even if he is in a compact/conspiracy that clashes with the Code.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially if you're a member of the Lucifuge or Cheiron Group and already traded out your one tenet for something besides the supernatural power source one. </div> </div> </div>You get a breaking point every time you receive a new Endowment. You can have up to five endowments, likely spaced out over a lot of time. From a mechanics standpoint it would be a waste for them to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 10-30-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T11:26:00-07:00","id":1154167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am pretty sure MM wouldn't counter God and Angels as &quot;monsters&quot;. </div> </div> </div>If you use Dread Powers to represent them, then yes they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You get a breaking point every time you receive a new Endowment. You can have up to five endowments, likely spaced out over a lot of time. From a mechanics standpoint it would be a waste for them to do that. </div> </div> </div>Unless the mechanics changed in 2e, both can remove their powers to replace them by new ones, and I am pretty sure the Cheiron Group don't have the 5 max limit. So yeah, they will end up doing it far more often than that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, i guess I'll have to give an example of my own.<br /> <br /> I am currently running a Hunter Chronicle. In the last session, my players had a brief encounter and semi-truce with a vampire hermit. Said vampire had never killed or harmed anyone, lived alone away from civilization, and ended up putting himself to sleep by staking himself just to make sure he wouldn't cause problem, only asking from them they let him rest in peace. Now, the Cell in general decided to honor this, and just let him be in this Torpor state in the middle of nowhere. But two of the players, respectively a Lucifuge and a Cheiron Group agent, both decided to act behind their comrads back: the Cheiron Group agent contacted his superiors and gave them the location of the vampire's resting place, so they could grab him and dissect him in their lab as they always do. Meanwhile, the Lucifuge (who had suspicions about what the Cheiron Group agent was doing) contacted his own allies and also gave them the location, so they could move him to a new, safer place.<br /> <br /> Now, at the time, I used the Mortal Remains rules. But let's examine how it would have turned out if I had used the Code as defined in this playtest, shall we?<br /> <br /> Both players acted in the back of their Cell, plus against each other. I am pretty sure that qualifies as &quot;betraying a fellow hunter&quot;: Breaking point triggered with a -2 penalty. So far, nothing wrong.<br /> <br /> But the Cheiron group agent acted at the vampire's detriment and to the benefit of his organization, so he gets no further modifier and stick to the -2<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Lucifuge acted against humans (the Cheiron Group) to the benefit of a monster (the vampire); he gets the -3 modifier, leaving him with a -5 penalty.<br /> <br /> Soooo, the Cheiron group agent, who is willingly trying to doom someone to a horrible fate with no further self-justification than the fact he is doing his job, get a lesser penalty than the Lucifuge, who is just trying to spare a horrible fate to a &quot;monster&quot; who represents no risk whatsoever to anyone at the moment, and is doing it with the firm conviction this is the right thing to do. I think that's kind of a problem here.<br /> <br /> And guess what? The Lucifuge can't even fix that by changing one of the Tenets, because &quot;actively helping a supernatural&quot; is a <i>modifier</i>, not a Tenet. He is stuck with a penalty that made no sense because it's based on an aspect of the Code he has no reason to believe in considering his origin, and which he can't even remove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-30-2017, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:18:21-07:00","id":1154178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154167#post1154167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you use Dread Powers to represent them, then yes they do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Unless the mechanics changed in 2e, both can remove their powers to replace them by new ones, and I am pretty sure the Cheiron Group don't have the 5 max limit. So yeah, they will end up doing it far more often than that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, i guess I'll have to give an example of my own.<br /> <br /> I am currently running a Hunter Chronicle. In the last session, my players had a brief encounter and semi-truce with a vampire hermit. Said vampire had never killed or harmed anyone, lived alone away from civilization, and ended up putting himself to sleep by staking himself just to make sure he wouldn't cause problem, only asking from them they let him rest in peace. Now, the Cell in general decided to honor this, and just let him be in this Torpor state in the middle of nowhere. But two of the players, respectively a Lucifuge and a Cheiron Group agent, both decided to act behind their comrads back: the Cheiron Group agent contacted his superiors and gave them the location of the vampire's resting place, so they could grab him and dissect him in their lab as they always do. Meanwhile, the Lucifuge (who had suspicions about what the Cheiron Group agent was doing) contacted his own allies and also gave them the location, so they could move him to a new, safer place.<br /> <br /> Now, at the time, I used the Mortal Remains rules. But let's examine how it would have turned out if I had used the Code as defined in this playtest, shall we?<br /> <br /> Both players acted in the back of their Cell, plus against each other. I am pretty sure that qualifies as &quot;betraying a fellow hunter&quot;: Breaking point triggered with a -2 penalty. So far, nothing wrong.<br /> <br /> But the Cheiron group agent acted at the vampire's detriment and to the benefit of his organization, so he gets no further modifier and stick to the -2<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Lucifuge acted against humans (the Cheiron Group) to the benefit of a monster (the vampire); he gets the -3 modifier, leaving him with a -5 penalty.<br /> <br /> Soooo, the Cheiron group agent, who is willingly trying to doom someone to a horrible fate with no further self-justification than the fact he is doing his job, get a lesser penalty than the Lucifuge, who is just trying to spare a horrible fate to a &quot;monster&quot; who represents no risk whatsoever to anyone at the moment, and is doing it with the firm conviction this is the right thing to do. I think that's kind of a problem here.<br /> <br /> And guess what? The Lucifuge can't even fix that by changing one of the Tenets, because &quot;actively helping a supernatural&quot; is a <i>modifier</i>, not a Tenet. He is stuck with a penalty that made no sense because it's based on an aspect of the Code he has no reason to believe in considering his origin, and which he can't even remove.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow, I feel that the scenario &quot;The Christian God is real, shows up in person for the story, and is represented only by Dread Powers&quot; is an incredibly rare one. Certainly not a canon one, unless the writers are feeling particularly brave.<br /> <br /> The new list says you can have as many Endowments as you have dots in status. Whether you can switch them out like you could in 1E is well beyond the playtest, though at worst it still isn't something you are going to do more often than other breaking points barring a strange playstyle. There is a note that some groups can have more than the five, but you are still looking at one breaking point every four EXP at worst.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:19:23-07:00","id":1154179,"title":"","content":"Those are <i>suggested</i> modifiers. You don't have to apply them if you don't want to.<br /> <br /> But besides that, all the examples given only reinforce what I and the text says: that the code is a facade, and that high integrity is built on a foundation of cognitive dissonance. Yes, the lucifurge might get a bigger penalty to the roll for doing the right thing. Here's the rub: <i>that's the whole point.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The hunter tells herself she\u2019s different, that she\u2019s doing it all for the greater good. If she can cling to her Integrity, she might even be right. The more she violates this Code, the hollower her insistence rings. She builds a wall of scars around her heart so she can live with herself. Do the job, slay the fiend, save the day. But the more Integrity she loses, the less she knows herself anymore. The further she falls, the harder it is to see the difference between herself and any other killer. </div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:29:14-07:00","id":1154183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those are <i>suggested</i> modifiers. You don't have to apply them if you don't want to. </div> </div> </div>Precising this would have been nice; I just checked the playtest, and I read &quot;Breaking Point Modifiers&quot;, not &quot;Suggested Modifier&quot;. And don't tell me that goes without saying, because other books <i>do</i> bother precising it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But besides that, all the examples given only reinforce what I and the text says: that the code is a facade, and that high integrity is built on a foundation of cognitive dissonance. Yes, the lucifurge might get a bigger penalty to the roll for doing the right thing. Here's the rub: <i>that's the whole point.</i> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if Hunters <i>actually follow that damn Code</i>. In order for the infraction of the Code to bother them, they have to actually follow it in the first place, to make the concious decision of seeing it as their code of life, even if deep down they know it's all rubbish. A Muslim won't feel bad or feel torn about eating meat on Friday, because that's part of the Catholic belief (well, some Catholics, at least), and he doesn't believe himself that's important. And the Lucifuge have no reason of feeling bad about screwing the Code because their description makes it pretty clear they <i>don't believe in it</i> <i>in the first place</i>.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I am wrong, but the way I get it, Breaking Points are supposed to represent a character's sanity withering due to being conflicted about his convictions and the way he understands things around him, the fact he goes against what he believes. It probably represents more than that, but that's the part the Code is supposed to represent. The Lucifuge in my example above was acting <i>completely</i><i> in accord with his own conviction</i>s; he wasn't just doing the right thing, he was <i>convinced</i> that was the right thing with no doubt about it. And as such he shouldn't get screwed up by the Code.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\">But the more Integrity she loses, the less she knows herself anymore. The further she falls, the harder it is to see the difference between herself and any other killer. </span> </div> </div> </div>You're telling me my Lucifuge player saving someone from being dissected by scientists <i>make it harder for him to make the difference between himself and some random killer?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-30-2017, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T13:17:00-07:00","id":1154198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154183#post1154183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precising this would have been nice; I just checked the playtest, and I read &quot;Breaking Point Modifiers&quot;, not &quot;Suggested Modifier&quot;. And don't tell me that goes without saying, because other books <i>do</i> bother precising it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, if Hunters <i>actually follow that damn Code</i>. In order for the infraction of the Code to bother them, they have to actually follow it in the first place, to make the concious decision of seeing it as their code of life, even if deep down they know it's all rubbish. A Muslim won't feel bad or feel torn about eating meat on Friday, because that's part of the Catholic belief (well, some Catholics, at least), and he doesn't believe himself that's important. And the Lucifuge have no reason of feeling bad about screwing the Code because their description makes it pretty clear they <i>don't believe in it</i> <i>in the first place</i>.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I am wrong, but the way I get it, Breaking Points are supposed to represent a character's sanity withering due to being conflicted about his convictions and the way he understands things around him, the fact he goes against what he believes. It probably represents more than that, but that's the part the Code is supposed to represent. The Lucifuge in my example above was acting <i>completely</i><i> in accord with his own conviction</i>s; he wasn't just doing the right thing, he was <i>convinced</i> that was the right thing with no doubt about it. And as such he shouldn't get screwed up by the Code.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're telling me my Lucifuge player saving someone from being dissected by scientists <i>make it harder for him to make the difference between himself and some random killer?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well it does say <b>&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Other modifiers may apply to the roll as well, at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion&quot;</span></span></b> (the modifier referred to was based on the level of the 'sin')<br /> <br /> As it says in the Core, &quot;Note that a breaking point is not necessarily something that the character considers wrong&quot;. In that situation, the Lucifuge member is putting the well being of something that isn't &quot;really&quot; alive (both in the sense that it is a vampire, and that it is in an apparently permanent self inflicted coma) over that of what is supposed to be an ally. By doing this, he is saying that the monster's life is worth at least as much as a humans, meaning that being a &quot;Monster Hunter&quot; is just being a vigilante who picks hard targets. Meanwhile, while the Cheiron operative is saying &quot;this walking corpse is just a walking corpse&quot;. If he had agreed with you, that means he was sending &quot;human beings&quot; to be horribly experimented on every time he sent a major splat monster back to the labs. Even if they had it coming, that realization wouldn't be good for your mental health. &quot;They are just monsters. I send them back to the lab, they get cut up for life saving medicine and weapons, there is one less monster in the world, and I get a fat paycheck. Good deal.&quot; Both come with the realization &quot;I can't really trust my allies when it counts&quot;, which is were the penalty comes from.<br /> <br /> In addition, you could give your Lucifuge +2 for &quot;Acting in the defense of another person&quot;, with another +2 if he has a Touchstone attached (which he does by default). If his Virtue is involved, or if he has interacted with someone he trusted recently he gets more bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T13:44:48-07:00","id":1154209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well it does say <b>&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Other modifiers may apply to the roll as well, at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion&quot;</span></span></b> (the modifier referred to was based on the level of the 'sin') </div> </div> </div>I didn't see that part. My bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it says in the Core, &quot;Note that a breaking point is not necessarily something that the character considers wrong&quot;. In that situation, the Lucifuge member is putting the well being of something that isn't &quot;really&quot; alive (both in the sense that it is a vampire, and that it is in an apparently permanent self inflicted coma) over that of what is supposed to be an ally. By doing this, he is saying that the monster's life is worth at least as much as a humans, meaning that being a &quot;Monster Hunter&quot; is just being a vigilante who picks hard targets. Meanwhile, while the Cheiron operative is saying &quot;this walking corpse is just a walking corpse&quot;. If he had agreed with you, that means he was sending &quot;human beings&quot; to be horribly experimented on every time he sent a major splat monster back to the labs. Even if they had it coming, that realization wouldn't be good for your mental health. &quot;They are just monsters. I send them back to the lab, they get cut up for life saving medicine and weapons, there is one less monster in the world, and I get a fat paycheck. Good deal.&quot; Both come with the realization &quot;I can't really trust my allies when it counts&quot;, which is were the penalty comes from. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the -2 Penalty, which I explicitly said wasn't a problem. Not the -3 one, which had no place here. Also, no, the Lucifuge <i>isn't </i>&quot;putting the well being of something that isn't &quot;really&quot; alive over that of what is supposed to be an ally&quot;. Nobody was being put in danger by moving that vampire; he was in Torpor, meaning he wouldn't harm anyone, and placed in an area where nobody could free him. <i>Nobody</i> mortal was put in danger by his action. I get that you're suggesting this makes him realize the Cheiron Group can't be trusted, but I would expect that to make him more distrustful toward them, not to question <i>himself</i> and get his sanity shaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, you could give your Lucifuge +2 for &quot;Acting in the defense of another person&quot;, with another +2 if he has a Touchstone attached (which he does by default). If his Virtue is involved, or if he has interacted with someone he trusted recently he gets more bonuses. </div> </div> </div>Except the rules are pretty clear that in game system, a monster doesn't count as a &quot;person&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T14:13:45-07:00","id":1154218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154209#post1154209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't see that part. My bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, the -2 Penalty, which I explicitly said wasn't a problem. Not the -3 one, which had no place here. Also, no, the Lucifuge <i>isn't </i>&quot;putting the well being of something that isn't &quot;really&quot; alive over that of what is supposed to be an ally&quot;. Nobody was being put in danger by moving that vampire; he was in Torpor, meaning he wouldn't harm anyone, and placed in an area where nobody could free him. <i>Nobody</i> mortal was put in danger by his action. I get that you're suggesting this makes him realize the Cheiron Group can't be trusted, but I would expect that to make him more distrustful toward them, not to question <i>himself</i> and get his sanity shaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except the rules are pretty clear that in game system, a monster doesn't count as a &quot;person&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, for some reason I was under the impression that they fought over it. The core issue is believing &quot;This monster has a right to live&quot; goes to &quot;All monsters have a right to live&quot; goes to &quot;Monsters are basically just people with powers&quot;. This in turn goes to &quot;I kill/hurt people. I'm just a vigilante with an odd choice in targets&quot;. It still putting the well being of the Monster over that of humans to a lesser extent (as before, Cheiron isn't cutting it up for fun. They do make medicine out of the creature, which could save human lives, and make their organization stronger). The Cheiron example was there just for comparison, what the &quot;violent&quot; hunter does vs what the &quot;merciful&quot; hunter does.<br /> <br /> The idea is that it shakes his worldview. &quot;I can't trust Cheiron&quot; isn't the lesson, its &quot;I can't trust other hunters&quot;, a group Cheiron happens to be a part of. And if I can't trust other hunters, I can't trust anybody. It makes your character a little more paranoid, a little more jaded, a little more like the middling/low integrity hunters if he fails his test.<br /> <br /> As above, the breaking point modifiers are suggestions. If you are running the game and you think he should get a +2 or a +1 for acting to save the vampire, you can give it to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T14:21:12-07:00","id":1154221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, for some reason I was under the impression that they fought over it. </div> </div> </div>No, at least not directly. They just acted behind each other's backs, with no direct confrontation. The mistake is understandable, though^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T15:34:00-07:00","id":1154237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154183#post1154183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I am wrong, but the way I get it, Breaking Points are supposed to represent a character's sanity withering due to being conflicted about his convictions and the way he understands things around him, the fact he goes against what he believes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are wrong. Breaking Points are not the when the character's sanity withers, losing a dot of Integrity is. Which can happen when you FAIL a breaking point but doesn't when you succeed. The point being that Breaking Points should occur when the character questions their world view (which for a hunter is going to be a bit different from a non-Hunter), if they pass then they have successfully coped with their world.<br /> <br /> So yeah, being a member of the Lucifuge and having to deal with the idea of defining a monster and what is good and bad and where you fall on the spectrum should cause a lot of Breaking Points cause it is a really hard life. The character shouldn't be able to just go 'welp, I'm descended from a demon prince and have powers that defy understanding and go around making decisions about good and bad/ monster and not; all while being a person/or not without having to face any difficult sense of self challenges about it. Life is good'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T17:09:52-07:00","id":1154254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154237#post1154237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are wrong. Breaking Points are not the when the character's sanity withers, losing a dot of Integrity is. Which can happen when you FAIL a breaking point but doesn't when you succeed. The point being that Breaking Points should occur when the character questions their world view (which for a hunter is going to be a bit different from a non-Hunter), if they pass then they have successfully coped with their world.<br /> <br /> So yeah, being a member of the Lucifuge and having to deal with the idea of defining a monster and what is good and bad and where you fall on the spectrum should cause a lot of Breaking Points cause it is a really hard life. The character shouldn't be able to just go 'welp, I'm descended from a demon prince and have powers that defy understanding and go around making decisions about good and bad/ monster and not; all while being a person/or not without having to face any difficult sense of self challenges about it. Life is good'</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that the compassionate hunter should have it easy. If Ms. Compassion saves a monster because it looks like a child and she finds it the next morning feasting upon the intestines of her friend, that should totally be a Breaking Point, regardless of her original good intentions. I just don't see why treating each monster on an individual basis should run a greater risk to the sanity of a hunter than slaughtering every one of them indiscriminately. If Mr. K in my earlier example is hunting down every hiding deviant child at the school so that he can shoot them in the face as they cry and plead for their lives, why should his sanity be more secure than that of a compassionate hunter witnessing their monster buddy hurting a human in self defense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T17:10:00-07:00","id":1154255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are wrong. Breaking Points are not the when the character's sanity withers, losing a dot of Integrity is. Which can happen when you FAIL a breaking point but doesn't when you succeed. The point being that Breaking Points should occur when the character questions their world view (which for a hunter is going to be a bit different from a non-Hunter), if they pass then they have successfully coped with their world. </div> </div> </div>Now you are just playing with semantics. <i>Yes</i>, the Sanity withers only and only when the Breaking Point fail. But that doesn't change anything to the fact going through a Breaking Point suggest you need to be in a situation where your sanity is put at risk of withering. And the current system looks like it'll trigger them even in situations where your character has no reason to question what he is doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah, being a member of the Lucifuge and having to deal with the idea of defining a monster and what is good and bad and where you fall on the spectrum should cause a lot of Breaking Points cause it is a really hard life. The character shouldn't be able to just go 'welp, I'm descended from a demon prince and have powers that defy understanding and go around making decisions about good and bad/ monster and not; all while being a person/or not without having to face any difficult sense of self challenges about it. Life is good' </div> </div> </div>No, but there is such a thing as middle ground. If making a distinction between good and bad monsters is something they do on regular basis, then by all logic that should have less impact on their point of view of the world; they cannot question their point of view on the world each time they meet a supernatural who isn't evil and decide to help it if they don't expect supernatural beings to be all evil in the first place. Taking time to observe monsters, capture them/approach them and talk with them, with clear plans of what to do regardless of if they are good or evil doesn't sound like you'd need to question your point of view. Breaking points should be for situations that get out of your comfort zone, like morally grey monsters or monsters who pretend to be good only to turn out worse later. Or having to pick a lesser evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-30-2017, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T17:35:24-07:00","id":1154263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154255#post1154255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you are just playing with semantics. <i>Yes</i>, the Sanity withers only and only when the Breaking Point fail. But that doesn't change anything to the fact going through a Breaking Point suggest you need to be in a situation where your sanity is put at risk of withering. And the current system looks like it'll trigger them even in situations where your character has no reason to question what he is doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, but there is such a thing as middle ground. If making a distinction between good and bad monsters is something they do on regular basis, then by all logic that should have less impact on their point of view of the world; they cannot question their point of view on the world each time they meet a supernatural who isn't evil and decide to help it if they don't expect supernatural beings to be all evil in the first place. Taking time to observe monsters, capture them/approach them and talk with them, with clear plans of what to do regardless of if they are good or evil doesn't sound like you'd need to question your point of view. Breaking points should be for situations that get out of your comfort zone, like morally grey monsters or monsters who pretend to be good only to turn out worse later. Or having to pick a lesser evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> too.<br /> <br /> I was only responding to the specific statement not the general point.<br /> <br /> It is not just semantics though, saying that Breaking points means something other than what it does has a lot of impact. It presents as if every Breaking Point was automatically a loss of Integrity, which it isn't. That's like saying that a Vampire feeding always kills a person rather than that sometimes when a Vampire feeds they kill the person. One will be more common than the other, and they should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154255#post1154255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If making a distinction between good and bad monsters is something they do on regular basis, then by all logic that should have less impact on their point of view of the world;</div> </div> </div> </div>On this point specifically, not really. If something is traumatic than doing it a bunch doesn't make it less traumatic, either they are good at coping with the trauma in the first place (they pass the tests) or it affects them (they lose Integrity).<br /> <br /> Still not saying that that specific example should be a Breaking Point or not. I think it is too general to say. If it's just making the determiniation in a vacuum then probably not, if it is constantly deciding whether you should kill a sentient being because they might be 'harming' others and trying to decide if it's just 'in their nature' or a choice, and what the 'correct' choice then is for either option then yeah, that's gonna wear on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 10-30-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T18:26:09-07:00","id":1154268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is not just semantics though, saying that Breaking points means something other than what it does has a lot of impact. It presents as if every Breaking Point was automatically a loss of Integrity, which it isn't. That's like saying that a Vampire feeding always kills a person rather than that sometimes when a Vampire feeds they kill the person. One will be more common than the other, and they should be. </div> </div> </div>Unless he suffers frenzy, a vampire can ensure he won't kill his victim by being careful to feed in small doses and not make a roll to be sure. Difficult, yes, but possible; that's how they make Herds. With a Breaking Point, there ALWAYS is a risk you'll lose Integrity. That's kind of a big difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On this point specifically, not really. If something is traumatic than doing it a bunch doesn't make it less traumatic, either they are good at coping with the trauma in the first place (they pass the tests) or it affects them (they lose Integrity). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, about that. Finding out someone died because you spared a werewolf is traumatic. Having your spouse turned into a vampire is traumatic. Finding out the changeling you have caught and torured all night was innocent is traumatic. Calmly studying a supernatural's past through observation and deciding without much dilemna that he deserves to live because he did nothing wrong is NOT a traumatic experience. At least not in itself; sure, you can suffer Breaking Point by finding out about all the messed up stuff he did, or getting too involved in his cult. But the act itself is rational and not something that should have the potential to induce a trauma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still not saying that that specific example should be a Breaking Point or not. I think it is too general to say. If it's just making the determiniation in a vacuum then probably not, if it is constantly deciding whether you should kill a sentient being because they might be 'harming' others and trying to decide if it's just 'in their nature' or a choice, and what the 'correct' choice then is for either option then yeah, that's gonna wear on you. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's kinda our point; it's too vague and can cover situations where it doesn't fit. There needs to be a better distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T19:53:36-07:00","id":1154280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154268#post1154268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless he suffers frenzy, a vampire can ensure he won't kill his victim by being careful to feed in small doses and not make a roll to be sure. Difficult, yes, but possible; that's how they make Herds. With a Breaking Point, there ALWAYS is a risk you'll lose Integrity. That's kind of a big difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, about that. Finding out someone died because you spared a werewolf is traumatic. Having your spouse turned into a vampire is traumatic. Finding out the changeling you have caught and torured all night was innocent is traumatic. Calmly studying a supernatural's past through observation and deciding without much dilemna that he deserves to live because he did nothing wrong is NOT a traumatic experience. At least not in itself; sure, you can suffer Breaking Point by finding out about all the messed up stuff he did, or getting too involved in his cult. But the act itself is rational and not something that should have the potential to induce a trauma.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, that's kinda our point; it's too vague and can cover situations where it doesn't fit. There needs to be a better distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Investigating monsters doesn't inflict any penalty or breaking point. Unless you let them go free and they kill someone, or you kill them after finishing your investigation.<br /> <br /> The real problem with Integrity loss is that while each breaking point gets you a beat, it takes 15 beats to get that integrity back (by core.) So if you have 10 dice average on your breaking point roll, you have an average of 0.7^10*100%=2.82% chance of failing each roll, with a (1-(0.7)^10)^15*100=65% chance of passing them all with a net outcome of success. Someone check my math, its getting late. At 7 dice average, that is only a ~28% chance of passing them all meaning you will most certainly lose &quot;Experience Value&quot; (considering each point of Integrity to be worth 5 Experiences) by taking breaking points. This means that, while Breaking points may look like they make your character stronger, you would lose &quot;Experience&quot; overall unless you are rolling lots of dice every time. <s>At 9, the odds slightly favor success, meaning that you would probably gain Experience in the long run purely from breaking points.</s><br /> <br /> Of course that is a super meta munchkiny way of looking at things, and the story changes if you don't consider Integrity having inherent value. If that experience is spent elsewhere instead and you take the Integrity hits, then it all becomes murkier than I can work out right now.<br /> <br /> Edit: Woops, forgot to take in the possibility of multiple failures in that math. At 9 you have a ~54% chance of succeeding them all, but you don't have a ~46% of losing once. The possibility of multiple failures means that it still probably isn't even yet. I told you it was late &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Edit2: Grumble Grumble. So to pull out some real math, it should be a ...(15!/(13!2!)(1-0.7^9)^13*(0.7^9)^2*100=10% chance of getting two failures, 1.82% of getting 3 for d9. And a 34% for one failure. So quick and dirty estimating, you will still have a net loss at 9 dice. Its *10* dice that you would start to gain at. 28.36% failure, 5.77% two failure, 0.7% three failures, 65% all successes. But please take that with a grain of salt at this point :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 10-31-2017, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T02:31:44-07:00","id":1154316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154127#post1154127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A hunter stares into the abyss. For them, high integrity is about compartmentalising. Separating the hunt form their everyday life. If you go empathising with the monsters then <i>of course</i> that's gonna make the two sides blur together. <br /> <br /> I mean look at how you phrased it. High integrity is just &quot;Bam, done, what's for lunch?&quot; whereas the other guy meticulously goes around background checking, probably staking them out or poking their nose in weird cults. Who's putting in more effort there? Whose sanity is more likely to crack? <br /> <br /> It looks backward form a distance, but get up close, think about what it involves and suddenly it <i>makes sense</i>. Just like with non-hunters, high integrity is born of looking at the shadows and <i>not thinking too hard about it. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>There is definitely a point to be made that a simpler us/them worldview would be more resilient to cracking, but I present the following counterpoints.<br /> <br /> 1) Hunters are not mechanically optimised vigil machines. They are the product of a society and upbringing that says Nazi-ish dehumaniseing ideals are evil. Many Hunters, arguably more than half of the core 12, would choose a code that judges monsters on their actions over one that thinks all monsters do not deserve to exist even if the other led to higher Integrity.<br /> <br /> 2) While a binary us/them may be better at keeping your integrity up I think it would be worse at keeping your two lives separate than a code closer to social norms. imagine a Hunter going to a dinner party and his friends daughter emerges from her room wearing lots of black and silver pentacle jewellery. A hunter who believes all witches are subhuman and deserve to die (even if he only suspects she might be a witch) is more likely to creep people out by the way he acts than one who thinks witches are human and only deserve to be hunted for criminal actions.<br /> <br /> 3) What's the Hunter's goal? Unless they genuinely believe the extermination of anything supernatural is a goal onto itself allying with the right monster can be an enormous asset. If your goal is to keep your community safe you want the witch who doesn't threaten anyone on your side. A Code that says she's not human is going to make it much harder if not impossible to win her trust. <br /> <br /> 4) Thematics. Saying that the default position for an oppressed group organising to fight back is for them to go full Nazi is a thematically weird message.<br /> <br /> For these reasons I think it's best to avoid a default code that deny's monsters even have the right to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-31-2017, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T08:52:52-07:00","id":1154397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154268#post1154268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless he suffers frenzy, a vampire can ensure he won't kill his victim by being careful to feed in small doses and not make a roll to be sure. Difficult, yes, but possible; that's how they make Herds. With a Breaking Point, there ALWAYS is a risk you'll lose Integrity. That's kind of a big difference.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So you can just ignore a possibility when it suits you (frenzy). I could have used a million different examples, the vampire thing was just what popped into my head. The point is that a Breaking Point and losing Integrity are NOT one and the same. And saying they are is disengenious and misleading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154268#post1154268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, about that. Finding out someone died because you spared a werewolf is traumatic. Having your spouse turned into a vampire is traumatic. Finding out the changeling you have caught and torured all night was innocent is traumatic. Calmly studying a supernatural's past through observation and deciding without much dilemna that he deserves to live because he did nothing wrong is NOT a traumatic experience. At least not in itself; sure, you can suffer Breaking Point by finding out about all the messed up stuff he did, or getting too involved in his cult. But the act itself is rational and not something that should have the potential to induce a trauma.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Again as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar18090_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"18090\" data-vbnamecard=\"18090\">Ruger</a> said and you admitted to misreading on the other thread: JUST HELPING A MONSTER IS NOT A BREAKING POINT!<br /> <br /> It is a negative modifier for when you do hit a Breaking Point and the fact that you helped them helped cause the situation.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154268#post1154268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's kinda our point; it's too vague and can cover situations where it doesn't fit. There needs to be a better distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that in the quoted post you are the one with a general example, not the rules. We should go back to your actual game example, since it is an actual specific example and use it. That was better.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, given that, I went back to your example and read it again. I have one question and then some thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> Why did the Lucifuge member not tell the rest of the Cell about his suspicions about the Chieron member?<br /> <br /> I am not sure I would say that the Lucifuge did 'betray a fellow hunter', he didn't know that the Cheiron member called his bosses. So he isnt really betraying him, and even if he did know then he is reacting to a betrayal no betraying in the first place. The cell had decided to leave the vampire alone, taking some of his own resources on the side to help the vampire is not really what I would call a betrayal. Even if it was, I would give a bonus to the Lucifuge since they were acting in the spirit of the cells decision and their own convictions.<br /> <br /> The real question is how are this Cheiorn and Lucifuge even on the same team? They clearly have some huge differences in how they should approach 'hunting'. If they continue this way then there should definetly be some issues. Either they come to blows or one of them (and I think the Lucifuge makes more sense) should start to have issues with their world view and sense of self (y'know, Breaking Points) while they try to reconcile working with this person who thinks that its ok to harvest monster parts no matter what versus how they feel that monsters should be left alone if harmless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 10-31-2017, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T09:48:42-07:00","id":1154416,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a> You can't win. The sole issue with the Code is reader bias. You can't debate someone that reads the preview and sees &quot;humans good, monsters bad&quot; as a simplistic representation of a view, not being dismissive. If someone thinks the Code suggests that monsters have no right to exist then there can be no discussion with someone that like me reads the same thing as &quot;human life is more valuable than monster life&quot;. It isn't a left-right argument, more like up-left as in no relation to each other.<br /> <br /> To others.<br /> <br /> I will skip the game talk and go to a real world type of example to explain how I saw the Code. I will switch out monsters with dogs. I like dogs. I prefer cats but dogs work better for this. I like the average dog more than the average human. If I see a dead dog on the side of the road, I think poor dog. If I saw a human instead, I would want somebody to clean that mess up. However, I accept the universal morality of humanity that says a human life is more valuable than a dog's life. A dog should be killed if it bites a human outside of defending itself or family. Given the choice of saving the life of a human or a dog, I choose human.<br /> <br /> It is instinct. I don't consider the quality of the lives. I assume the human leans towards ass-hat and the dog is likely a good dog. I still choose human. It doesn't matter if the human has a year left to live and the dog could go on for 10 or 15 years. There is no way I would choose a generic dog over a generic human. A known example of one or the other complicates the equation.<br /> <br /> The Code is supposed to be messy when dealing with known baddies. Human may not be good. Monsters may not be bad. However, human life has more value than monster life. That does not mean destroy all monsters. It definitely means when there is a choice between human and monster a hunter should choose human. Some hunter groups blur lines, but the hunters that work for those groups take up the Vigil to benefit humanity, and work to the detriment of monsters (some) in their effort. These far reaching changes to the Code belong as house rules because the problem exists solely within the house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:27:39-07:00","id":1154433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar18090_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"18090\" data-vbnamecard=\"18090\">Ruger</a> said and you admitted to misreading on the other thread: JUST HELPING A MONSTER IS NOT A BREAKING POINT!<br /> <br /> It is a negative modifier for when you do hit a Breaking Point and the fact that you helped them helped cause the situation. </div> </div> </div>That's STILL a problem because as I demonstrated, that modifier can apply in situations where it shouldn't. Unless obviously it's just a suggested Breaking point, which we already discussed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why did the Lucifuge member not tell the rest of the Cell about his suspicions about the Chieron member? </div> </div> </div>Beat me, I am not in my players' head when they take decisions. This is an actual session that happened, not a story I wrote. Maybe he was worried about some of them taking the Cheiron Group agent's side and creating needless conflict (one of the other players <i>was</i> very reluctant about letting the vampire here). Maybe he didn't trust them to not give away the info to him. Or maybe the player just didn't think about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not sure I would say that the Lucifuge did 'betray a fellow hunter', he didn't know that the Cheiron member called his bosses. So he isnt really betraying him, and even if he did know then he is reacting to a betrayal no betraying in the first place. The cell had decided to leave the vampire alone, taking some of his own resources on the side to help the vampire is not really what I would call a betrayal. Even if it was, I would give a bonus to the Lucifuge since they were acting in the spirit of the cells decision and their own convictions. </div> </div> </div>That is an entirely different intepretation of &quot;betraying&quot;. Personally, my interpretation was &quot;acting against another hunter&quot;, or if you want to be generous &quot;acting against a hunter who is your ally&quot;. Admittedly, we are entering in when the breaking point apply or not, which is another debate entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The real question is how are this Cheiorn and Lucifuge even on the same team? They clearly have some huge differences in how they should approach 'hunting'. If they continue this way then there should definetly be some issues. Either they come to blows or one of them (and I think the Lucifuge makes more sense) should start to have issues with their world view and sense of self (y'know, Breaking Points) while they try to reconcile working with this person who thinks that its ok to harvest monster parts no matter what versus how they feel that monsters should be left alone if harmless. </div> </div> </div>The alliance between the two makes sense in the context of my Chronicle's story, but you will forgive me for not digressing by giving needless details about it in a conversation that is about something else entirely; I didn't feel you'd want me to narrate you a summary of multiple sessions just to give an example that was covered in a single one. We are here to discuss the Code, not to judge my skills as a CoD Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Though if I may, are you suggesting making a Chronicle about hunters from different Compacts and Conspiracies forming a Cell together should not be allowed? Because I am pretty sure nothing forbid it in either 1E or 2E, and some books even give examples. The game would be rather limiting if players had to all play the same group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will skip the game talk and go to a real world type of example to explain how I saw the Code. I will switch out monsters with dogs. I like dogs. I prefer cats but dogs work better for this. I like the average dog more than the average human. If I see a dead dog on the side of the road, I think poor dog. If I saw a human instead, I would want somebody to clean that mess up. However, I accept the universal morality of humanity that says a human life is more valuable than a dog's life. A dog should be killed if it bites a human outside of defending itself or family. Given the choice of saving the life of a human or a dog, I choose human.<br /> <br /> It is instinct. I don't consider the quality of the lives. I assume the human leans towards ass-hat and the dog is likely a good dog. I still choose human. It doesn't matter if the human has a year left to live and the dog could go on for 10 or 15 years. There is no way I would choose a generic dog over a generic human. A known example of one or the other complicates the equation. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is. But we would be entering a Nature vs Nurture argument if we tried debating on this, so I'd say, let's avoid too much digression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Code is supposed to be messy when dealing with known baddies. Human may not be good. Monsters may not be bad. However, human life has more value than monster life. That does not mean destroy all monsters. It definitely means when there is a choice between human and monster a hunter should choose human. Some hunter groups blur lines, but the hunters that work for those groups take up the Vigil to benefit humanity, and work to the detriment of monsters (some) in their effort. These far reaching changes to the Code belong as house rules because the problem exists solely within the house. </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean, and to some extend I understand. If I remember correct, some monsters have the same thing; Forsaken Werewolves don't hate humans and won't go on their way to slaughter them like the Pure, but they still value Werewolf life over humans. But... I don't know, I am still reluctant.<br /> <br /> Let's make something clear: I don't like arguing with people like ElvesOfZion. I don't want to &quot;win&quot; this argument. I am just explaining my problem with the Code and defending my point of view. My opinion, as well as Raven's, is that it's too limiting as it is, and doesn't make sense for some of the hunter groups. Maybe instead of dismissing our complain, it could be a good idea to think about how to make it more nuanced, or figure out what could be improved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-31-2017, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T12:43:46-07:00","id":1154474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154433#post1154433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beat me, I am not in my players' head when they take decisions. This is an actual session that happened, not a story I wrote. Maybe he was worried about some of them taking the Cheiron Group agent's side and creating needless conflict (one of the other players <i>was</i> very reluctant about letting the vampire here). Maybe he didn't trust them to not give away the info to him. Or maybe the player just didn't think about that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect you to read their mind, but it would be helpful for the discussion if you were to ask them. It does have bearing on the discussion to know the setup of the team and the characters personalities and motiviations because that's what determines what Breaking Points should be taken and what modifiers should be applied. Anything else is bad white room theorycrafting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154433#post1154433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alliance between the two makes sense in the context of my Chronicle's story, but you will forgive me for not digressing by giving needless details about it in a conversation that is about something else entirely; I didn't feel you'd want me to narrate you a summary of multiple sessions just to give an example that was covered in a single one. We are here to discuss the Code, not to judge my skills as a CoD Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Though if I may, are you suggesting making a Chronicle about hunters from different Compacts and Conspiracies forming a Cell together should not be allowed? Because I am pretty sure nothing forbid it in either 1E or 2E, and some books even give examples. The game would be rather limiting if players had to all play the same group.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It matters how the story is setup because it matters why they should trust each other or not; it matters if the Lucifage member even considers the Chieron person a Hunter that should be trusted.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it is not aloud at all. I didn't many ANY Lucifuge and Cheiron member, just these specific two. Again, the situation that brought them to this point is important, and by default I would expect there to be some constant friction between the factions given the overall stance they both have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154433#post1154433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's make something clear: I don't like arguing with people like ElvesOfZion. I don't want to &quot;win&quot; this argument. I am just explaining my problem with the Code and defending my point of view. My opinion, as well as Raven's, is that it's too limiting as it is, and doesn't make sense for some of the hunter groups. Maybe instead of dismissing our complain, it could be a good idea to think about how to make it more nuanced, or figure out what could be improved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not trying to 'win' either. I am trying to make rationed and explained commentary about the rules and how they work so that the Developers, writers and fans can read them and improve their games (both made and played) by understanding and making conscious decisions about the way things work. What I am not doing is throwing my 'opinion' out like it is some golden thing and expecting everyone to either agree or be silent; and I am especially not misrepresenting the rules as a way to back up my opinion.<br /> If you don't want to argue with me that is easy, just don't quote and reply to me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1526\" data-vbnamecard=\"1526\">Diggs</a> , the reason I haven't replied to TheKingsRaven is that their comments are clearly just opinion. Statements about how the game 'should' be. Darinas on the other hand made erroneous mechanical statements which is what I was commenting on (even starting with 'Correct me If I am wrong').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 10-31-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:22:23-07:00","id":1154491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't expect you to read their mind, but it would be helpful for the discussion if you were to ask them. It does have bearing on the discussion to know the setup of the team and the characters personalities and motiviations because that's what determines what Breaking Points should be taken and what modifiers should be applied. Anything else is bad white room theorycrafting.<br /> <br /> It matters how the story is setup because it matters why they should trust each other or not; it matters if the Lucifage member even considers the Chieron person a Hunter that should be trusted.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it is not aloud at all. I didn't many ANY Lucifuge and Cheiron member, just these specific two. Again, the situation that brought them to this point is important, and by default I would expect there to be some constant friction between the factions given the overall stance they both have. </div> </div> </div>... You do realize that by your logic, weither the Code applies or not becomes extremely subjective and will change in the same situation depending on how the Storyteller sees it? I kinda was under the impression the intend with this Code was to avoid that and establish clear lines, what with the playtest giving a clear definition of what counts or doesn't count as a monster (namely having Dread Powers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I am not doing is throwing my 'opinion' out like it is some golden thing and expecting everyone to either agree or be silent; and I am especially not misrepresenting the rules as a way to back up my opinion. </div> </div> </div>Neither am I, despite what you seem to think. I don't &quot;expect everyone to agree or be silent&quot;, otherwise there would be no point in this; I am trying to explain why I think this Code doesn't work, demonstrating it with examples, and as you said it yourself, I <i>admitted</i> I could be wrong on some points. Just the fact I stated this proves I wasn't giving my opinions as facts.<br /> <br /> As for misrepresenting the rules... clearly we have a completely different interpretation. As I said, for me, &quot;betraying a fellow hunter&quot; qualifies as &quot;acting against another hunter&quot;, obviously you disagree on that. I don't see why your interpretation would be more valid than mine, but I will admit that if both are valid, then yeah, my exemple might not be that much of a problem. But as I said above, I was under the impression this Code was meant to be more clear-cut than that. Again, that impression might be false, I fully admit it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't want to argue with me that is easy, just don't quote and reply to me. </div> </div> </div>I still want to debate on the Code and defend my points, I just wish it was less agressive than it is right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Darinas on the other hand made erroneous mechanical statements which is what I was commenting on (even starting with 'Correct me If I am wrong'). </div> </div> </div>Again, <i>I acknowledged from the start that I could be wrong.</i> Stop treating me as if I was presenting my opinions as facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-31-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T16:26:04-07:00","id":1154540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154491#post1154491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... You do realize that by your logic, weither the Code applies or not becomes extremely subjective and will change in the same situation depending on how the Storyteller sees it? I kinda was under the impression the intend with this Code was to avoid that and establish clear lines, what with the playtest giving a clear definition of what counts or doesn't count as a monster (namely having Dread Powers).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Neither am I, despite what you seem to think. I don't &quot;expect everyone to agree or be silent&quot;, otherwise there would be no point in this; I am trying to explain why I think this Code doesn't work, demonstrating it with examples, and as you said it yourself, I <i>admitted</i> I could be wrong on some points. Just the fact I stated this proves I wasn't giving my opinions as facts.<br /> <br /> As for misrepresenting the rules... clearly we have a completely different interpretation. As I said, for me, &quot;betraying a fellow hunter&quot; qualifies as &quot;acting against another hunter&quot;, obviously you disagree on that. I don't see why your interpretation would be more valid than mine, but I will admit that if both are valid, then yeah, my exemple might not be that much of a problem. But as I said above, I was under the impression this Code was meant to be more clear-cut than that. Again, that impression might be false, I fully admit it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I still want to debate on the Code and defend my points, I just wish it was less agressive than it is right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, <i>I acknowledged from the start that I could be wrong.</i> Stop treating me as if I was presenting my opinions as facts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The misrepresentation was in the Breaking Point versus Integrity loss point. And when I said there was a difference, you called it semantics and then went on as if there was no difference. Admitting you COULD be wrong only works if you later admit that you ARE wrong when it comes up. <br /> <br /> I'm not intending to being aggressive at all, I apologize if it comes off that way. I do expect in a conversation about a game system that the rules be presented clearly and accurately and that opinions be backed up by examples and facts. Otherwise no progressive discourse can be had. <br /> <br /> Given the quoted post about your statements of restrictiveness, maybe that should be what you ask. The issue may not be with the actual mechanics at all, just in the wording of the presentation, leading some to interpret them more harshly or strictly than intended. It seems to me that the given that the Storyteller is a role this game intends to have and a presumption that this game (like all others in the Chronicles line) will have sections about the Golden Rule and the Storyteller being an arbitrator of when to apply rules that it is odd to assume that the intention is that The Code be so strict mechanically that a Storyteller's judgment is not needed in its application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T16:44:38-07:00","id":1154543,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's just forget about this, since clearly neither of us intends to be agressive, and I feel we are completely lost in the argument. To be frank I am not even sure <i>what</i> the point of the conversation initially was anymore. Just to clarify, I think the problem here, at least based on both King Raven and me, is that the Code looks like it's too restrictive because it assumes all hunters reason on a &quot;humans matter more than monsters do&quot; (even though not all groups seem like they would adhere to this point of view) and, based on the &quot;Calling a Spades a Spade&quot;, feels like it's encouraging the player to kill monsters indiscriminately while protecting humans even if they are assholes. What point of view are you trying to defend yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T16:57:02-07:00","id":1154547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154543#post1154543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's just forget about this, since clearly neither of us intends to be agressive, and I feel we are completely lost in the argument. To be frank I am not even sure <i>what</i> the point of the conversation initially was anymore. Just to clarify, I think the problem here, at least based on both King Raven and me, is that the Code looks like it's too restrictive because it assumes all hunters reason on a &quot;humans matter more than monsters do&quot; (even though not all groups seem like they would adhere to this point of view) and, based on the &quot;Calling a Spades a Spade&quot;, feels like it's encouraging the player to kill monsters indiscriminately while protecting humans even if they are assholes. What point of view are you trying to defend yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. That Breaking Points are not Integrity loss. (This was the main reason I commented).<br /> 2. That experiencing Breaking Points should be a regular experience for anyone in a stressful and/or traumatic position such as being a Hunter.<br /> 3. That The Code adding additional Breaking Points makes sense because a normal mortal does their best to move on after experiencing the supernatural and the definition of a Hunter is (at bare minimum*) someone who after encountering the Supernatural decides it is so important that they must dedicate an ever larger portion of their life to it.<br /> 4. That without therapy or other release and recovery, ALL Hunters should be dropping towards 0 Integrity over time.<br /> <br /> *I say at bare minimum because it is possible to be completely engrossed in the supernatural without being a Hunter. See Mystery Cult Initiation, Heroes, Alchemists, members of various Deviant Orgs, Deava and other companies that deal with the supernatural but are not Hunters. I am probably missing some other examples.<br /> <br /> A couple points that I had not yet gotten to:<br /> <br /> 1. Maybe some of the 'Hunter' groups from 1e, shouldn't be. They can be other kinds of organizations.<br /> 2. That the Call a Spade a Spade sidebar apparently comes across to some people quit differently than others and could stand to be softened since I and others have focused much more on the 'when push comes to shove' nature of it's message but other see it as a hard and fast rule about daily interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 10-31-2017, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T17:22:18-07:00","id":1154555,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks for clarifying. Now let's see how I can answer point by point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. That Breaking Points are not Integrity loss. (This was the main reason I commented). </div> </div> </div>Fine, point acknowledged; To be frank, that wasn't really what I meant, sorry if I gave you that impression; clearly I misphrased.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. That experiencing Breaking Points should be a regular experience for anyone in a stressful and/or traumatic position such as being a Hunter. </div> </div> </div>Acknowledged too, though I personally think that suffering one based on the regular Integrity system (such as the ones caused by Lunacy or by seeing something supernatural new for the first time) should already make it regular enough. Moving on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. That The Code adding additional Breaking Points makes sense because a normal mortal does their best to move on after experiencing the supernatural and the definition of a Hunter is (at bare minimum*) someone who after encountering the Supernatural decides it is so important that they must dedicate an ever larger portion of their life to it. </div> </div> </div>For the first part, I refer you to my answer to point 2. Same for the second part, though I will admit I think your definition of hunters fits my point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. That without therapy or other release and recovery, ALL Hunters should be dropping towards 0 Integrity over time. </div> </div> </div>No argument here, I don't even remember saying anything against this particular point.<br /> <br /> Now moving to your new points:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Maybe some of the 'Hunter' groups from 1e, shouldn't be. They can be other kinds of organizations </div> </div> </div>Strongly (and respectfully) disagreed. As I mentioned before, one of the main appeals Hunters had for me (and by extension for many of my friends, including my own players) was the diversity in its groups, their approach of the supernatural, their beliefs and the kind of abilities they could have. Remove that, and the whole game would lost a lot of its charm and become much less rich, at least as far as I am concerned. Moving these groups to other kinds of organizations would admittedly mean they would still be playable, that would make them lose the spotlight and potentially mean some of them wouldn't be playable anymore, depending how it's handled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. That the Call a Spade a Spade sidebar apparently comes across to some people quit differently than others and could stand to be softened since I and others have focused much more on the 'when push comes to shove' nature of it's message but other see it as a hard and fast rule about daily interactions. </div> </div> </div>Nothing to say against that one.<br /> <br /> Here, hope this clarified things for both of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T19:49:24-07:00","id":1154584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154474#post1154474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1526\" data-vbnamecard=\"1526\">Diggs</a> , the reason I haven't replied to TheKingsRaven is that their comments are clearly just opinion. Statements about how the game 'should' be. Darinas on the other hand made erroneous mechanical statements which is what I was commenting on (even starting with 'Correct me If I am wrong').</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool with me. I don't like to see people wasting their time and I've seen this conversation from the other thread. If you switched to simply corrected mechanics, that is a sound plan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wasn't implying anyone was trying to win an argument. It is more like there has been a fair amount of talking past each other because when one person sees a gold dress and another sees a blue dress there can be no reasonable discussion of which shade. I assumed it was largely unintentional. No right or wrong. There is an irreconcilable difference of opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 10-31-2017, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T20:11:09-07:00","id":1154588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154547#post1154547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *I say at bare minimum because it is possible to be completely engrossed in the supernatural without being a Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div> Who says the groups you listed aren't Hunters? I've always treated them as Hunters. (Except Heroes who're supernatural beings themselves).<br /> <br /> take alchemists, the Ascending Ones are alchemists so alchemy can't exclude you from hunterdom. The alchemists in Promethian 2ed spend a lot of time hunting Promethians. It makes perfect sense to give them access to the Hunter template.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154547#post1154547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Maybe some of the 'Hunter' groups from 1e, shouldn't be. They can be other kinds of organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monica has already confirmed all the core 12 are in 2ed. And if they're in then the code needs to work for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T20:12:16-07:00","id":1154590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wasn't implying anyone was trying to win an argument. It is more like there has been a fair amount of talking past each other because when one person sees a gold dress and another sees a blue dress there can be no reasonable discussion of which shade. I assumed it was largely unintentional. No right or wrong. There is an irreconcilable difference of opinion. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's cool with me. I don't like to see people wasting their time and I've seen this conversation from the other thread. If you switched to simply corrected mechanics, that is a sound plan. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> </div> </div>Thanks^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who says the groups you listed aren't Hunters? I've always treated them as Hunters. (Except Heroes who're supernatural beings themselves).<br /> <br /> take alchemists, the Ascending Ones are alchemists so alchemy can't exclude you from hunterdom. The alchemists in Promethian 2ed spend a lot of time hunting Promethians. It makes perfect sense to give them access to the Hunter template. </div> </div> </div>So you play them as hunters? As in they could risk Willpower and everything?<br /> <br /> (also, on an unrelated note: what about the Stormwracked, do you consider them hunters? Not part of the debate, I am just curious.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Monica has already confirmed all the core 12 are in 2ed. And if they're in then the code needs to work for them. </div> </div> </div>Does that include the Ashwood Abbey? I remember they considered removing them at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-31-2017, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T03:04:11-07:00","id":1154656,"title":"","content":"The Alchemists in Promethean strike me as could-have-been hunters akin to the not-lucifurge from Inferno. A sort of foil to the ascending ones, if you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T03:29:37-07:00","id":1154660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154590#post1154590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (also, on an unrelated note: what about the Stormwracked, do you consider them hunters? Not part of the debate, I am just curious.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Stormwracked are written as Hunters just without mentioning any terms unique to the Hunter books. Though they're a Compact. They're not organised enough to be a Conspiracy. Their Checkmate firing pattern Merit is a Tactic.<br /> <br /> Other hunters would frown on their obvious loyalty to the Queen of Storms and her Nobles, but there's Hunters who'd frown on the MM's loyalty to God. I wouldn't make Hunters that loyal to physical monsters (rather than disembodied gods) in a Hunter book (maybe in the antagonist chapter), but they're not in a Hunter book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-01-2017, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T03:46:41-07:00","id":1154663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Absolutely. Stormwracked are written as Hunters just without mentioning any terms unique to the Hunter books. Though they're a Compact. They're not organised enough to be a Conspiracy. Their Checkmate firing pattern Merit is a Tactic.<br /> <br /> Other hunters would frown on their obvious loyalty to the Queen of Storms and her Nobles, but there's Hunters who'd frown on the MM's loyalty to God. I wouldn't make Hunters that loyal to physical monsters (rather than disembodied gods) in a Hunter book (maybe in the antagonist chapter), but they're not in a Hunter book. </div> </div> </div>... Well, we'll have to take that into account for the Princess supplement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:39:05-07:00","id":1154786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154107#post1154107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the Code stands now, I see several problems that would be encountered in my games. Namely, one of the major recurring themes in my games is that for all the power possessed by supernatural creatures, the greatest monsters are often human.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The true monster is Man!&quot; is generally not going to be a theme supported by a set of games that have been repeatedly emphasized as humanist in tone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another scenario: Hunter B's best friend escapes from Arcadia, and pours out the whole ordeal over a couple drinks. Hunter B gives a shoulder to cry on, and promises that he's not alone anymore. He even helps his changeling buddy to deal with that pesky Huntsman that just won't leave him alone. Then one day, he comes across another hunter that's beaten his changeling buddy to within an inch of his life. If his buddy manages to turn things around and takes out the guy, Hunter B will suffer a breaking point because a supernatural creature that he refused to harm ended up hurting someone. Perhaps I misunderstood, but it didn't sound like self defense was a valid justification. </div> </div> </div>I'll be completely frank: <i>This is a terrible example. </i>Let's put this into the context of the world and an actual story/game to diagram out all the major failure points.<br /> <br /> <b>First</b> and most pressingly: Crossover like what you've implied by direct reference to several Changeling-specific narrative elements being interacted with by this hypothetical hunter is <i>inherently </i>going to run into difficulties \u2014 Hunter's mechanics not playing well with the abilities of actual characters in other gamelines without making judgment calls as an ST was a remarked-upon issue with running the game in allied crossover play in 1e. &quot;Your mortal monster-hunter character is going to encounter some narrative/psychological tension maintaining friendly relations with monsters&quot; is one of those things that seems like an expected problem that you either accept or houserule around if you want to press onward with it, much like the nocturnal constraints of Vampire or the risk of Disquiet in most meaningful interactions Prometheans have with people.<br /> <br /> &quot;The thing I changed about myself so that dunking myself in exposure to magic doesn't make me a complete wreck of a person pulls in ways that I rationally and intellectually and surface-emotionally may not be comfortable with when confronted with the problems keeping up a friendship with someone a mad god turned into a monster&quot; is a point of drama that informs the setting and affects how those characters interact in a way that underlines the themes of the supernatural in the Chronicles of Darkness, which is not a generic system where magic is harmless and monster-hunters exist entirely out of unfounded paranoia and prejudice.<br /> <br /> <b>Second</b>: Okay, your buddy was changed by the Fae and made his way back. One \u2014 <i>Believing this at face value is being overtrusting verging on gullible, as is volunteering this information.</i> General trends being what they are, if your friend is a changeling, he's not the only one in town, to say nothing of what fetches do to hike up the threshold for trusting people to be who they seem to be. If these characters either <i>don't exist</i> or haven't <i>already been antagonists in the story</i>, then you have brought a lone changeling into your Hunter story, presumably for the purposes of underlining the problems with how that character living in the same town as you with magic powers, which indicates a certain degree of stewardship over the buddy on your hunter character's part, which the Code covers through its Persistent Conditions and the fact that allowing harm to come to people because of the supernatural is a breaking point.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, if those characters <i>do</i> exist in the story and your Hunter character inhabits a setting populated in part by the setting's most notorious imposters and the pod-people their erstwhile masters left behind \u2014 the former of which often have the ability to mess with memory and emotion or change their features or invade people's dreams, never mind trade and sell roles and information like the things that might confirm your supposed changeling buddy's identity \u2014 then you have to deal with not only a breaking point every time your buddy develops a new magic power and demonstrates it to you as an exercise of trust/full disclosure, but you have to deal with the fact that the people who understand what he's been through are generally invested in keeping the things they got away from out, which is generally best managed by getting more magical powers and/or interfering in people's lives, which you and your cell may take umbrage with and which will generally be a reason for your changeling buddy to keep secrets from you.<br /> <br /> Two \u2014 <i>Changelings are trouble-magnets</i>. Even if your buddy and his support group behave themselves completely as model citizens and don't ever pursue resources to enhance their own security (to say nothing of just deciding to flee the coop through the <i>dread dimension they can all make a lasting portal to at minimal cost</i>), the fact is that there are certain temptations they all have at their fingertips (to say nothing of the more particular fixations some of them may have developed during their time in Arcadia) and ensuring that they do not seize those temptations requires a level of scrutiny and surveillance that is comparable to imprisonment \u2014 i.e. <i>the thing they all have pretty strong feelings about</i>. And that temptation to gird themselves against aggressors is only going to get stronger when the world they inhabit is one where most of them are on the run from fate-twisting god-monsters and the lesser horrors that seek to court their favor \u2014 going after the Lost's friends and loved ones is a time-honored tactic among their enemies, and most of those aren't going to be hunters. Do you put your friend above your family, his family, your entire town and everyone you love?<br /> <br /> <b>Third</b>: Huntsmen aren't early-game antagonists in either iteration of Changeling 2e \u2014 the Fae don't send one out for a fresh-from-the-Hedge fugitive, which means you and your buddy with the heart-twisting magical powers either went through a lot of stuff that imperiled your worldview as someone who tries to keep the supernatural from harming the mundane or reconnected a long way into his time as a faerie. Neither speaks well for your Integrity with or without the Code.<br /> <br /> Hunters, by a similar metric, generally aren't going to go after a monster without a reason \u2014 sometimes that reason may be petty or banal, but &quot;a hunter comes after your changeling friend&quot; is inherently not something which Just Happens. This holds especially true for changelings, whose innate disguises are helped by the relative manageability of their personal weaknesses \u2014 they don't have Death Rage or the daysleep or even the flickering of their mundane disguises with power use to worry about giving them away, which means either you didn't keep a close enough eye on your buddy or something that wants to get at him tattled to this other hunter (who you've apparently never heard of despite operating in the same region, if the lack of detail is any indication) to call in a hit.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if you <i>are present for a conflict between your changeling buddy and a hunter and you do nothing to intervene</i>, then of course you're going to get shaken up if your buddy dies or your buddy with supernatural powers kills a guy. The workaround for that is to step in before it escalates to the point of murder, broker an understanding, and make it clear that your changeling buddy is not going to hurt anybody on your watch. &quot;Monsters hurt people&quot; is something that regular Integrity normalizes by not looking at it \u2014 a direct confrontation with that facet is inherently going to be a problem for a monster-hunter who is friends with a monster.<br /> <br /> Your buddy attracting a conflict with a hunter due to his state as a supernatural being does not get a pass from consideration to Integrity just because he's your buddy and to assume two members of differently-regularly-paranoid splats having an unconditionally trusting relationship without difficulty as the goal of a core narrative widget in a monster-hunting game diminishes the themes of both Hunter and Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As written, it seems like &quot;Make sure you have the right weapon, make sure you have no witnesses, make sure it's really dead, make sure you leave no evidence,&quot; is always a safe approach to the Vigil, at least as far as Integrity is concerned. If you want to maintain a high Integrity on the Vigil, be a speciesist bastard and sentence everything touched by the supernatural to death regardless of actions or context. </div> </div> </div>In other words, the folks who can manage the occasional doublethink of being a serial killer or a mass-murderer because they get enough of a reprieve from the supernatural to cool down and reinforce their ties to humanity sleep better at night than the folks who give the monsters a chance and keep tabs on every one that they know about in an environment where the monsters are not universally well-behaved.<br /> <br /> You maintain a high Integrity on the Vigil by strengthening your Resolve and Composure, maintaining multiple Touchstones, being self-sacrificing and adhering to your Virtue, regularly engaging positively with people you trust, and not letting monsters hurt people while you're around. Killing every monster you see happens to have a more long-term success rate in this regard than babysitting an entire motley or freehold, but as has been underlined multiple times in other games, a high or low Integrity rating does not translate to a &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; character, and as has been highlighted within this very discussion, a breaking point roll is not synonymous with Integrity loss.<br /> <br /> A high-Integrity hunter who burned down a house full of ghost-children is no more a contradiction in terms than a high-Wisdom Seer of the Throne who makes liberal use of hard mind-control. Meanwhile, the Integrity 5 werewolf-watcher is going to be growing a lot faster thanks to the Beat-engine strapped to her psyche, and she'll have less cleanup to worry about in the long-term even without membership in a clandestine government agency or a debauched secret society to lighten the load.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:27:58-07:00","id":1154798,"title":"","content":"Satchel. A mortal who's loved one is kidnapped by faeries and resolves to rescue them is one of the classic faerie tale plots. That alone makes it a valid backstory for a Hunter. So don't go looking for reasons why it can't work. Look for ways to make it work: From Compacts who can provide inside knowledge on the fae, to the Wyrd itself stepping in to make sure a Hunter is in the right place at the right time. Dream Catchers has at least three different things just about that plot.<br /> <br /> and if your changeling buddy got into a fight with another Hunter and someone died that could be worth a breaking point. But if your buddy merely arranged matters so the police caught the Hunter breaking into their home. And the Hunter asks you to use your connections to get the charges quashed and you refuse because he's a dangerous loose cannon who tried to kill your friend, that should not be a breakdown point. <br /> <br /> As for &quot;Humans are the real monsters&quot;. It's not my taste but so long as the Cherion Group exist it's a completely valid theme, and using Cherion as the antagonist is also valid. There's plenty of examples of Hunter vs Hunter in 1E. Far too much to assume Hunters having any other Hunter's back is a default position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-01-2017, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:45:09-07:00","id":1154809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The true monster is Man!&quot; is generally not going to be a theme supported by a set of games that have been repeatedly emphasized as humanist in tone. </div> </div> </div>... Either you have a completely different definition of &quot;humanist&quot; than I do, or we REALLY don't have the same understanding of this game. To me, Chronicles of Darkness, and Hunter especially, always had as a major theme that no, being human doesn't automatically makes you a good guy, and humans can in fact be just as much assholes as any random supernatural critter you'll see bump in the night. I mean, seriously, we are talking about the gameline where the protagonists are at risk of turning into slasher movie villains, and the books are very clear that while supernatural influence can help to the transition, in the end a hunter who goes slasher has nobody to blame but himself. Can hardly get more &quot;humans are the real monsters&quot; than that.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, not gonna get involved with the rest of your post, that particular bit is between you and White Oak Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:46:06-07:00","id":1154831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154809#post1154809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Either you have a completely different definition of &quot;humanist&quot; than I do, or we REALLY don't have the same understanding of this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've engaged with people who think humans having the capacity to be assholes or criminals or otherwise awful is a legitimate mark against Promethean's central default pursuit. Their misanthropy is as irrelevant to that game as it is about this game. &quot;The part of me that resolved to be a monster-hunter means I'm going to run into some trouble when I identify more with the ethos of a monster than with a human they're preying upon&quot; is a problem that the game <i>puts forth as a problem for characters to struggle with</i>. The core character concept is not one that gets to avoid these complications.<br /> <br /> If you aren't willing to make the buy-in of &quot;I'm hunting monsters and some of those monsters are an awful lot like people and this forces me to confront some unpleasant questions about who I am and what I'm doing hunting monsters unless I draw some hard boundaries about the things that can change shapes or control minds and hurt my friends' heads to look directly at&quot; then there's not much point in talking about what the game should and shouldn't do in the name of notional flexibility based on a rigid reading of narrative mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, Chronicles of Darkness, and Hunter especially, always had as a major theme that no, being human doesn't automatically makes you a good guy, </div> </div> </div>Not positing that it does! But if your position is &quot;humans are, on the whole, worse than monsters that regularly steal blood, ruin lives, break reality, shatter sanity, and attract the attention of eldritch horrors from beyond mortal ken,&quot; then a set of gamelines where being a conscious and responsible supernatural being often means interfering with humankind as little as possible while maintaining a limited number of strong personal mundane relationships is perhaps not the best place to exercise the assertion that that position is equally valuable to the game as the one where knowing who you are and what your life is depends on applying a certain degree of compartmentalization to the horror of those parts of reality that strain the mind to encounter.<br /> <br /> Humanity does not need to be unanimously virtuous for mundane criminals to be a different category of issue from sanity-melting creatures of variable ethics and cognizance, nor does an instinctive understanding that the supernatural is naturally incentivized to keep its distance from mundane humanity translate to anything that merits a prompt for Godwin's Law.<br /> <br /> If your Hunter characters are in a setting where the monsters only go after bad people and their attentions are obvious enough that monster-hunters are present and active, your Hunter characters are going to have to make decisions that influence their place in the narrative. What happens when the monsters run out of bad people? What is your cell's plan for bad people in the absence of monstrous interference? Why should poking at the dark underbelly of the world in either sense of the word not be a strain on your self-image? What does being a bad person actually have to do with vampires and why is letting a bad person get eaten supposed to be better for your sense of self than letting a bad person try to become a better person in the absence of bloodhungry undead interference? Is handling these issues their job or can they just stick to keeping monsters from messing with human lives and systems?<br /> <br /> These are things a Hunter game that doesn't deal with the monstrous equivalent of wild animals attacking complete innocents has to handle, and a monster hunter who makes an exception is one who has trouble coming down the line one way or another. Humanity as a general phenomenon and at least in the particulars of the people you take up the Vigil for has to be worth it for stability to be a thing. You find out your neighbor's a serial murderer who's not a slasher? Kill him and deal with the consequences, let the prospective-hero vampire have him and deal with the consequences, hope he becomes a slasher or a vampire and deal with him then, or alert the authorities and let them deal with the consequences. This isn't a situation where being a monster-hunter gives you an advantage or an excuse and Hunter would be a <i>very different game</i> if it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:37:11-07:00","id":1154847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then you have to deal with not only a breaking point every time your buddy develops a new magic power and demonstrates it to you you. </div> </div> </div>I am not sure if I understood this right, but I interpreted the wording on the breaking point of &quot;Type of supernatural power&quot; to be more broad. As in, you encounter a Ghost for the first time and witness one of its powers, then get a breaking point. If you then witness a second ghost that uses the same &quot;Type&quot; of power, you don't get a breaking point. I didn't interpret it as &quot;Every separate power is its own breaking point&quot;, though I could certainly be wrong there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T16:52:55-07:00","id":1154885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154831#post1154831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not positing that it does! But if your position is &quot;humans are, on the whole, worse than monsters that regularly steal blood, ruin lives, break reality, shatter sanity, and attract the attention of eldritch horrors from beyond mortal ken&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> To play devil's advocate for a theme I've admitted is not to my taste, I can think of two ways to make this theme work.<br /> <br /> The first is to say that human organization's are larger, stronger, and more omnipresent than supernatural ones so when they go evil they do more harm than supernatural equivalents. A Vampire might abduct and Ghoul someone to use as a slave, but an international human trafficking ring with thousands of slaves - supernatural's innate drawbacks keep them from playing at that level. You'd have to ignore setting elements from the other gamelines that say supernaturals do play at that level, but ignoring other gamelines is normal.<br /> <br /> The second is to say that monsters are innately evil or at least innately damaged in a way that's likely to cause them to harm others. Humans are unique because they alone have the freedom too choose good or evil. Thus even if they cause worse harm they are morally worse. This theme would work great for the Lucifuge since internal evils and choice are core themes to them, their primary foe, Infernals, are created by human evil. I think it also fits Catholic theology so that works with the Lucifuge too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154831#post1154831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity does not need to be unanimously virtuous for mundane criminals to be a different category of issue from sanity-melting creatures of variable ethics and cognizance, nor does an instinctive understanding that the supernatural is naturally incentivized to keep its distance from mundane humanity translate to anything that merits a prompt for Godwin's Law.</div> </div> </div> </div> Contrawise you can acknowledge that human criminals and supernaturals are different categories without concluding that it's acceptable to kill said supernaturals without evidence of wrongdoing on their part.<br /> <br /> Nobody is making Nazi comparisons because Hunters have different categories but because the default Code says killing innocent children is acceptable if they're in the other category. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154831#post1154831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You find out your neighbor's a serial murderer who's not a slasher? Kill him and deal with the consequences, let the prospective-hero vampire have him and deal with the consequences, hope he becomes a slasher or a vampire and deal with him then, or alert the authorities and let them deal with the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Make a choice and deal with the consequences&quot; are words I can live by. But I think Breaking Points are the wrong mechanic to model those consequences.<br /> <br /> I would rather The Code was flexible enough that a Hunter could make any of those choices without a Breaking Point, and the consequences are Tells and of course having to live up to your Code.<br /> <br /> (Maybe killing a human should be too much for the code to allow without a severe risk of becoming a Slasher, but there's always beating a confession out of them and pointing the police to the bodies)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:08:10-07:00","id":1154888,"title":"","content":"How much of the problems people have with the code is just from the Calling A Spade A Spade Sidebar? Cause I am thinking it is a lot. How does the rest of it read to you without that sidebar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:52:28-07:00","id":1154902,"title":"","content":"You're right to ask, that sidebar is a very large part of the problem. If that sidebar was replaced with something saying the list of breaking points presented in the playtest document was a game mechanic and not something that makes a statement about the player characters beliefs or emotions that would go a long way towards fixing things. <br /> <br /> It wouldn't be the entire solution. Only being able to change one element is not enough flexibility, even Network Zero needs at least two changes: one for revealing the supernatural and one saying they don't have to help their arch enemy (VALKARIE). <br /> <br /> You could also get weirdness if you didn't distinguish between modifications that made your Code closer or further from mundane society. <br /> <br /> But yes, that sidebar is a big part of the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-01-2017, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:56:26-07:00","id":1154905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Make a choice and deal with the consequences&quot; are words I can live by. But I think Breaking Points are the wrong mechanic to model those consequences. </div> </div> </div>I agree. There are other ways to cause dilemna than force Breaking points everywhere.<br /> <br /> On a sidenote, I don't get something: what's that &quot;a mundane serial killer who isn't a slasher&quot; bullcrap even is anyway? I mean, I <i>might</i> not understand how this work, or maybe that changed compared to 1E, but I was under the impression mundane serial killers WERE slashers in the New World of Darkness. I mean, isn't that the entire point of making the distinction between Rippers and Scourges? With Rippers being mundane serial killers while Scourges are the supernatural ones? At least I didn't get the impression they made a distinction between a Ripper and a mundane serial killer when I read the Slasher supplement. Kinda feel like they are making this distinction to enforce a clear line with this Code.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:01:48-07:00","id":1154907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154885#post1154885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrawise you can acknowledge that human criminals and supernaturals are different categories without concluding that it's acceptable to kill said supernaturals without evidence of wrongdoing on their part.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When the chips are down&quot; does not mean &quot;at the drop of a hat.&quot;<br /> <br /> The vast majority of sapient monsters for whom wrongdoing is a concern are liable to understand that showing off their supernatural qualities is damaging to the human psyche to the point where most of them have at least an institutional mandate against such revelations if not an internal consequence for breaking that secrecy. Most of the ones y'all're expressing concern over will generally have ample room to provide evidence against their doing wrong. If they've gotten caught out as a monster, you're at the point where their doing harm is on the table and the Code says that you have to <i>treat them as a concern</i> \u2014 and therefore at least <i>keep an eye on them</i> and be prepared for the possibility that you have to put them down if they get worse instead of better \u2014 or take their word that it won't happen again and leave the possibility open that they break your trust.<br /> <br /> That's an incentive to not leave monsters alone once you're aware of them, which installs them in your character's notional relationship web about as solidly as your character's Touchstones. The base dichotomy of your gut telling you to kill-or-confine things that break with mundane reality regardless of how personable they are is there to feed into the drama of hunters struggling with trust as a scarce commodity in the Chronicles of Darkness, not to Force Your Character To Kill Varney The Harmless Ratsucker just because Jack The Egomaniac down at the Abbey has no problem doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nobody is making Nazi comparisons because Hunters have different categories but because the default Code says killing innocent children is acceptable if they're in the other category. </div> </div> </div>Most innocent children do not survive long as supernatural creatures while remaining innocent children and most monsters a hunter is liable to encounter outside of a contrived hypothetical or a purpose-built scenario are not going to be innocent children. The Code does not mandate killing a school full of Deviant kids \u2014 it just adds the tacit burden of responsibility for any harm they do to mortals if given free reign to the things that can potentially break you down, which some hunters determine to be too much of a risk, but holding onto your self as a monster hunter while allowing a group of monsters whose activities drew your attention as a monster hunter to continue to act unmonitored is entirely possible under the Code.<br /> <br /> That the Code does not inherently limit the potential for localized monster-genocide does not make every Hunter a would-be Hitler just because the superpowered night-people that traumatize mortal minds to confront are harder to justify protecting than the block full of muggers and car-thieves who happen to share a species with most of your friends and family. Humans generally can't impersonate your loved ones, fake consciousness as a tendril of an eldritch god-thing, or make you believe they were never in the room where they ripped out your cellmate's guts with a dining fork. The unknown is a broad field, and the motives and capabilities of supernatural entities are known-unknowns even to a lot of monsters dealing with their own condition. Contagion spreads unless killed or contained, and the Vigil exists in response to that quality one way or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154847#post1154847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if I understood this right, but I interpreted the wording on the breaking point of &quot;Type of supernatural power&quot; to be more broad. As in, you encounter a Ghost for the first time and witness one of its powers, then get a breaking point. If you then witness a second ghost that uses the same &quot;Type&quot; of power, you don't get a breaking point. I didn't interpret it as &quot;Every separate power is its own breaking point&quot;, though I could certainly be wrong there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more concerned about the fact that seeing your buddy with the face of a cat leap three stories into the air does not prepare you for his pal with the burning hair opting to transmogrify into a pillar of flame. Changelings in particular have some of the most diverse supernatural portfolios this side of the Supernal, but even within the comparatively narrow band of, say, vampiric Disciplines, radiating attraction, becoming invisible, sprouting claws and seemingly Nightcrawling your way across the room are all capabilities that you might never have encountered before you concluded your beef with the local Ventrue dynasty. Hunters who can hyperspecialize are lucky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:19:09-07:00","id":1154915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154905#post1154905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a sidenote, I don't get something: what's that &quot;a mundane serial killer who isn't a slasher&quot; bullcrap even is anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey, look at the text:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Slashers do bear some resemblance, in terms of their pathology and methods, to serial killers. The most important difference is a subtle one, but crucial to understanding the slasher. Serial killers take human life to inflict pain, to elicit emotion or sensation in themselves, or to lash out at their abusers in symbolic fashion. For a slasher, the kill is the point. Some varieties of slasher do espouse higher or more complex agendas, but faced with a choice between killing and not killing, a slasher will always kill. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the frightening truth: sometimes, people kill. And not just out of passion, not because of poor judgment or misguided revenge. No, sometimes they kill because they want to, they need to. Maybe they\u2019re born that way. Maybe they\u2019re made. Some are driven to the point, while others are programmed.<br /> <br /> They can\u2019t just kill one person. Oh, no. They kill two, three, ten, and they keep going until the body count mounts or until they\u2019re stopped. They become compulsive about it. It must be done in a proper way. A certain organ must be harvested. A cipher needs to be painted on the ceiling above the body. The kill must be completed with a homemade weapon: a set of teeth made from bone spurs or a makeshift ax forged out of junkyard metal. Some have their victims and will not stray: they only kill liars, lustful teens, corrupt cops, beautiful people, pedophiles, perverts, prostitutes, cops, or housewives. Some just don\u2019t care. They\u2019ll kill anybody. Anywhere. A horror house with bodies stacked to the goddamn rafters.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the killing changes them. It\u2019s like a switch. Except, instead of turning something on, it\u2019s turning something off. A light, maybe. A part of one\u2019s self, of one\u2019s soul. A place inside goes dead \u2014 or, hell, maybe it was dead long ago. Maybe it was never alive in the first place.<br /> <br /> And out of that darkness rises power. From the void comes secret power that couples the endless urge to kill with supernatural might or monstrous cunning. Soon, the killer cannot be stopped by bullets. Or maybe his words become truly honeyed, sliding into the ear canals and the brains of his victims like a little snake: could be that, as long as he uses his trusty crowbar, his kills are always perfect, always immediate.<br /> <br /> The slasher. A perfect predator. Society\u2019s modern bogeyman. Part human, part\u2026 something else. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:28:32-07:00","id":1154920,"title":"","content":"1) I did say I might be wrong and have missed something. You could have just said &quot;actually, it's mentioned here&quot; instead of being snarkily agressive, I would have appreciated.<br /> 2) I would appreciate even more if you actually<i> listed the source of the text </i>instead of just dropping it like this. Is it from the 1E hunter corebook? The Slasher supplement? The 2E playtest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:30:57-07:00","id":1154921,"title":"","content":"The 2E Playtest. It's kind of recognizable at a glance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:40:31-07:00","id":1154924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 2E Playtest. It's kind of recognizable at a glance. </div> </div> </div>Actually, I checked, the second paragraph is from the Slasher supplement. That said, this paragraph doesn't explicitly refer to them as distinct from mundane serial killers (the &quot;Part human, part\u2026 something else&quot; bit can easily be interpreted as a metaphor or the character being monstrous by his sole personality), and the Hunter corebook explicitly gives &quot;a serial killer&quot; as a definition for Slasher, while stating they &quot;often&quot; have supernatural powers (though as the Slasher supplement confirms, that's not always the case).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the first quote indeed isn't either from the 1e Corebook nor from the Slasher supplement, meaning it's indeed probably from the 2E playtest. Which would explain why I didn't see it; I was mostly focused on the Code and didn't really read the rest of the playtest yet. Considering my primary problem is with the Code, I think I can be forgiven for that.<br /> <br /> But this only reinforces my impression they are trying to make Slashers distinct from serial killers in 2E in order to draw a clearer line between humans and supernatural and enforce that Code. Which I personally feel is a mistake, since the whole point of slashers was to get hunters out of their comfort zone by giving them true humans killers who still manage to be just as inhuman as supernatural beings. But whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-01-2017, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:43:18-07:00","id":1154925,"title":"","content":"Ah, my apologies, the second part is from Slasher, you are correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:59:11-07:00","id":1154926,"title":"","content":"No problem^^ that can happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:13:38-07:00","id":1154934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154907#post1154907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more concerned about the fact that seeing your buddy with the face of a cat leap three stories into the air does not prepare you for his pal with the burning hair opting to transmogrify into a pillar of flame. Changelings in particular have some of the most diverse supernatural portfolios this side of the Supernal, but even within the comparatively narrow band of, say, vampiric Disciplines, radiating attraction, becoming invisible, sprouting claws and seemingly Nightcrawling your way across the room are all capabilities that you might never have encountered before you concluded your beef with the local Ventrue dynasty. Hunters who can hyperspecialize are lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on your interpretation of the text. I could mean &quot;Once you see a Changeling ability, other changeling abilities don't bother you&quot;. The other obvious interpretation would be &quot;Once you see mind control, no more mind control would bother you&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) I did say I might be wrong and have missed something. You could have just said &quot;actually, it's mentioned here&quot; instead of being snarkily agressive, I would have appreciated.<br /> 2) I would appreciate even more if you actually<i> listed the source of the text </i>instead of just dropping it like this. Is it from the 1E hunter corebook? The Slasher supplement? The 2E playtest? </div> </div> </div>1E hunter core didn't have Slashers yet, and the text does appear in the 2E playtest.<br /> <br /> It specifically appears under the &quot;Slasher&quot; tab on the right. The quote has a space after it, so copying+pasting the whole thing makes it look like it isn't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 11-01-2017, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:23:24-07:00","id":1154958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154924#post1154924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I checked, the second paragraph is from the Slasher supplement. That said, this paragraph doesn't explicitly refer to them as distinct from mundane serial killers (the &quot;Part human, part\u2026 something else&quot; bit can easily be interpreted as a metaphor or the character being monstrous by his sole personality), and the Hunter corebook explicitly gives &quot;a serial killer&quot; as a definition for Slasher, while stating they &quot;often&quot; have supernatural powers (though as the Slasher supplement confirms, that's not always the case).</div> </div> </div> </div>Things change throughout the course of the line and the Lexicon section of a corebook sometimes exhibits discrepancies with what the terms come to refer to. Slasher mentions &quot;serial killers and slashers&quot; separately throughout and the Conspiracy introduced in that same book draws a distinction between slashers and serial killers as part of the fact that they specialize in the investigation of serial killings:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First and foremost, VASCU investigates and deals with serial killers. The vast majority of those are slashers, <b>serial killers with a mysterious edge</b> that leaves normal law enforcement agencies unable to cope. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> VASCU gets called in to investigate repeat killings. It\u2019s a given that a significant percentage of those calls involve humans who may be monsters, but who aren\u2019t slashers. <b>Not every serial killer is a slasher</b>, and there\u2019s plenty of people who are canny murderers but never make their third kill. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T23:49:29-07:00","id":1154992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154934#post1154934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1E hunter core didn't have Slashers yet, and the text does appear in the 2E playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>correction- Hunter had Slashers in it since its very beginning. See page 294 in the 1E core (sure, a more in depth look was given in Slasher's book, but the concept was there from the start)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T04:46:31-07:00","id":1155017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things change throughout the course of the line and the Lexicon section of a corebook sometimes exhibits discrepancies with what the terms come to refer to. Slasher mentions &quot;serial killers and slashers&quot; separately throughout and the Conspiracy introduced in that same book draws a distinction between slashers and serial killers as part of the fact that they specialize in the investigation of serial killings: </div> </div> </div>Much better.<br /> <br /> Okay, so my bad, Slashers <i>does</i> make a clear distinction between the two terms. Though if I may mention, most of the distinction is made by the fact Slashers don't necessarly fit the exact definition of the serial killer because they don't necessarly follow the same modus operanti, <b>not</b> because they are somehow less mundane or less human. Admittedly that's a bit of a nitpick, but I think it's important, because again, part of what made slashers scary as Hunter antagonists was the fact they could be mundane and were still more human than any supernatural. Dehumanizing them, especially in the contest of this new Code, just turn them into another kind of monster to kill. Don't get me wrong, Slashers <i>should</i> be monstrous, but not in a way that allows hunters to say &quot;well, that's not human, I can kill it just fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> But let's move on and get back to what this thread really is about-- namely the Code.<br /> <br /> As pointed out by Monica, the Code actually did exist in 1E, just with very different mechanics, so I suggest we go check how it worked here and see how it compares to the 2E playtest version.<br /> <br /> On a note, I noticed that the very first thing the appendix on the Code tells us is that Hunters <i>shouldn't</i> make morality rolls on regular basis:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply put, if hunters are held to the same Morality ratings as non-hunter humans, a Hunter: The Vigil game has the potential for the characters to degenerate into low-Morality lunatics in a very short span of time (and that may very well be a game you want to play). If characters are forced to make degeneration rolls for killing a vampire, werewolf or other monster, as they would for killing an innocent human, a dedicated hunter cell is quickly going to find itself making degeneration rolls on a regular basis, and the chances are high that the Storyteller will be spending more time herding the derangement-swamped characters as they rampage across the game setting than actually running any sort of scenario. </div> </div> </div>But admittedly, the new Integrity system in Chronicles of Darkness makes it much easier to get success than with the old Morality one, and hunters now have the benefit of Touchstones, so you could argue it's not that much of a problem anymore. Plus Breaking Points, in contrast with the old degeneration rolls, can actually have a positive effect, since you get Beats from them. So moving on.<br /> <br /> So based on what I read, Hunters in 1E start out with the same morality system than regular humans (which makes sense, because, you know, they <i>are</i> regular humans, at least they start out as such), and the Code is an option allowing them to modify it so they will be able to kill monsters without suffering degeneration rolls/breaking point every five minutes. The book actually offers three alternative methods to help:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Code:</b> The Vigil changes a person. \u201cThe Code\u201d (below) details an alternative set of game rules that can be used to adapt a hunter\u2019s Morality away from the human standard and into a Vigil-specific Code over time. While this system has its own drawbacks (social penalties and hunt-specifi c derangements known as Tells), it works well with a kill-heavy game, allowing characters to continue their hunt long after the normal Morality system would have sent them spiraling into madness. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Monsters Don\u2019t Count:</b> As discussed earlier in the book, hunters may not identify superhuman monsters as human. Storytellers may take this perspective into consideration, ruling that assaulting or killing monsters doesn\u2019t count as a Morality sin at all, and not requiring hunters to make any sort of Morality degeneration roll for actions taken against a monstrous foe. This ruling skews the Morality scale in a major way, and Storytellers who utilize it should be cautioned that it lifts one of the major weights of consequence of hunter characters\u2019 actions, but may allow for a more \u201cheroic\u201d game. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>It\u2019s Not Like They\u2019re Really People:</b> Slightly less extreme than the Monster\u2019s Don\u2019t Count theme is the idea that, while taking a sinful action against a monster may be bad, it\u2019s nowhere near as morally damning as taking the same action against a normal human. This Morality variation gives characters bonus dice (+1 to +3 depending on how inhuman the monster is) whenever the player rolls for degeneration for an action related to that monster. A Storyteller might give a player a +1 bonus to a degeneration roll for an action taken against a seemingly human magic wielder, +2 for a sin against a humanoid lycanthrope, and +3 extra dice when making a roll for slaying a human who\u2019s already dead (vampire, ghost, Reanimated, zombie). </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Do Nothing:</b> The Vigil is a morally perilous journey, and holding strictly to the standard human Morality scale only emphasizes that danger. Appointing oneself judge, jury and executioner is a path fraught with risks \u2014 physically, emotionally and spiritually. By forgoing any of the options that soften these dangers, players may have the opportunity to address a broad variety of moral issues themselves: where do you draw the line between duty and obsession? How does the punisher avoid becoming as bad as the criminal? And, finally, when the body count rises, what separates the hunter from his prey? </div> </div> </div>As you can see, the players are given multiple alternatives depending on the type of hunter chronicle they want to play, which already is more open-minded compared to what we saw in the playtest, albeit admittedly more chaotic too.<br /> <br /> In 2E, the &quot;Do nothing&quot; no longer is much worth, since the new Integrity system allows you to customize what triggers a Breaking Point or what doesn't, and Hunter already have Inner Breaking Points seperate from this system anyway, while the &quot;It's Not Like They're Really People&quot; has been removed entirely.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the &quot;Monster Don't Count&quot; has been made integral to the system, albeit with some nuance it somewhat (you still get breaking points the first time you torture a monster for example). I would like to point out this is the option the book advises NOT to use, precisely because it means hunters can now slaughter monsters indiscriminately and face no consequences regarding their sanity. So already back then, the game was suggesting hunters should not be allowed to kill supernatural beings in mass without risking their Integrity in the process.<br /> <br /> Now let's focus on the actual Code, AKA Option number 1, in the 1E Book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mechanics of the Code are deceptively simple at heart. As a hunter progresses on her Vigil, her obsession with the hunt pushes her, at various points, to take actions that are a sin on the normal Morality code. At these times, called Trigger Points, the player may decide that her character\u2019s Morality changes, and one of the \u201csins\u201d associated with the normal human Morality rating is changed to an edict that applies directly to her particular Vigil. The original \u201csin\u201d is no longer a part of her Code; it is replaced by a new sin, just as limiting, but more specific to her experiences and goals. Further along in the Vigil, another Trigger Point may be reached, and another of the hunter\u2019s Morality sins might be replaced by a Vigil-specific mandate, gradually customizing the basic tenets of not only how she behaves, but also how she views the world around her. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a hunter to deviate from that common recognition in a single \u201csin\u201d is enough to start to crack the fa\u00e7ade of normalcy. [...] In terms of game mechanics, each deviation is represented by a cumulative -1 Social penalty (to a maximum -5 dice) when dealing with other mortals. Every time the hunter\u2019s Code shifts away from normal human Morality, interacting socially with other human beings becomes more diffi cult, until, at later stages, the hunter is likely to be viewed by nonhunters as a monster himself. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each shift also brings with it a crack in the hunter\u2019s own psyche \u2014 regardless of drive, a hunter is, at heart, human himself. Thus, the same obsession that drives him away from the rest of humanity also warps him internally. This damage is represented by the accumulation of hunt-related derangements. Each time a tenet of the hunter\u2019s Morality Code shifts away from the human norm, he automatically gains a derangement specifi cally suited to the shift in ethics that has occurred. These derangements, as detailed below, differ from standard derangements in that they manifest only in relation to the hunter\u2019s Vigil. </div> </div> </div>So, to summarize: in 1E, the Code essentially was a set of rules representing a Hunter gradually warping his own Morality code compared to most people's standards in an effort to cope with the horrible things hunting monsters makes him do on regular basis without losing too much of his Integrity. Which is done at the cost of alienating himself from normal humans (hence the social penalty) and damaging his own sanity.<br /> <br /> Now, I see how that system no longer works for 2E, seeing how the Chronicles of Darkness' new Integrity system makes morality something subjective and no longer goes with the idea humanity commonly accepts some values. But personally, I do distinguish a major theme in this Code-- that going around killing people, monsters or humans, is still bad, and while you can lessen its impact with these rules so your character won't become a NPC, it will <i>still</i> mess you up and alienate you from humanity.<br /> <br /> With all that said, I will let you guys judges. How do you think the 1E Code compares to the 2E one, and vice-versa?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T05:11:10-07:00","id":1155020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155017#post1155017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all that said, I will let you guys judges. How do you think the 1E Code compares to the 2E one, and vice-versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned before - to me, on general level, 2E playtest Code is fine - IF you still can modify it in personal life of each Hunter. Truth be told, hunters ARE doing what they do to answer the constant threat of supernatural. So 'instinctive' answer of all them SHOULD be to kill the threat. HOWEVER - at least some of them should be able to 'grow beyond it', just like most humans do not attack with weapons their enemies now, even if few thousands years ago it was common answer. Vigil may have the same source - i.e. Instinct to 'kill the beast' - but how to respondent to those stimuli should be each hunter individual matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T08:41:34-07:00","id":1155078,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Satchel, for your review of my example. Perhaps I should have been a bit more detailed with it, but I have a tendency to be a bit briefer in my ramblings when responding by phone.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I'm not saying that humanity should be seen as inherently inferior to supernatural creatures, or that hunters that feel that way should be seen as normal or healthy. I'm saying that since some hunters draw the line of what constitutes a person in different places, the mechanics of the Code should allow for that kind of adjustment instead of treating it as though those arguments between hunters about what constitutes a person are mere words hiding the fact that they all agree. I don't think that taking the merciful approach should make a character more likely to gain the Merciless Condition than someone who is merciless to begin with. I also think that breaking points should relate more to a hunter's world view on an individual basis, rather than having them be universal with the possible exception of one. If Mr. K says that all monsters are horrible and irredeemable creatures that need to die, he should be disturbed if he sees a monster engage in selfless acts, as he becomes haunted by the fear that maybe these creatures are people, and that he's been acting as a murderer rather than a protector. I want hunters to question their actions regardless of philosophy, and I want zealots of the cause to be in greater danger of losing themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:17:34-07:00","id":1155113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1154992#post1154992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">correction- Hunter had Slashers in it since its very beginning. See page 294 in the 1E core (sure, a more in depth look was given in Slasher's book, but the concept was there from the start)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks for the correction. I completely forgot about their mention there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately, I'm not saying that humanity should be seen as inherently inferior to supernatural creatures, or that hunters that feel that way should be seen as normal or healthy. I'm saying that since some hunters draw the line of what constitutes a person in different places, the mechanics of the Code should allow for that kind of adjustment instead of treating it as though those arguments between hunters about what constitutes a person are mere words hiding the fact that they all agree. I don't think that taking the merciful approach should make a character more likely to gain the Merciless Condition than someone who is merciless to begin with. I also think that breaking points should relate more to a hunter's world view on an individual basis, rather than having them be universal with the possible exception of one. If Mr. K says that all monsters are horrible and irredeemable creatures that need to die, he should be disturbed if he sees a monster engage in selfless acts, as he becomes haunted by the fear that maybe these creatures are people, and that he's been acting as a murderer rather than a protector. I want hunters to question their actions regardless of philosophy, and I want zealots of the cause to be in greater danger of losing themselves. </div> </div> </div>Its easier to say &quot;Its just an act&quot; if you see someone doing something good than it is to do so if it is something awful. &quot;Vampires don't have feelings. The 'Pacifist' we just met just has a different hunting tactic. One with less risk and less reward.&quot; Any time you see them do something good, it is obvious that those manipulative lying monsters being manipulative and lying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:58:17-07:00","id":1155171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155113#post1155113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, thanks for the correction. I completely forgot about their mention there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Its easier to say &quot;Its just an act&quot; if you see someone doing something good than it is to do so if it is something awful. &quot;Vampires don't have feelings. The 'Pacifist' we just met just has a different hunting tactic. One with less risk and less reward.&quot; Any time you see them do something good, it is obvious that those manipulative lying monsters being manipulative and lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the responding question is: &quot;And that train of thought is different from the justifications of racists, how?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:58:52-07:00","id":1155172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155113#post1155113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its easier to say &amp;quot;Its just an act&amp;quot; if you see someone doing something good than it is to do so if it is something awful. &amp;quot;Vampires don't have feelings. The 'Pacifist' we just met just has a different hunting tactic. One with less risk and less reward.&amp;quot; Any time you see them do something good, it is obvious that those manipulative lying monsters being manipulative and lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>All very fair points. A known werewolf volunteering at a soup kitchen is easily explained away as trying to display a respectable front while identifying future victims that might not be missed. But what about if it's not simply charity? What if the werewolf risks their life to save a human's? Hell, what if it's the hunter's life? What if the werewolf sacrifices their own life to save that of their self-proclaimed enemy? Shouldn't that screw with a zealous hunter's head just as much (or more) as another hunter who learns that their Nosferatu informant beat up a gang of skinheads that chose the wrong guy to attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T16:47:09-07:00","id":1155221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155171#post1155171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the responding question is: &quot;And that train of thought is different from the justifications of racists, how?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say that with any argument about any kind of justification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All very fair points. A known werewolf volunteering at a soup kitchen is easily explained away as trying to display a respectable front while identifying future victims that might not be missed. But what about if it's not simply charity? What if the werewolf risks their life to save a human's? Hell, what if it's the hunter's life? What if the werewolf sacrifices their own life to save that of their self-proclaimed enemy? Shouldn't that screw with a zealous hunter's head just as much (or more) as another hunter who learns that their Nosferatu informant beat up a gang of skinheads that chose the wrong guy to attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the situation. &quot;Of course the wolf took the bullet for that human. They just regenerate anyway, and that human's influence is valuable to it.&quot; &quot;Wow, lucky that mindless beast went into one of those rages and got itself killed making a distraction for us to get away. Good thing they are such dumb brutes right?&quot; (Naturally, still applies if there was no actual rage) or &quot;I never new those wolves were so territorial. They'll even rush other monsters they have no chance against! Good thing we got away...&quot; Etc etc.<br /> <br /> If they are all mindless monsters, then anything that looks like they are helping is either an attempt to manipulate you or part of their violent nature that just happens to fall on other targets. After all, if it was a Vampire instead of a Werewolf, the situation it &quot;saved&quot; him from could easily have been constructed by the creature in an attempt to gain a new ally. If a viper bites a lion that is trying to kill you, does that mean the viper is a friend? No, you just got lucky and the snake was in the right place at the right time.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T17:00:39-07:00","id":1155225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155078#post1155078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, I'm not saying that humanity should be seen as inherently inferior to supernatural creatures, or that hunters that feel that way should be seen as normal or healthy. I'm saying that since some hunters draw the line of what constitutes a person in different places, the mechanics of the Code should allow for that kind of adjustment instead of treating it as though those arguments between hunters about what constitutes a person are mere words hiding the fact that they all agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more about supernaturals being at a level inherently detrimental to humanity.<br /> <br /> A hunter would be ravaged by Lunacy by a werewolf even sacrificing itself to save them, for instance.<br /> <br /> But at a certain point you're not drawing a different line at what constitutes a person. You're deciding a monster is okay, while still being a monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that taking the merciful approach should make a character more likely to gain the Merciless Condition than someone who is merciless to begin with. </div> </div> </div>Merciless doesn't necessitate harmful. A merciful, low Integrity hunter might go out searching for monsters to 'save' for instance. Mechanically all it means is if you see evidence of the supernatural, you must follow up on it. You don't have to eliminate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think that breaking points should relate more to a hunter's world view on an individual basis, rather than having them be universal with the possible exception of one. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they already are. Even in the playtest you can tailor your own past experiences, which allow you to determine many of your 'the first time' Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Mr. K says that all monsters are horrible and irredeemable creatures that need to die, he should be disturbed if he sees a monster engage in selfless acts, as he becomes haunted by the fear that maybe these creatures are people, and that he's been acting as a murderer rather than a protector. I want hunters to question their actions regardless of philosophy, and I want zealots of the cause to be in greater danger of losing themselves. </div> </div> </div>That's a Breaking Point, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-02-2017, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T17:24:01-07:00","id":1155227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155221#post1155221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could say that with any argument about any kind of justification.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually. Any &quot;X are all alike&quot; justifications, sure, but that isn't even half of the justification catalog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155221#post1155221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the situation. &quot;Of course the wolf took the bullet for that human. They just regenerate anyway, and that human's influence is valuable to it.&quot; &quot;Wow, lucky that mindless beast went into one of those rages and got itself killed making a distraction for us to get away. Good thing they are such dumb brutes right?&quot; (Naturally, still applies if there was no actual rage) or &quot;I never new those wolves were so territorial. They'll even rush other monsters they have no chance against! Good thing we got away...&quot; Etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that sounds like some severe denial of reality there. Almost as if they had a few screws loose. Perhaps a mind hiding it its own idealized, black &amp; white world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155221#post1155221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are all mindless monsters, then anything that looks like they are helping is either an attempt to manipulate you or part of their violent nature that just happens to fall on other targets. After all, if it was a Vampire instead of a Werewolf, the situation it &quot;saved&quot; him from could easily have been constructed by the creature in an attempt to gain a new ally. If a viper bites a lion that is trying to kill you, does that mean the viper is a friend? No, you just got lucky and the snake was in the right place at the right time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that Hunter isn't going to last long thinking they are all &quot;mindless beasts&quot;.<br /> <br /> My point is, holding this worldview isn't remotely healthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T18:39:03-07:00","id":1155243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155171#post1155171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the responding question is: &amp;quot;And that train of thought is different from the justifications of racists, how?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a racist justification. Some Hunters are racist (specieist?) and I'm OK with that. I just don't like the idea that the default position when you stand up to oppression is that you start thinking like a racist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:43:16-07:00","id":1155272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155225#post1155225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merciless doesn't necessitate harmful. A merciful, low Integrity hunter might go out searching for monsters to 'save' for instance. Mechanically all it means is if you see evidence of the supernatural, you must follow up on it. You don't have to eliminate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the nearest thing to a pressure to eliminate monsters as a Merciless hunter is running out of new monsters to find cutting you off from sleep-based Willpower recovery, which doesn't prevent you from regaining Willpower through risking it or playing to your Anchors or (if you're an NPC) resolving Conditions. If you're already suffering from sleepless nights or broken dreams then you've barely gained an incentive at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155172#post1155172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All very fair points. [\u2026] But what about if it's not simply charity? [\u2026] Shouldn't that screw with a zealous hunter's head just as much (or more) as another hunter who learns that their Nosferatu informant beat up a gang of skinheads that chose the wrong guy to attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devil may quote Scripture and the gods play dice with the lives of men. A hunter who treats supernatural actors in general as a talkative set of iconography with widely varying degrees of not-having-her-best-interests-at-heart is not going to be especially shaken by one of them committing deeply to the supposed pretense of virtue unless she actually has doubts about whether driving the people around her to wrack and ruination like the monsters do is really all that bad.<br /> <br /> The problems a zealot runs into are the same as the fella who pals around with the monsters, but in reverse: The supernatural does not exist in a vacuum, and sooner or later you're going to run into human friends and supporters who're going to defend their werewolf protector in a way that you can't solve without some strain of breaking the Code. (This also happens with run-of-the-mill hostage-taking, but that's less of a direct reflection.) The problems a zealot runs into are that monsters in human skin spend an awful lot of their time connecting with humans and sometimes those humans get something out of the interaction that puts them in your way in a way that forces you to choose between the chase and the Code.<br /> <br /> Mister K isn't going to get unconnected killboxes full of innocent splicers forever, and he's also not going to have the luxury of prep and recovery periods every time. As with Mage, eventually you're going to hit a threshold where cascade failure is a real and present danger in your lifestyle, and by that point you either set up the necessary precautions or go down screaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T03:19:42-07:00","id":1155335,"title":"","content":"Just wondering, shouldn't it be much more logical to directly write things like &quot;discovering a friend or loved one is a monster&quot; directly as a Breaking point? That would actually trigger a shock but let enough opening that players don't feel forced to play as zealots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:21:38-07:00","id":1155402,"title":"","content":"Wow, this debate has almost singlehanded given me so much interest in Hunter. While this is a meta/okc discussion, I'd love to see it in game. Take Ashwood Abbey. If the Hunter Code really does just, theoretically, come down to Human vs Monster... I could see a lot of debates and gray areas. The Abbey follows the Code, clearly. But are they letting go of their humanity instead, relying on the Code like an addiction? Would your Hunter be okay with them? Would they stop an ashwood, even if it meant questioning whether you are better, or the same, or worse? Would you kill a Hunter who obeys the Code code but not their integrity? Would you kill a Hunter who obeys their humanity but not the code?<br /> <br /> Reversed, the Lucifuge shirks the code in favor of integrity. Despite sympathizing with monsters and risking the Code and their understanding of the Most Dangerous Game, the biggest difference between a Lucifuge and the Children of the Devil is that the Lucifuge holds into their humanitu, code be Damned, while a true son of Satan cares nothing of either but could take it either way.<br /> <br /> LIKE RISKING WILLPOWER. It looks a lot like deliberately risking Integrity is now a part of Hunter, and the Y splats are differentiated by what parts of innate human integrity vs the Code they follow. Would you murder a human who was Ashwood? Would you forgive them because they still hunt monsters? Are either of you the same anymore? Are both of you monsters, holding up the Vigil' s candle from outside?<br /> <br /> I would agree that I think that there should be more than one &quot;breaking point&quot; that you can change, I'd also suggest you should be able to change innate ones too. Id lovd it if it was unlimited, but escalating, exponential. Change one and you're iffy. Change two and you're weird. Change three, good luck convincing hunters you are human. Change five and prepare to be hunted like Dracula.<br /> And every kind of hunter blurs the line between you and the monsters, and every situation is still a risk and reward question. If my Hunter feels confident in killing an asswood, it's a risk not because the line is clearly defined between man and monster, but because huntehunters justify their lives on black and white when the world is gray. I would expect an asswood would roll for Integrity as often as a Lucifuge, just for wholly different reasons (remdmber, the human side of Hunter integrity is still a little human, so &quot;My first time getting high on V&quot; would still be a breaking point for humans, even if not for the Code.)<br /> <br /> And sadly, the extreme sides of being a Hunter rather than a well adjusted mortal do make sense. MR. killer could maybe stay a Hunter, and sane, because he compartmentalizes things. That won't stop other hunters from risking their own beliefs and sanity to take him down (see Hermits and Waywards of owod hunter). On top of the Code, there are very human breaking points I truly believe we rent addressed in the pkaytest because that side has been playtested in every Cofd game. I still do see how Ms. Compassion could go insane with her risks to the code, because she a) bulwarks with human touchstones, b) if she isn't just playing around, she will invest in willpower attributes, c) have good modifiers via virtue and ST judgement for old childhood friendships or proof of the monster doing effort to being good. But it's possible a human-serial-killer sympathizer who burns Eleven and young Louis the Vampire stays sane and Ms Compassion could go slasher, it's possible the other way is true because the Code isn't as ingrained as actual human integrity. While all Hunters use the Code to justify most of what they do, I truly believe beyond the playtest, there will be MORE human breaking points. And thus extremists towards the Code or Humanity will betray the other side of themselves, and more mentally balanced hunters will look at both askance.<br /> <br /> As much as the CofD has moved away from the OWoD, I think Compassion, Zeal, and Vision can still exist. They all risk their Integrity, though, just like they risk willpower. You put Faith in what you believe is right, and you roll the dice. Whether you roll it because you're obeying the code and denying what sounds morally right and human, or whether you're rolling the dice because you were obeyying your humanity and ignoring the code... It doesn't matter in the end. The sad fact is... Hunters are in fact a monster Splat. They don't see themselves that way, but unfortunately even compassionate Hunters can become slashers. Just like zealous Hunters can keep themselves from degrading into real monsters. Part of it is creating a carefully and demanding mindset, and part of it is literally risking your sanity every time you go out and do your job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 11-03-2017, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:59:44-07:00","id":1155417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155335#post1155335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering, shouldn't it be much more logical to directly write things like &quot;discovering a friend or loved one is a monster&quot; directly as a Breaking point? That would actually trigger a shock but let enough opening that players don't feel forced to play as zealots.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a series of questions when designing your potential Breaking Points in Chronicles. One is 'What is the most traumatic thing that has ever happened to your character.' Depending on how you answer, discovering your friend is or becomes a monster might not be traumatic. But it's always within your control.<br /> <br /> Please keep in mind the playtest's Breaking Points section was written for the playtest. It seems representative of the final version, but not a complete copy of it.<br /> <br /> With that said, I have to ask, along with the werewolf sacrificing its life situation, why this would have any bearing on it? Certainly it would be a surprise if you thought people were born a monster and found it to be true, but that's rarely the case to begin with. Deciding that one werewolf saved your life, so maybe other werewolves are like them, would be a wildly naive way to react, and likely lead to the death of the hunter. And whatever gameline they're playing, the changes one goes through when becoming a monster are generally considered monstrous. Would the fact that Maxwell was your friend let you ignore the fact that he's eating people now and enslaving others with his blood? Or that every month he and a bunch of his new friends go out and kill people and monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-03-2017, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:27:21-07:00","id":1155439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please keep in mind the playtest's Breaking Points section was written for the playtest. It seems representative of the final version, but not a complete copy of it. </div> </div> </div>I didn't realize that. Maybe it's not as bad as I thought it was, then. I assumed it was the full code for the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that said, I have to ask, along with the werewolf sacrificing its life situation, why this would have any bearing on it? Certainly it would be a surprise if you thought people were born a monster and found it to be true, but that's rarely the case to begin with. Deciding that one werewolf saved your life, so maybe other werewolves are like them, would be a wildly naive way to react, and likely lead to the death of the hunter. And whatever gameline they're playing, the changes one goes through when becoming a monster are generally considered monstrous. Would the fact that Maxwell was your friend let you ignore the fact that he's eating people now and enslaving others with his blood? Or that every month he and a bunch of his new friends go out and kill people and monsters? </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this whole debate is pointless. You can make arguments in both direction; someone who assumes there might be other good werewolves might end up naive, but one who tries to make up excuses is in denial. There are pro and cons for both cases, and since hunters don't think all the same anyway, they could go either direction and suffer a Breaking Point or not depending on the situation. I honestly don't think there is a right answer to this specific part. But the very fact we are debating about it shows it's more complex than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:49:56-07:00","id":1155445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155221#post1155221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the situation. &quot;Of course the wolf took the bullet for that human. They just regenerate anyway, and that human's influence is valuable to it.&quot; &quot;Wow, lucky that mindless beast went into one of those rages and got itself killed making a distraction for us to get away. Good thing they are such dumb brutes right?&quot; (Naturally, still applies if there was no actual rage) or &quot;I never new those wolves were so territorial. They'll even rush other monsters they have no chance against! Good thing we got away...&quot; Etc etc.<br /> <br /> If they are all mindless monsters, then anything that looks like they are helping is either an attempt to manipulate you or part of their violent nature that just happens to fall on other targets. After all, if it was a Vampire instead of a Werewolf, the situation it &quot;saved&quot; him from could easily have been constructed by the creature in an attempt to gain a new ally. If a viper bites a lion that is trying to kill you, does that mean the viper is a friend? No, you just got lucky and the snake was in the right place at the right time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It absolutely depends on the situation. I just think that there are (or at least should be) situations that cause even a zealous hunter to think twice. &quot;Wow, lucky that mindless beast went into one of those rages and got itself killed making a distraction for us to get away. Good thing they are such dumb brutes, right?&quot; is a great example, but it becomes more complicated if they're following that line with a &quot;Kind of weird how it seemed to be yelling 'Run! I'll hold them off as long as I can!', though.&quot; At that point, it takes some mental gymnastics to completely dismiss the possibility that the werewolf knowingly and deliberately sacrificed itself. It's not impossible of course, but I still think that it should be unsettling enough that it forces them to question themselves. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155417#post1155417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With that said, I have to ask, along with the werewolf sacrificing its life situation, why this would have any bearing on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>My purpose with the werewolf sacrificing its life situation was purely to point out that it should be possible to shake someone's faith that the monsters are entirely evil, irredeemable bastards. If one werewolf dies for a human, the hunter's reaction shouldn't be a &quot;Heh. I guess there was actually one exception to the 'All werewolves are evil man-eating bastards' rule. Clearly that was the only one that ever has or ever would exist, though.&quot; That said, the fact that werewolves are dangerous is still a valid reason to keep hunting them. They might see werewolves as tragic figures at that point (&quot;Yeah, I know it's not your fault. I'm sorry, but I still need to put the good of the community first. I wish there was another way.&quot;), but they'd still do the job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155272#post1155272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the nearest thing to a pressure to eliminate monsters as a Merciless hunter is running out of new monsters to find cutting you off from sleep-based Willpower recovery, which doesn't prevent you from regaining Willpower through risking it or playing to your Anchors or (if you're an NPC) resolving Conditions. If you're already suffering from sleepless nights or broken dreams then you've barely gained an incentive at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155272#post1155272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problems a zealot runs into are the same as the fella who pals around with the monsters, but in reverse: The supernatural does not exist in a vacuum, and sooner or later you're going to run into human friends and supporters who're going to defend their werewolf protector in a way that you can't solve without some strain of breaking the Code. (This also happens with run-of-the-mill hostage-taking, but that's less of a direct reflection.) The problems a zealot runs into are that monsters in human skin spend an awful lot of their time connecting with humans and sometimes those humans get something out of the interaction that puts them in your way in a way that forces you to choose between the chase and the Code.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very good point, too. In the case of monsters that are legitimately doing good in the world despite it all, they would likely have numerous people (in the know or not) that would stand up to try and defend their buddy, and a hunter that tries to stop another from killing their Nosferatu informant will likely cause breaking points for both hunters. It also occurs to me that I've been a bit unfair about the breaking points in general, as the document even said that it didn't matter whether they thought they were doing the right thing or not. I've been interpreting that as an &quot;Oh my God, what have I done?&quot; moment, but while that may be the case for some, others may be shaken by it for other reasons. If the Nosferatu informant beats up the gang of skinheads that attacked him, the hunter's breaking point and potential Integrity loss may reflect more of a &quot;How can such things still happen in a supposedly enlightened society?&quot; reaction. Of course, that doesn't explain why that would only happen to them if their informant was a supernatural creature rather than something like a rogue Cheiron Group agent, but it's still a point I need to consider. A friend of mine even pointed out that the merciful hunter descending into low Integrity and even slasherhood doesn't mean that they've started picking school children off the street for victims. A merciful hunter that descends into low Integrity because she can't handle sending murderers to jail to help the ghosts of their victims might not come to the conclusion that she's been wrong to help the ghosts, but rather that the legal system doesn't punish them enough.This doesn't change my position in the debate, but I do acknowledge that if I'm going to call for nuance in the system, I need to acknowledge that which already exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155272#post1155272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mister K isn't going to get unconnected killboxes full of innocent splicers forever,</div> </div> </div> </div>I laughed so hard at this comment! Thank you, Satchel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:18:21-07:00","id":1155457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155243#post1155243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a racist justification. Some Hunters are racist (specieist?) and I'm OK with that. I just don't like the idea that the default position when you stand up to oppression is that you start thinking like a racist.</div> </div> </div> </div>My ability to read this is some serendipitous failure of blocking.<br /> <br /> Anyways, and that would be fine if this was a game about fighting oppression.<br /> <br /> It's not. It's a game about hunting monsters. You can dress it up however you want, and you might even actually fight some oppression on the way. If you are really thinking about it and being careful, you really could. But the game is about hunting monsters, and that means you characters are always, on some level, discriminatory. It might be more like &quot;I'm not racist towards black people, but-&quot; style discrimination instead of Ku Klux Klan style discrimination, but in the end, you hunt monsters, and you do it because they just aren't people like you are.<br /> <br /> Integrity is not Morality. Hunters are not (intrinsically) heroes. These are things that must be sought after, not given freely.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'll give a straight 1st ED vs 2nd ED The Code thought later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-03-2017, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:19:47-07:00","id":1155478,"title":"","content":"So, 1st Edition Code versus 2nd Edition Code.<br /> <br /> Perfectly honest, I hated The Code in First Edition back when I first read it and ran my game (Which, as an ironic twist for this conversation, ended up with the group being more like a team of negotiators between monstrous factions). I felt like it was an attempt to paper up the conflict with Morality, which at the time was a major thing for me-that the game had consequences for not being a good person was hella awesome for me, and the Code kind of took away that struggle. I still kind of feel that way about it now, even though I have a better context on what Morality was trying to be and the various ways it was broken as well as less of an inclination towards ease as concerns morals and ethics. And honestly, I wouldn't use it now. I would rather just let people deal with their morality.<br /> <br /> Second Edition Code though? It cements a lot of what's going on with Hunter and it's conflicts, particularly as it now incarnates in Second Edition. Since Integrity represents how well you have held up to psychological and emotional stresses, it suddenly makes a lot more sense for there <i>to</i> be some kind of 'papering up' mechanic, a way of numbing yourself to the horrors you subject yourself. I like that it <i>does</i> create a hard line between monsters and humans and places hunters firmly in some shade of human supremacist, and I do like that that complicates both times where they are gainly employing the supernatural or having some kind of work relationship with monsters <i>and</i> where the groups are softer and less typical hunters, because I think that creates a thematically more consistent game alongside some really hard hitting questions and dynamics to play with, as it forces confrontation with some of our easiest dark instincts in othering people and justifying our actions, particularly given that, yeah, sometimes there are plenty of surrounding reasons that are justified. That alongside the Conditions you pick up with sliding Integrity make the stresses of the game that much more potent, much more character centered, and dynamic in question. I like that it implies that there is always <i>some </i>blood on your hands, even with your best intentions, and the ways you own or discard that creates intensely personal stories.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I, uh. I'm strongly in opposition to the crowd who has a problem. My Hunters are monsters now, and that only makes them fuller and more deeply human to me, and it makes any effort I spend trying to be a good guy in this games <i>way more interesting and fulfilling.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:28:31-07:00","id":1155481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not. It's a game about hunting monsters. You can dress it up however you want, and you might even actually fight some oppression on the way. If you are really thinking about it and being careful, you really could. But the game is about hunting monsters, and that means you characters are always, on some level, discriminatory. It might be more like &quot;I'm not racist towards black people, but-&quot; style discrimination instead of Ku Klux Klan style discrimination, but in the end, you hunt monsters, and you do it because they just aren't people like you are. </div> </div> </div>As has been mentioned previously in the debate, this book has a VERY large definition of what &quot;Hunter&quot; means. The Union, for example, hunts supernatural and regular criminals with very little discrimination, because in their opinion, there is very little difference between a vampire sucking the life from the population and a crime lord getting richer by ruining the life of people around. The Promethean Brotherhood doesn't see difference between Tier-3 Hunters and monsters when it comes to what they hunt, because their criterial for a quarry is &quot;something with powers I can steal&quot;. VASCU hunts Slashers on the basis that they are criminals in the eyes of the American government, NOT that they are supernatural beings. And Network Zero &quot;hunt&quot; the monsters by filming them, because their reason for hunting is that they are trying to prove the existence of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> I am sorry to repeat myself, but in my personal opinion you<i> really</i> can't summarize the concept of hunter in this book to &quot;fight and kill monsters to protect humanity&quot; or &quot;consider monsters as inferior to/different than humans&quot;. Which is why I disapprove of the Code as it is on this playtest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second Edition Code though? It cements a lot of what's going on with Hunter and it's conflicts, particularly as it now incarnates in Second Edition. Since Integrity represents how well you have held up to psychological and emotional stresses, it suddenly makes a lot more sense for there <i>to</i> be some kind of 'papering up' mechanic, a way of numbing yourself to the horrors you subject yourself. I like that it <i>does</i> create a hard line between monsters and humans and places hunters firmly in some shade of human supremacist, and I do like that that complicates both times where they are gainly employing the supernatural or having some kind of work relationship with monsters <i>and</i> where the groups are softer and less typical hunters, because I think that creates a thematically more consistent game alongside some really hard hitting questions and dynamics to play with, as it forces confrontation with some of our easiest dark instincts in othering people and justifying our actions, particularly given that, yeah, sometimes there are plenty of surrounding reasons that are justified. That alongside the Conditions you pick up with sliding Integrity make the stresses of the game that much more potent, much more character centered, and dynamic in question. I like that it implies that there is always <i>some </i>blood on your hands, even with your best intentions, and the ways you own or discard that creates intensely personal stories.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I, uh. I'm strongly in opposition to the crowd who has a problem. My Hunters are monsters now, and that only makes them fuller and more deeply human to me, and it makes any effort I spend trying to be a good guy in this games <i>way more interesting and fulfilling.</i> </div> </div> </div>Happy for you if you like your Hunters as human supremacists, because I <i>most definitely don't</i>. But I think I made that clear by now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:33:56-07:00","id":1155483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155481#post1155481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As has been mentioned previously in the debate, this book has a VERY large definition of what &quot;Hunter&quot; means. The Union, for example, hunts supernatural and regular criminals with very little discrimination, because in their opinion, there is very little difference between a vampire sucking the life from the population and a crime lord getting richer by ruining the life of people around. The Promethean Brotherhood doesn't see difference between Tier-3 Hunters and monsters when it comes to what they hunt, because their criterial for a quarry is &quot;something with powers I can steal&quot;. VASCU hunts Slashers on the basis that they are criminals in the eyes of the American government, NOT that they are supernatural beings. And Network Zero &quot;hunt&quot; the monsters by filming them, because their reason for hunting is that they are trying to prove the existence of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> I am sorry to repeat myself, but in my personal opinion you<i> really</i> can't summarize the concept of hunter in this book to &quot;fight and kill monsters to protect humanity&quot; or &quot;consider monsters as inferior to/different than humans&quot;. Which is why I disapprove of the Code as it is on this playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can think that, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:46:09-07:00","id":1155489,"title":"","content":"True, but again, it's a fact this code doesn't work for some of these groups. And when a Code supposed to be followed by every single character contradicts the ethics/modus operanti of half the playable factions, you got a problem.<br /> <br /> Though again, if that's just for the playtest and the final Code is different, I'll be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:50:31-07:00","id":1155491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155457#post1155457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, and that would be fine if this was a game about fighting oppression.</div> </div> </div> </div> What definition of oppression are you using?<br /> <br /> I'm using &quot;<a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/oppression\" target=\"_blank\">the exercise of authority or power in a burdensome, cruel, or unjust manner.</a>&quot; which covers any case where a monster uses their supernatural power to prey or feed upon humanity. So any Hunter who's Vigil is about protecting people from monstrous predation is fighting oppression.<br /> <br /> Hunter isn't <i>only</i> a game about fighting oppression, but it certainly includes fighting oppression as a major element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155457#post1155457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the game is about hunting monsters, and that means you characters are always, on some level, discriminatory. It might be more like &quot;I'm not racist towards black people, but-&quot; style discrimination instead of Ku Klux Klan style discrimination,</div> </div> </div> </div> Baring edge cases like VASCU or a Cell of police officers who treat mortal and supernatural criminals roughly the same, I concede the point. Even when a Cell makes a point of only Hunting monsters when they have proof of wrongdoing, they're still treating monsters differently from the equally dangerous humans who they leave to the police.<br /> <br /> However that doesn't mean there isn't massive room for improvement. Here's the key phrase from the Call a Spade a Spade sidebar: &quot;He might want to view the cooperative vampire as a person&quot;. Once you start thinking of <i>them</i> as not even people you've gone way beyond &quot;I'm not racist but&quot;, you've gone way beyond Jim Crow and Separate But Equal. You're somewhere on the level of Nazi death camps, which should be presented as the tail end of hunter discrimination rather than the base case.<br /> <br /> Basically. Some amount of discrimination is inevitable but there's still room for improvement. The presentation could certainly be dialed back significantly. For example, rather than saying killing Monsters never causes a breaking point you could say that killing an innocent monster is a breaking point but a guilty one is not and contrast that to humans where killing is always a breaking point for a Hunter who isn't rapidly approaching Slasherdom. You could replace the Spade a Spade sidebar with a new sidebar that says the Code as presented is optimized for certain gameplay considerations and is not supposed to imply that a Hunter would automatically be ok with killing people who haven't hurt anyone just because they have supernatural power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155457#post1155457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity is not Morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity is not Morality. However the call a spade a spade sidebar makes statements about how Hunters think, and those thought patterns can be judged for their morality.<br /> <br /> And once you look at what it's saying about a Hunter's morality, I think the results clash with the intended themes of Hunter. Defending your community or humanity as a whole from harm was the single most common motivation among 1E Hunter groups. I really doubt anyone on the writing team wants to say doing that, fighting oppression, directly makes you think like a Nazi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:00:24-07:00","id":1155493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155491#post1155491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Defending your community or humanity as a whole from harm was the single most common motivation among 1E Hunter groups. I really doubt anyone on the writing team wants to say doing that, fighting oppression, directly makes you think like a Nazi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there needs to be something that makes Hunters (who actively prepare for and go out to fight monsters) different from Mortals that happen to deal with a monster when it sets up shop in their community. I do think the content of the playtest as written is problematic (if even just from a reactionary stance), but I think that there needs to be a clear delineation between regular mortals and Hunters. Moreso in 2e then there was in 1e due to the inclusion of so many Merits (Supernatural, MCI, and MicroTemplates) that make the old line between the two more muddied.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:12:38-07:00","id":1155497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155493#post1155493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there needs to be something that makes Hunters (who actively prepare for and go out to fight monsters) different from Mortals that happen to deal with a monster when it sets up shop in their community. I do think the content of the playtest as written is problematic (if even just from a reactionary stance), but I think that there needs to be a clear delineation between regular mortals and Hunters. Moreso in 2e then there was in 1e due to the inclusion of so many Merits (Supernatural, MCI, and MicroTemplates) that make the old line between the two more muddied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty clear it's meant to be the Code. Hunters dedicate their lives to the Code and change their entire psyche to deal with it. A regular mortal who occasionally deals with the supernatural is just treated like a regular mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155445#post1155445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My purpose with the werewolf sacrificing its life situation was purely to point out that it should be possible to shake someone's faith that the monsters are entirely evil, irredeemable bastards.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Code doesn't say monsters are 'entirely evil, irredeemable bastards,' it's just that they don't belong. And they don't. Werewolf specifically is a great example of that, their world is gone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If one werewolf dies for a human, the hunter's reaction shouldn't be a &quot;Heh. I guess there was actually one exception to the 'All werewolves are evil man-eating bastards' rule. Clearly that was the only one that ever has or ever would exist, though.&quot; That said, the fact that werewolves are dangerous is still a valid reason to keep hunting them. They might see werewolves as tragic figures at that point (&quot;Yeah, I know it's not your fault. I'm sorry, but I still need to put the good of the community first. I wish there was another way.&quot;), but they'd still do the job. </div> </div> </div>A hunter can see things that way. But does that mean when the next werewolf comes by and starts killing their cell they're going to shrug and say, 'Well, he'll sacrifice himself for me when it's important.' The Code doesn't say you can't see a monster as a 'good monster' but that doesn't make them people. If you really want there's probably an option to change your Code to allow for that, but they're still likely considered a monster.<br /> <br /> 'When the Code gets in the way of empathy for the plight of a creature that had no choice in becoming what it is, or one that\u2019s trying its best not to harm anybody, it forces a hunter to confront the consequences of the Vigil he swore to uphold.'<br /> <br /> It's explicitly called out as something that can happen. 'Why am I doing this? Maybe they aren't so bad. Maybe I shouldn't be part of this group of killers.' It's not blocking off character options.<br /> <br /> And then there's the other problem with your example. 'The only good werewolf is one who died for me,' is a ridiculously high bar, especially because this 'redemption' only comes in death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-03-2017, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:13:18-07:00","id":1155498,"title":"","content":"Look, I kinda feel like we are running in circles here, so I have a suggestion. How about we list all the Code-related Breaking points from the playtests here, and then see how each of them works for the various Compacts and Conspiracies? If it turns out they aren't as much a problem as Raven and I think, I will concede.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that there needs to be something that makes Hunters (who actively prepare for and go out to fight monsters) different from Mortals that happen to deal with a monster when it sets up shop in their community. I do think the content of the playtest as written is problematic (if even just from a reactionary stance), but I think that there needs to be a clear delineation between regular mortals and Hunters. Moreso in 2e then there was in 1e due to the inclusion of so many Merits (Supernatural, MCI, and MicroTemplates) that make the old line between the two more muddied. </div> </div> </div>I understand your point of view, but personally I disagree. I feel like drawing a line kinda misses the point of the gameline, since it's <b>supposed to be</b> about humans dealing with the supernatural. But I will concede this is an understandable opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:19:53-07:00","id":1155501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155498#post1155498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I kinda feel like we are running in circles here, so I have a suggestion. How about we list all the Code-related Breaking points from the playtests here, and then see how each of them works for the various Compacts and Conspiracies? If it turns out they aren't as much a problem as Raven and I think, I will concede.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... I think that exercise has merit. But a huge part of my issue is with the Spade Sidebar and not the breaking points themselves.<br /> <br /> Just to get the ball rolling. Network Zero has issues with the following elements:<ul><li>Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural - self evident.</li> <li>Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - VALKARIE has been portrayed as Net0's enemy. So an exemption for them makes sense.</li> <li>Causing significant harm to a person. Net0 have a strong X-Files conspiracy theorist anti-establishment streak. So exposing a corrupt politician online and getting him arrested (is that what's meant by &quot;significant harm&quot;? I'd assume so) seems fitting to me. I can't see Net0 killing humans, but doing an expose, I could see that.</li> </ul>All in all, the code is not too bad for Net0 but it still requires two modifications in my opinion and the limit is one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155493#post1155493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there needs to be something that makes Hunters (who actively prepare for and go out to fight monsters) different from Mortals that happen to deal with a monster when it sets up shop in their community.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you said it yourself: The difference is proactivity. A Mortal will deal with a monster if they're forced too. But if you're actively looking for trouble or training so you're ready if a monster shows up you're a Hunter. I mean &quot;deal with a monster when it sets up shop in their community&quot; is The Union in a single sentence.<br /> <br /> Admittedly most Hunters will have more differences than just reactive/proactive. But IMO being proactive is the minimum you need to distinguish between a mortal and a Hunter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155478#post1155478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as it forces confrontation with some of our easiest dark instincts in othering people and justifying our actions, particularly given that, yeah, sometimes there are plenty of surrounding reasons that are justified.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have several thoughts on this point:<br /> 1. Games that explore themes about othering and justifications but use monster's who're hardwired to prey on people and cause suffering as the stand in for the quickly other go into thematically weird and often incoherent territory. You either end up ignoring the parallel because there's no Always Chaotic Evil monsters in real life so there's no real reason to compare the fiction to reality, or the game ends up implying or skirting dangerously close to implying that othering is actually justified because the other really as bad as racists claim. This becomes especially bad when the PCs stand in for full on Nazi racists, not just &quot;I'm not racist but&quot; racists.<br /> <br /> 2. The presentation as written is actually very bad at forcing confrontation with our darkest instincts since it presents a single Code, and single hunter mindset in the Spade Sidebar. A far better way to force confrontation would be to encourage every player to modify their character's Code, at least to some extent, and present a verity of different opinions for players to consider; all to maximize the amount of time they spend thinking of it.<br /> <br /> 3. We already have Heroes to explore the niche where monster hunters are as monstrous as the monsters themselves, and whether or not it's intentional a lot of people saw strong themes about othering in Heroes. Why do Heroes twice rather than explore something different? Or at least explore many different perspectives of which a Hero like perspective is part but not the whole.<br /> <br /> 4. The Hunter core had 12 different groups, and many more were written later. Each had different personalities, ideologies, goals and methods. I can't see one theme working for all of them, nor can I see why you'd want to tie them all into one theme rather than explore many different themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155497#post1155497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Code doesn't say monsters are 'entirely evil, irredeemable bastards,'</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the impression that it does from the Call a Spade a Spade sidebar. It doesn't outright say &quot;evil&quot; but dehumanizing requires demonizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-03-2017, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:33:09-07:00","id":1155506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155501#post1155501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impression that it does from the Call a Spade a Spade sidebar. It doesn't outright say &quot;evil&quot; but dehumanizing requires demonizing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's dehumanizing because monsters are not more than superficially human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Edited for clarification. 11-03-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:34:11-07:00","id":1155508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155498#post1155498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I kinda feel like we are running in circles here, so I have a suggestion. How about we list all the Code-related Breaking points from the playtests here, and then see how each of them works for the various Compacts and Conspiracies? If it turns out they aren't as much a problem as Raven and I think, I will concede.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had thought about that before and I think it has three issues. One is what TheKingsRaven just said and I asked about earlier: The spade sidebar. Another is related to the sidebar and your comment here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155498#post1155498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand your point of view, but personally I disagree. I feel like drawing a line kinda misses the point of the gameline, since it's <b>supposed to be</b> about humans dealing with the supernatural. But I will concede this is an understandable opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not it works for a group is going to depend on what the person thinks the game SHOULD be about.<br /> <br /> The third is the thing I mentioned before and related to the second: It is in my opinion that just because a group was a Hunter Compact or Conspiracy in 1e doesn't mean it should be in 2e (although as previously said, the core ones will be) or that the presentation of them in 1e has to 100% match their presentation in 2e. It doesn't matter if The Code works for the section on them in 1e, it only matters if it works for the section on them in 2e.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155501#post1155501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you said it yourself: The difference is proactivity. A Mortal will deal with a monster if they're forced too. But if you're actively looking for trouble or training so you're ready if a monster shows up you're a Hunter. I mean &quot;deal with a monster when it sets up shop in their community&quot; is The Union in a single sentence.<br /> <br /> Admittedly most Hunters will have more differences than just reactive/proactive. But IMO being proactive is the minimum you need to distinguish between a mortal and a Hunter.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Enough to justify a difference Narratively sure, but not as a gameline. What you are describing is a bluebook supplement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155497#post1155497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's pretty clear it's meant to be the Code. Hunters dedicate their lives to the Code and change their entire psyche to deal with it. A regular mortal who occasionally deals with the supernatural is just treated like a regular mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was basically my point. There needs to be a line, and it seems the devs have decided The Code is it (or part of it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 11-03-2017, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:39:25-07:00","id":1155512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155508#post1155508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enough to justify a difference Narratively sure, but not as a gameline. What you are describing is a bluebook supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but I'm not trying to justify an entire gameline. Just a small part of it.<br /> <br /> Most Hunters will be way more different from the aforementioned mortal than just being proactive. But I think there's room in the setting for a minority of Hunter's who're just regular mortals that proactively defend their little community.<br /> <br /> There is definitely a niche in the WoD for regular people standing up for themselves against monsters. Why not put it in a corner of Hunter - I.E. one Compact among many - where it can benefit from systems like Tactics instead of a Blue Book supplement where it can't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-03-2017, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:42:17-07:00","id":1155513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155512#post1155512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, but I'm not trying to justify an entire gameline. Just a small part of it.<br /> <br /> Most Hunters are way more different from the aforementioned mortal than just being proactive. But I think there's room in the setting for a minority of Hunter's who're just regular mortals that proactively defend their little community.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't that just a bluebook game then though? Maybe with Risking Willpower and Tactics added in? Why does the Hunter book need to do that for you? you already can play that game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:45:03-07:00","id":1155514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had thought about that before and I think it has three issues. One is what TheKingsRaven just said and I asked about earlier: The spade sidebar. </div> </div> </div>Then we'll treat the sidebar as a separate problem after that. But establishing weither or not the Tenet actually cause problem will be a good first step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether or not it works for a group is going to depend on what the person thinks the game SHOULD be about. </div> </div> </div>Not really. It really is just a matter of seeing if it matches here or not here, no real subjectivity involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The third is the thing I mentioned before and related to the second: It is in my opinion that just because a group was a Hunter Compact or Conspiracy in 1e doesn't mean it should be in 2e (although as previously said, the core ones will be) or that the presentation of them in 1e has to 100% match their presentation in 2e. It doesn't matter if The Code works for the section on them in 1e, it only matters if it works for the section on them in 2e. </div> </div> </div>Already thought about that. Which is why I intend to compare the Code to the Core factions, and <i>only </i>the Core factions. No VASCU, no Promethean Conspiracy, no Faithful of Schulpae. I think it's only fair. As for the fact the core factions themselves might change, well... yeah, we can't do much about that, but I doubt they will change that much. And if they really remove things like the Lucifuge's more tolerant stand toward supernaturals or the Union's reactive attitude just so it'll match the Code, then frankly it's another problem entirely, since that means they just made all the groups much less interesting. But regardless, I think comparing to the 1e versions of the group is already a good exercise to judge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:05:12-07:00","id":1155527,"title":"","content":"Alright, here we go. Before I start, here are some rules I establish myself:<br /> <br /> 1) Only listing the Breaking Points related to the Code. The Innate ones have nothing to do with the debate.<br /> <br /> 2) Not listing the Modifiers. Based on what I was told sooner, they are supposed to be suggested, not obligatory.<br /> <br /> 3) For simplicity's sake, I suggest we only compare to the 12 core Compacts and Conspiracies. As much as I would like to use VASCU or the Promethean Brotherhood as examples again, we are not sure yet if they will be in 2E in any form (... I think).<br /> <br /> Now, here are the Breaking Points, or Tenets:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">* Causing significant harm to a person</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">* Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">* Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural<br /> * </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need<br /> * </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Killing a person<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Now, does someone want to start analyzing how this matches the 12 core factions, or should I start it myself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:46:47-07:00","id":1155547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) For simplicity's sake, I suggest we only compare to the 12 core Compacts and Conspiracies. As much as I would like to use VASCU or the Promethean Brotherhood as examples again, we are not sure yet if they will be in 2E in any form (... I think). </div> </div> </div>All current compacts/conspiracies will get something according to the Kickoff Opendev post. VASCU is confirmed to have a splat alongside the core book groups.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:57:06-07:00","id":1155553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All current compacts/conspiracies will get something according to the Kickoff Opendev post. VASCU is confirmed to have a splat alongside the core book groups. </div> </div> </div>Sweet, they are among my favourite; Thanks for the info^^<br /> <br /> Still, I think it's better to focus on the 12 core ones for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T15:12:24-07:00","id":1155558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155527#post1155527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Causing significant harm to a person<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil<br /> * Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need<br /> * Killing a person<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's roll with it - I start with my most loved/hated group - <b>Malleus Maleficarum </b>- here is analysis:<br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - MM is rumored to torture monsters, so... Maybe 'Yes'?<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Mostly aggresive priests wanting to exorcise monsters so - No<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - There are some tensions for the groups that are non-Catholic - I would rather point it as 'Yes'<br /> * Killing a person - Mostly 'No', at least as whole organisation<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - Mostly 'No' - MM wants to resolve problems as they know about them.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - Certiny 'No' - MAYBE on the seeing of Angel, but not sure.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Maybe 'Yes'? Their Benedictions are preys to Saints, but there are rumors for orginis from Angels.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Sometimes... But I would mark as 'No' for the organisation at large.<br /> <br /> <b>So it leaves us on maybe three, certinly only one Tenent need modification for MM members.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T15:34:12-07:00","id":1155564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155558#post1155558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's roll with it - I start with my most loved/hated group - <b>Malleus Maleficarum </b>- here is analysis:<br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - MM is rumored to torture monsters, so... Maybe 'Yes'?<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Mostly aggresive priests wanting to exorcise monsters so - No<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - There are some tensions for the groups that are non-Catholic - I would rather point it as 'Yes'<br /> * Killing a person - Mostly 'No', at least as whole organisation<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - Mostly 'No' - MM wants to resolve problems as they know about them.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - Certiny 'No' - MAYBE on the seeing of Angel, but not sure.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Maybe 'Yes'? Their Benedictions are preys to Saints, but there are rumors for orginis from Angels.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Sometimes... But I would mark as 'No' for the organisation at large.<br /> <br /> <b>So it leaves us on maybe three, certinly only one Tenent need modification for MM members.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Monsters aren't 'persons' by the 2e Code. So that isn't a problem.<br /> <br /> That leaves 'not helping other Hunters'?<br /> <br /> And maybe the source of their powers? Which I argue should be a Breaking Point when confronted with the posiiblity of their powers being given from a monster (assuming we don't get a clear cut, 'their powers come from god and that doesn't count' thing for them).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T15:38:51-07:00","id":1155566,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Wyrdhamster^^ I appreciate the enthousiasm. I'll take the Cheiron Group:<br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person: most certainly &quot;Yes&quot;. The Cheiron Group regularly experiments on its own agents and treats its employees about as well as Umbrella Corp from the Resident Evil game. Admittedly though, they might feel conflict about it and try to persuade them it's for the sake of science.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil: Definitely yes. They gladly send people on suicide missions or ruin people's lives for their own interest.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need: ... I am not sure for that. Though they would probably trigger a &quot;yes&quot; to every single more moral group, since what they do is pretty fucked up. As for themselves? I guess &quot;Yes&quot;, since they serve mostly their own interests.<br /> * Killing a person: ... ambiguous. They sure as hell don't mind harming people for their own goal, but direct killing probably is avoided, if just out of pragmatism, so I'd say &quot;No&quot;.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t: Yes. The group itself doesn't give a shit if people get hurt because they didn't do anything.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person: No. At worst they would want to preserve a specimen so they can dissect it later, but their very job involve considering monsters as stuff to collect, so they don't need to care about them as people, and it's probably discouraged.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source: <b>Yes</b>. They are literally putting monster parts in their body. Can hardly get more monstrous than that.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter: Possibly Yes. Again, they are mostly out for their own interest, and Compact and Conspiracies reveal they are willing to use lucifuge bodyparts. But admittedly that one is debatable, because they would probably avoid it out of pragmatism.<br /> <br /> <b>This leaves us with four certain Yes and possibly one more.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Monsters aren't 'persons' by the 2e Code. So that isn't a problem.<br /> <br /> That leaves 'not helping other Hunters'?<br /> <br /> And maybe the source of their powers? Which I argue should be a Breaking Point when confronted with the posiiblity of their powers being given from a monster (assuming we don't get a clear cut, 'their powers come from god and that doesn't count' thing for them). </div> </div> </div>Agreed for the &quot;monsters aren't person by the Code&quot;. We have to follow the rules for this exercise to work.<br /> <br /> As for the Benediction... I'll have to say &quot;up to the Storyteller&quot; for that one. Benediction MIGHT be from a monstrous source, but it's not obvious at first sight.<br /> <br /> Anyone wanna take the next one?^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T16:07:39-07:00","id":1155570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155566#post1155566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, Wyrdhamster^^ I appreciate the enthousiasm. I'll take the Cheiron Group:<br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person: most certainly &quot;Yes&quot;. The Cheiron Group regularly experiments on its own agents and treats its employees about as well as Umbrella Corp from the Resident Evil game. Admittedly though, they might feel conflict about it and try to persuade them it's for the sake of science.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil: Definitely yes. They gladly send people on suicide missions or ruin people's lives for their own interest.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need: ... I am not sure for that. Though they would probably trigger a &quot;yes&quot; to every single more moral group, since what they do is pretty fucked up. As for themselves? I guess &quot;Yes&quot;, since they serve mostly their own interests.<br /> * Killing a person: ... ambiguous. They sure as hell don't mind harming people for their own goal, but direct killing probably is avoided, if just out of pragmatism, so I'd say &quot;No&quot;.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t: Yes. The group itself doesn't give a shit if people get hurt because they didn't do anything.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person: No. At worst they would want to preserve a specimen so they can dissect it later, but their very job involve considering monsters as stuff to collect, so they don't need to care about them as people, and it's probably discouraged.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source: <b>Yes</b>. They are literally putting monster parts in their body. Can hardly get more monstrous than that.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter: Possibly Yes. Again, they are mostly out for their own interest, and Compact and Conspiracies reveal they are willing to use lucifuge bodyparts. But admittedly that one is debatable, because they would probably avoid it out of pragmatism.<br /> <br /> <b>This leaves us with four certain Yes and possibly one more.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling from the 1e Core writeup that the only Hunters in Cheiron are the Field Projects Division operatives, not the upper management, not even the scientists or other pieces of standard business stuff. And the 5 sample hunters are not really happy about being a field agent for Chieron, they just don't have a choice anymore (one of them isn't against hurting people, just against the control that is held over him).<br /> <br /> I think field agents for Chieron should have issues with The Code, they are barely on the same side as other Hunters when they are forced to do what their bosses say (who might secretly be part of an ancient cult, etc.).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155566#post1155566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the Benediction... I'll have to say &quot;up to the Storyteller&quot; for that one. Benediction MIGHT be from a monstrous source, but it's not obvious at first sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means it isn't monstrous by the rules:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Playtest</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">In system terms, the Code considers any creature that wields Dread Powers a monster \u2014 <b>as long as the hunters know it is such a creature</b> \u2014 as well as slashers and obviously inhuman beings</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. If it isn't a known monstrous source then it isn't one.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T16:17:20-07:00","id":1155572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get the feeling from the 1e Core writeup that the only Hunters in Cheiron are the Field Projects Division operatives, not the upper management, not even the scientists or other pieces of standard business stuff. And the 5 sample hunters are not really happy about being a field agent for Chieron, they just don't have a choice anymore (one of them isn't against hurting people, just against the control that is held over him).<br /> <br /> I think field agents for Chieron should have issues with The Code, they are barely on the same side as other Hunters when they are forced to do what their bosses say (who might secretly be part of an ancient cult, etc.). </div> </div> </div>I thought about that, but frankly that doesn't change much. Even if they aren't the upper management, they will still be encouraged to go against the Code because they are supposed to obey orders. And while I do agree it would make sense for some of them to have Breaking Points because of all the horrible stuff they are ordered to do, it's entirely possible some of the field agents the Cheiron Group recruits are sociopaths to begin with, or that some of them end up loosening their standards by modifying the Code as a way to cope with what they do. So they should still be allowed to modify more than one Tenet. And they are by far the group for who the social penalty makes the most sense, because they are second only to the Ashwood when it comes to being a sick hunter group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T16:22:33-07:00","id":1155573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155572#post1155572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they should still be allowed to modify more than one Tenet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, at present that doesn't seem like a bad change, although there may be a specific reason it was only one in the Playtest that we don't know about. There could be other mechanics that cover this, or conflict with it. Or it could be a matter of not providing too much complications to the system.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Or that allowing yourself to loosen your hold on The Code is how you slide down Integrity and become a Slasher.<br /> <br /> Also, being a sociopath doesn't mean that you can't choose to hold to The Code and that then violating that code is not still a hit to your Integrity. Sociopathy is not something they have attempted to model in ChroD and I don't think Integrity or The Code is the correct place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 11-03-2017, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T16:26:05-07:00","id":1155574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, at present that doesn't seem like a bad change, although there may be a specific reason it was only one in the Playtest that we don't know about. There could be other mechanics that cover this, or conflict with it. Or it could be a matter of not providing too much complications to the system. Or that allowing yourself to loosen your hold on The Code is how you slide down Integrity and become a Slasher. </div> </div> </div>Obviously. I didn't say otherwise. But that's beside the point of this exercise;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, being a sociopath doesn't mean that you can't choose to hold to The Code and that then violating that code is not still a hit to your Integrity. Sociopathy is not something they have attempted to model in ChroD and I don't think Integrity or The Code is the correct place to start. </div> </div> </div>That was an expression. If that really bothers you, replace &quot;sociopath&quot; by &quot;person who doesn't give a shit about the Code to begin with&quot; (which, you know, a sociopath would, because the whole Code boil down to &quot;protect humans against supernaturals&quot;). I am pretty sure people who never heard about the supernatural before being recruited and were forced into this have no reason to adopt this code. Please let's not expand on this or we'll be back to that argument that never ends.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, that's 2 groups done out of 12. Someone wanna take the next one?^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T16:41:07-07:00","id":1155578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155574#post1155574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, that's 2 groups done out of 12. Someone wanna take the next one?^^</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm re-reading the Lucifge entry from the 1e core now. If someone else posts a full list before I do then I will respond to them, otherwise I will post it myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T16:42:12-07:00","id":1155579,"title":"","content":"Fine by me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:04:25-07:00","id":1155586,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lucifuge<br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - No.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">* Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - No.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">* Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural - No.<br /> * </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - No<br /> * </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Killing a person - No<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - Maybe, but I think that is a good thing.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - maybe, this has issue with person/monster versus good/evil.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - yes, they will hit this every endowment, but again, I think that makes sense, they are using their powers for good but that doesn't mean they have to agree with the source<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Maybe, it could come up if the Hunter is being Evil while still being a Hunter.<br /> <br /> So that's two that would be hit semi-often for the consipracy that I think make sense for them to hit and 2 that are maybes based on the divide between good/evil and monster/hunter (or person or good/evil).</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:27:19-07:00","id":1155593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2 that are maybes based on the divide between good/evil and monster/hunter (or person or good/evil).</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Please clarify what you mean by this exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:28:58-07:00","id":1155595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155586#post1155586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucifuge<br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - No.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - No.<br /> * Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural - No.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - No<br /> * Killing a person - No<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - Maybe, but I think that is a good thing.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - maybe, this has issue with person/monster versus good/evil.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - yes, they will hit this every endowment, but again, I think that makes sense, they are using their powers for good but that doesn't mean they have to agree with the source<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Maybe, it could come up if the Hunter is being Evil while still being a Hunter.<br /> <br /> So that's two that would be hit semi-often for the consipracy that I think make sense for them to hit and 2 that are maybes based on the divide between good/evil and monster/hunter (or person or good/evil).</div> </div> </div> </div><b>ElvesofZion</b>, I do not think you are doing this exercises in honest heart. Here is what I think you miss in Lucifuge takes on Hunting:<br /> <br /> * Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural - It clearly should be 'Yes' - Lucifuge are all about embracing their demonic legacy. Just their day-to-day activity is to use those powers for 'doing good'. Omitting not showing other their powers will be <i>really</i> hard - and as such, a bit no sense.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - I would say 'Yes' - by embracing their demonic legacy, Lucifuge are clearly stating their are at least part monsters. And by doing their own thing - they are putted against 'autonomy' of a person. Well-being - that's probably not.<br /> <br /> I added at least 2 strong points on 'Yes' to your list then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:39:26-07:00","id":1155597,"title":"","content":"Please, please, let's not start pointing fingers at each other. Elves of Zion agreed to take part in the exercise, I feel it's the least we can do to be fair with him.<br /> <br /> I will admit I have to side a bit more with Elves of Zion here at least on the first point, sorry Wyrdhamster. Lucifuge willingly use their demonic powers, yes, but I still think they are to some extent trying to not embrace them too much - that's what makes them different from L'Enfant Diabolique, as well as the reason they have to make degeneration rolls when they get Exceptional Success in 1E. And they would still not want to harm people by exposing them to the supernatural, they are trying to do good after all, not traumatize humans.<br /> <br /> I do agree with you, Wyrd, about &quot;Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person&quot; should be yes, because the book puts a strong emphasis on the fact they acknowledge themselves as monsters and as such treat monsters as persons, but I wanna hear what exactly ElvesOfZion means by his good/evil part. He might have a reason to put that here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-03-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:51:13-07:00","id":1155601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155593#post1155593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please clarify what you mean by this exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that as written there is the potential for an issue since the Lucifuge have a stronger care about good versus evil then they do for human versus monster. I still said a maybe because I don't know that the two breaking points would come up regularly enough to be a 'problem for the conspiracy'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155595#post1155595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>ElvesofZion</b>, I do not think you are doing this exercises in honest heart. Here is what I think you miss in Lucifuge takes on Hunting:<br /> <br /> * Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural - It clearly should be 'Yes' - Lucifuge are all about embracing their demonic legacy. Just their day-to-day activity is to use those powers for 'doing good'. Omitting not showing other their powers will be <i>really</i> hard - and as such, a bit no sense.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - I would say 'Yes' - by embracing their demonic legacy, Lucifuge are clearly stating their are at least part monsters. And by doing their own thing - they are putted against 'autonomy' of a person. Well-being - that's probably not.<br /> <br /> I added at least 2 strong points on 'Yes' to your list then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am absolutely doing this in honest heart.<br /> <br /> * The lucifuge is not all about embracing thier heritage, they are about doing the most good they can and fighting Lucifer with the infernal powers they have been cursed with. Even if it was though, that has nothing to say on showing supernatural to people, at least not in their core write-up.<br /> <br /> * The Code says that Hunters never count as monsters, so their own well being doesnt count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 11-03-2017, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:56:45-07:00","id":1155604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I meant that as written there is the potential for an issue since the Lucifuge have a stronger care about good versus evil then they do for human versus monster. I still said a maybe because I don't know that the two breaking points would come up regularly enough to be a 'problem for the conspiracy </div> </div> </div>I think it would come up quite often given the setting, but I see your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am absolutely doing this in honest heart. </div> </div> </div>And I appreciate it^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T18:10:30-07:00","id":1155607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155604#post1155604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would come up quite often given the setting, but I see your point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I appreciate it^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the more I think about it, the more I think the situations where it would come up (for either breaking point) are again places I feel it is appropriate for them to have an issue questioning the correctness of their attitude, it would be places where they have to stop and say ' I know the monster says they are good, but will they always stay that way? And what does that say about me? If I do this too much am I really fighting evil (it does say that they feel that all monsters come from Satan even if an individual can fight being evil).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Fixing phone typos 11-03-2017, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T19:20:01-07:00","id":1155616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155558#post1155558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's roll with it - I start with my most loved/hated group - <b>Malleus Maleficarum </b>- here is analysis:</div> </div> </div> </div> The MM always struck me as having a very broad definition of &quot;witch&quot;. The Code says Endowed Hunters never count as Monsters, the MM says that all power comes from either God or the Devil, and they alone get their power from God. So any Endowed Hunter who's powers look magical (and doesn't have the Ghoul in Chief covering for them) would likely get on their bad side.<br /> <br /> So I'd say definitely a yes to causing harm to a person, killing a person. I'd also say that while a code that lets you kill mortals is definitely a fast track to Slasherdom, treating Endowed Hunters as monsters should be safer. It's just not Hunter if you can't have a Conspiracy vs Conspiracy war now and again.<br /> <br /> <u>Anyway: VALKARIE</u><br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - Yes: They've gone after other hunters before.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - I get the feeling they're a bit trigger happy with the big guns. But I'd say that should be a Breaking Point for them.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - Yes: more inter-hunter conflict.<br /> * Killing a person - Yes: more inter-hunter conflict.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - There's that whole thing about the beaurocracy surrounding Vampires, but perhaps that should be a breaking point regardless.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - No<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - IMO: Advanced Armory is not an obviously monstrous source.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - I'd say no. VALKARIE wont betray your trust, they'll shoot you in the front.<br /> <br /> So I'd say three at a minimum, all of which stem from the source VALKARIE has canonically fought rival Hunters. Which makes perfect sense. An armed group performing extra-judicial killings on American Soil or Endowed Russian Spies should get the government's attention, and if they're using supernatural tricks to do it then VALKARIE has jurisdiction. It doesn't matter that Elixirs are an Endowment, VALKARIE knows how to fight people with strange powers, most other government departments do not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Ascending Ones</u><br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - Yes: They sell drugs.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Yes. If you're going to negociate with vampires or beasts you have to compromise when it comes to feeding. Also the drugs.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - Yes: If they've negotiated a great peace that keeps their protectees safe and another hunter is about to destroy it by being a kill-em-all fanatic they Ascending Ones won't be helping them.<br /> * Killing a person - Probably. They must get into the occasional turf war with rival drug dealers. But it's likely a Breaking Point when someone dies.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - No. Protecting people is what they're all about.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - I could see it happen. They're diplomats so they might put a friend among the monsters first.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Yes. I think Elixirs count.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Maybe, realpolitik is a dirty game.<br /> <br /> So there's only one definite no there. It's all maybes or yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155513#post1155513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that just a bluebook game then though? Maybe with Risking Willpower and Tactics added in? Why does the Hunter book need to do that for you? you already can play that game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is a game about playing a monster hunter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hunter's greatest strength has always been it's diversity, the fact that it always supported so many different kinds of monster hunters. That diversity is what I want to see preserved in 2ED and Hunter's who're pretty much regular guys but proactively train for the day a monster rolls into town are part of that diversity.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the previous sentence described The Union.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T19:53:07-07:00","id":1155624,"title":"","content":"<b>I'll try the Ascending Ones:</b><br /> <br /> Causing significant harm to a person: They run drugs.<br /> <br /> Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil: They run drugs.<br /> <br /> Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural: I think they're ok there.<br /> <br /> Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need: Maybe? I can see KR's argument.<br /> <br /> Killing a person: They run drugs.<br /> <br /> Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t: They engage in diplomacy when they can, which entails leaving certain monsters alone if they think a deal has been struck - that leaves them vulnerable to this happening.<br /> <br /> Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person: I don't think their diplomacy extends to this.<br /> <br /> Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source: I'd say they're good here.<br /> <br /> Betraying a fellow hunter: According to their 1st Edition writeup, they think the Lucifuge should join their fellow monsters in Hell once they're no longer useful. But that has the dodge that once they're betraying, they don't consider the Lucifuge fellow hunters any more.<br /> <br /> <br /> So they're vulnerable to certain things happening against the Code, and directly violate it three times over - but for the same reason each time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>And the Loyalists of Thule:</b><br /> <br /> Causing significant harm to a person: Many of them have done this in the past and the Vigil is about making up for it; so I'd say they're ok.<br /> <br /> Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil: This is a risk - they're secretive to a fault, and careless secrets can cost lives as easily as careless talk.<br /> <br /> Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural: Everything about them makes this unlikely.<br /> <br /> Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need: Again, secretive enough that they'll sometimes do this.<br /> <br /> Killing a person: Do Nazis count? (Serious question, really - they do take time out of the Vigil to fight Nazis).<br /> <br /> Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t: Probably ok.<br /> <br /> Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person: Probably ok.<br /> <br /> Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source: Probably ok.<br /> <br /> Betraying a fellow hunter: Does obsessively keeping secrets from them count?<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> I see the point of a universalised Code - or <i>a</i> point to it, I don't know if it's the actual reason. The Integritype stat represents the psychological question no member of that species can ever get away from. How the Vigil affects you is that for Hunters. But Integrity can manage that largely on its own.<br /> <br /> And I like the way in the first edition that the Code functioned in a way as a hunter's z-splat. All things considered, I'd rather keep that.<br /> <br /> Or, take a leaf from Deviant and have two Integritypes: Integrity to represent holding onto the core of yourself, and Code, representing the question of &quot;are monsters people.&quot; And for the latter, perhaps structure it like Harmony, with &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;no&quot; marking the ends of the scale, and breaking points leading in both directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T21:06:06-07:00","id":1155642,"title":"","content":"Salient question for the exercise: How valuable are the High Integrity breaking points to this discussion considering their tacit irrelevance to the vast majority of active hunters doing active hunter things?<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, I wouldn't play a NetZero Army of Truth hardliner and blow any number of freebies on opting out of High Integrity breaking points that will go away the moment I go Vigilant when the cost is alienating even non-VALKYRIE hunters and picking up a Low Integrity breaking point in the process. I'd have better luck trading out betrayal for loyalty to the message or the compact for that kind of cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T03:56:33-07:00","id":1155686,"title":"","content":"A fair question. To me it's a matter of principal. That character clearly believes it's ok to expose mortals, so you should modify the code and alienate other Hunters. Anything less would be exploiting a loophole in the rules to avoid the logical consequences of his beliefs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155624#post1155624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[b]I'll try <br /> <b>And the Loyalists of Thule:</b></div> </div> </div> </div> don't forget that the loyalists standard recruitment method is blackmail. That's at least harming another, and maybe betraying a Hunter if they use it on Tier 1 hunters<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155624#post1155624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, take a leaf from Deviant and have two Integritypes: Integrity to represent holding onto the core of yourself, and Code, representing the question of &quot;are monsters people.&quot; And for the latter, perhaps structure it like Harmony, with &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;no&quot; marking the ends of the scale, and breaking points leading in both directions.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like this a lot.<br /> <br /> You could say that if your Code reaches one extreme you risk becoming a Slasher (monsters and people are the same hunt both) and at the other extreme you risk becoming something like a Hero (monsters are so bad collateral damage doesn't matter). Not a guarantee, if you don't kill anyone you can treat monsters just like humans and not become a slasher, but a risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-04-2017, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T05:31:18-07:00","id":1155701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155686#post1155686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say that if your Code reaches one extreme you risk becoming a Slasher (monsters and people are the same hunt both) and at the other extreme you risk becoming something like a Hero (monsters are so bad collateral damage doesn't matter). Not a guarantee, if you don't kill anyone you can treat monsters just like humans and not become a slasher, but a risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm... Low Integrity coupled with the &quot;Yes&quot; extreme of the Code does sound like a good slasher risk - you equate monsters with people, but in such a way as to do down people rather than raise up monsters. I usually define the Hero attitude as &quot;it doesn't matter whether the monster deserves to die, only that I deserve to kill it&quot; - and low Integrity coupled with &quot;No&quot;-end Code does fit that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T08:53:23-07:00","id":1155742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155686#post1155686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fair question. To me it's a matter of principal. That character clearly believes it's ok to expose mortals, so you should modify the code and alienate other Hunters. Anything less would be exploiting a loophole in the rules to avoid the logical consequences of his beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most hunters are more worried about the practical impact of exposing people to the supernatural in direct pursuit of the Vigil rather than its impact on their own level of comfort with what they do&quot; isn't exploiting a loophole any more than a Merciless hunter who's made his peace with murder is. Experience is going to make the average hunter recognize that other hunters generally knew what they were getting into when they resolved to keep the Vigil long-term, that they're often better-equipped to deal with monsters than average mortals, and that while it stings your heart a little to admit it, sometimes the monsters win in a straight fight and you have to prioritize survival over common cause. Those that are still genuinely deeply bothered by it can easily pick a tenor and target for their obsession or shut down until someone spots their inner conflict, but Vigilant hunters just try to avoid running into those decisions too often out of practical necessity.<br /> <br /> There's more than one way to blatantly expose people to the truth and it seems entirely suitable for membership in the Compact focused around recording and circulating media capturing the supernatural to have to still make you pick your priority if you're going to leverage it to maintain <i>High</i> Integrity instead of hanging out at the level where your instinctive paranoia kicks in at signs of supernatural danger.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think the Government is in on it and so is Big Pharma, so there's no need to step in and help the institutionally-backed conspiracy goons when a werewolf's got their back to a wall&quot; does not strike me as a reason to shift your Code compared to &quot;I have cameras everywhere but stopping people from getting hurt isn't as important as gathering evidence,&quot; nor does a blas\u00e9 attitude toward indirectly traumatizing mortals seem like something likely to arise out of institutional devotion \u2014 media capture of occult phenomena has a couple inherent buffers against being an outright and immediate breaking point trigger next to, say, bringing Roommate Steve along on your next recording session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:22:34-07:00","id":1155748,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you are saying. Are you saying that:<br /> <br /> * The Army of Truth's mission to force people to look at evidence of the supernatural won't trigger the exposure breaking point?<br /> * That it will trigger the exposure breaking point but you don't think the Army of Truth need to modify that part of the code?<br /> * That they have a reason to modify that part of the code but other issues take priority?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:16:28-07:00","id":1155770,"title":"","content":"Alright, for starter, I would like to thank you all for actively taking part in that exercise. The result is most interesting, and we already managed 6 groups out of 12. I am impressed.<br /> <br /> However, we have two alternative opinions of the Ascending Ones, so a tie-breaking might be needed. Here's my own opinion on the points where King Raven and Sunless Nick disagree:<br /> <br /> * Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural: I'd say no. As far as I know, nothing in their code or modus operanti contradicts this.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need: Maybe yes.<br /> *Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t: No. True, the diplomacy can lead to this, but the point of the negociation still is to ensure as little people as possible get harmed.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person: ... Not sure. Maybe yes, if they consider some humans deserve it. But I admit it's stretching it.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source: No. Whatever the Elixirs are, they aren't obviously monstrous in source, at least in my opinion. Some Elixirs <i>might</i> be, such as that one that turns you into a vampire for a short period of time in Nightstalker, but I don't think<i> some</i> Elixirs triggering Breaking points is enough justification to use your freebie.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter: maybe yes.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps^^<br /> <br /> Now for Satchel's question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Salient question for the exercise: How valuable are the High Integrity breaking points to this discussion considering their tacit irrelevance to the vast majority of active hunters doing active hunter things?<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, I wouldn't play a NetZero Army of Truth hardliner and blow any number of freebies on opting out of High Integrity breaking points that will go away the moment I go Vigilant when the cost is alienating even non-VALKYRIE hunters and picking up a Low Integrity breaking point in the process. I'd have better luck trading out betrayal for loyalty to the message or the compact for that kind of cost. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I still think they should count to some extent though, as some players might want to keep a high Integrity. How about we give half-value to every point from 10 to 7?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:27:36-07:00","id":1155779,"title":"","content":"Thinking a little more, maybe modifying high integrity breaking points should have less drawbacks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T21:18:50-07:00","id":1155940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155748#post1155748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you are saying. Are you saying that:<br /> <br /> * The Army of Truth's mission to force people to look at evidence of the supernatural won't trigger the exposure breaking point?<br /> * That it will trigger the exposure breaking point but you don't think the Army of Truth need to modify that part of the code?<br /> * That they have a reason to modify that part of the code but other issues take priority?</div> </div> </div> </div>That putting up a video of supernatural activity is not going to be enough by itself to warrant a breaking point in a casual viewer, that trading out a breaking point specifically has to happen in the <i>direct</i> pursuit of the Vigil and not as a thing you do after a hunt, and that the Network Zero portion of the trade-out section is probably not talking about the group's de facto core practice when it says they <i>tacitly encourage</i> blatant exposure.<br /> <br /> Also that the Army of Truth and other militant/extreme branches of hunter organizations are unlikely to maintain High Integrity during an extended stretch of hunting, and that the most militant faction of the rip-open-the-veil compact is probably going to have more egregious violations of the Code to inure themselves to like getting the hidden monster to reveal its killing form in front of a live audience and failing to prevent all casualties rather than the unexpected-failure-of-planning catch that mere exposure is there to tag onto.<br /> <br /> Unchallenged high Integrity isn't generally <i>for</i> mortal characters who are deeply committed to hardline supernatural-proximate lifestyles, particularly when the threshold for middling Integrity is one point below the starting character average. You're better off playing into the scale's default support structure if you're worried about losing a single point of Integrity from narratively-infrequent breaking points with no inherent penalties attached to them. <br /> <br /> It seems fairly clear that membership in a higher-tier group is supposed to help keep you from falling below Middling range rather than to hold you above it \u2014 these are groups that have committed to the cause, after all, and that implies a certain base level of Vigilance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T23:55:30-07:00","id":1155962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155940#post1155940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That putting up a video of supernatural activity is not going to be enough by itself to warrant a breaking point in a casual viewer, that trading out a breaking point specifically has to happen in the <i>direct</i> pursuit of the Vigil and not as a thing you do after a hunt</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you provide some evidence of that? I'm not seeing that interpretation in the text that we have been provided with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T00:30:25-07:00","id":1155964,"title":"","content":"I think Satchel's suggesting out that while seeing a tentacle beast swallow someone then spit them up mostly dissolved might rattle your understanding of the world, seeing it on TV might make you think you were watching <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0118956/\" target=\"_blank\">Deep Rising</a>.<br /> <br /> For a more mechanical backing, the Breaking Points are, 'First time personally encountering a particular type of supernatural trait or power,' and 'Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural,' which a video tape isn't (usually, at least, there are supernatural effects that can travel across media).<br /> <br /> The Army of Truth being the people who storm TV stations with shotguns so they can show their videos and steal nuclear weapons and vials of smallpox to potentially help their 'cause' doesn't really suggest a High Integrity group of people. In fact it strongly implies the Merciless Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-05-2017, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T00:39:35-07:00","id":1155965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155964#post1155964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Causing a person to suffer a breaking point from exposure to the supernatural,' which a video tape isn't (usually, at least, there are supernatural effects that can travel across media).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the breaking point isn't from some supernatural effect, just seeing supernatural things is meant to create breaking points in most people. The CofD rules say that seeing something &quot;that rattles his understanding of the world&quot; is one of the things which cause a breaking point, and the whole point of Network 0 is to show the rest of humanity that these entities exist and expand their understanding of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-05-2017, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T00:46:42-07:00","id":1155967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155965#post1155965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the breaking point isn't from some supernatural effect, just seeing supernatural things is meant to create breaking points in most people. The CofD rules say that seeing something &quot;that rattles his understanding of the world&quot; is one of the things which cause a breaking point, and the whole point of Network 0 is to show the rest of humanity that these entities exist and expand their understanding of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you would need more to rattle someone's understanding of the world than to show a video, or the horror industry in Chronicles is a disaster and Network Zero would have succeeded the moment YouTube went up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T01:02:56-07:00","id":1155969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155967#post1155967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe you would need more to rattle someone's understanding of the world than to show a video, or the horror industry in Chronicles is a disaster and Network Zero would have succeeded the moment YouTube went up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the horror industry be a disaster? The bit I quoted was not just &quot;rattle someone&quot;. <br /> <br /> Also if you dismiss everything network zero does then your basically saying they shouldn't exist. Why do other groups get to do their purpose, but apparently Network Zero never achieves anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T01:32:53-07:00","id":1155971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155969#post1155969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the horror industry be a disaster? The bit I quoted was not just &quot;rattle someone&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because every horror movie and quite a few thrillers would be a public health disaster, with people leaving movie theaters in fugue states or driven to madness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also if you dismiss everything network zero does then your basically saying they shouldn't exist. Why do other groups get to do their purpose, but apparently Network Zero never achieves anything? </div> </div> </div>Implying they haven't succeeded in all their goals doesn't mean I'm dismissing 'everything network zero does,' and I was not basically saying any such thing. They get the word out, some people believe it, show their own and sign up, but it's even called out as not the best method to do things, that's why the Pan Opticons started up, because it's a passive way of doing things that makes the truth more of an 'entertaining curiosity.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T01:37:57-07:00","id":1155972,"title":"","content":"Been trying to follow the discussions here, and... breaking points are experiences that shock people, right? If it doesn't shock you, it isn't a breaking point. And a recording of some event would be much less shocking than the real thing for most people, In other words, much less likely to register as a breaking point in the first place. Network Zero should be fine in that space.<br /> <br /> And even if it isn't... I dare say that the old principle of &quot;We're playing the monsters, as in, the guys morally grey at best&quot; still work here. Remember, <i>we aren't playing the Good Guys. </i>We're playing characters with some screwed up issues to one degree or another, who have the ability to good in an otherwise horrible world. Not everything the protagonist groups do have to be justified, nor are they justified in the first place. Why should hunters, Network Zero or not, be the exception?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T01:51:14-08:00","id":1155982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155971#post1155971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because every horror movie and quite a few thrillers would be a public health disaster, with people leaving movie theaters in fugue states or driven to madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it wouldn't.... as I already said simply rattling someone isn't the condition for a breakpoint. You're arguing against a point that no one has argued.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Implying they haven't succeeded in all their goals doesn't mean I'm dismissing 'everything network zero does,' and I was not basically saying any such thing. They get the word out, some people believe it, show their own and sign up, but it's even called out as not the best method to do things, that's why the Pan Opticons started up, because it's a passive way of doing things that makes the truth more of an 'entertaining curiosity.' </div> </div> </div>I didn't say all their goals, could you actually argue against things I'm saying rather than turning what I'm saying into a strawman?<br /> <br /> You were implying that they wouldn't be changing anyone's understanding of the world, despite the fact that is the thing they spend their entire vigil doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T02:59:23-08:00","id":1155986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155940#post1155940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That putting up a video of supernatural activity is not going to be enough by itself to warrant a breaking point in a casual viewer,</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the 2E Army of Truth should be updated to use strategies that trigger Breaking Points. <br /> <br /> If you're going to have militant Hunters dedicated to tearing down the Masquerade you should give them a strategy that works, at lest well enough to win some victories, those strategies will trigger Breaking Points. From what you say later in your post I think we agree on this.<br /> <br /> And if your core concept revolves directly around breaking a clause of the code you should modify it as a matter of principal regardless of how mechanically optimal it is.<br /> <br /> (Also, why did you pick the Army of Truth as an example of a group who trigger a high Integrity Code Breaking Point if you're going to turn around and say they don't)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155940#post1155940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and that the Network Zero portion of the trade-out section is probably not talking about the group's de facto core practice when it says they <i>tacitly encourage</i> blatant exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;tacitly&quot; is an odd word to use here. But what other clause in the code could it be referring too? State the actual breaking point you think it's referring to because right now it really looks like the document itself is saying I'm right about The Army of Truth modifying that part of The Code.<br /> <br /> (Perhaps &quot;tacitly&quot; means the Compact as a whole tacitly encourages exposure while the minority of members who comprise the Army of Truth are more explicit)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155940#post1155940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also that the Army of Truth and other militant/extreme branches of hunter organizations are unlikely to maintain High Integrity</div> </div> </div> </div> They probably won't. But as a matter of principal, if The Code says your core goal is a breaking point you modify that part of the code. Even if your Integrity is too low for it to matter mechanically.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155940#post1155940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> during an extended stretch of hunting, and that the most militant faction of the rip-open-the-veil compact is probably going to have more egregious violations of the Code to inure themselves to</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I and others argue for the ability to make multiple changes to the code. So you aren't forced to choose between thematic consistency and a mechanically useful choice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155940#post1155940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">like getting the hidden monster to reveal its killing form in front of a live audience and failing to prevent all casualties</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the Army of Truth have a code that says getting innocents killed is acceptable? Their goal is to convince people, you can do that without killing anyone if all goes according to plan. And when things don't go according to plan you should risk breaking points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155940#post1155940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unchallenged high Integrity isn't generally for mortal characters who are deeply committed to hardline supernatural-proximate lifestyles, </div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is arguing for unchallenged high integrity. I certainly am not. I'm arguing that if you follow your organisation's mission and modus operandi, and *everything goes according to plan* it should not cause a breaking point.<br /> <br /> but if the plan goes wrong and people get hurt that's likely a breaking point","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-05-2017, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T07:08:45-08:00","id":1156037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155986#post1155986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably won't. But as a matter of principal, if The Code says your core goal is a breaking point you modify that part of the code. Even if your Integrity is too low for it to matter mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Principle, not principal. But nitpick aside, I agree.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, the Code is how hunters maintain their sense of the rightness of what they do - without it, they're adrift. Yes? But a hunter group has a shared philosophy of what the hunt itself should be. And it's not really coherent if that philosophy - the thing the holds them together in the face of horror and madness - depends on them acting in ways that they know hunters shouldn't. If their idea of what the hunt should be clashes with their idea of what a hunter should be, one of them will change.<br /> In the case of N0, their mission says that the hunt should involve shaking people out of their complacent ignorance of the supernatural - therefore, they won't hew to a code (or a Code) that says not to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T15:39:31-08:00","id":1156176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155986#post1155986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm arguing that if you follow your organisation's mission and modus operandi, and *everything goes according to plan* it should not cause a breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> The Covenants have its members deal in shady and bloody business that will shake a vampire's Humanity.<br /> The Tribes give direction on what and how its members should Hunt, but no guidelines on balancing a werewolf's Harmony amidst the Hunt.<br /> The Orders encourage Obsessions of certain kinds, and Obsessions are known to mar a mage's Wisdom.<br /> The Refinements, although they ultimately encourage a Promethean's Pilgrimage, are not without pitfalls thanks to Prometheans keep getting stuck in Roles.<br /> The Courts are ultimately support groups, but they're still fae affairs. And delving too deep into fae affairs was never good for a changeling's Clarity.<br /> A demon has no clear parallel to Integrity, but following their Agendas lead them vulnerable to many Cover compromises, Cover being the closest thing to Integrity they have.<br /> Likewise, Beasts have no direct equivalent of Integrity (other than high Satiety making them closer to human), but we know that their Hungers erode at what human morality they keep.<br /> Likewise, Deviant isn't out yet, but as for now it's clear that whatever a Renegade is up to won't be good for their &quot;higher&quot; calling/Integrity (their Loyalty, also doubling as their Virtue) in the long run.<br /> <br /> Organizations and objectives messing with its members' personal integrity (and Integrity) isn't new to the CofD. (And I daresay, even in real life) Even if, and sometimes especially if, everything does go according to their plan. Why should hunter Compacts and Conspiracies be the exception?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T16:53:45-08:00","id":1156188,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155962#post1155962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you provide some evidence of that? I'm not seeing that interpretation in the text that we have been provided with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The compact's founder was a veteran special effects maker who had to go over a set of old tapes backwards and forwards to confirm they couldn't have been faked, broadcast them on public access television and put a call out for more, got in touch with people who had supernatural experiences on record, and <i>then </i>dropped into a powerful obsession with things he himself had never seen face to face. That the Secret Frequency is dedicated to exposing the supernatural does not make uploading spooky videos their end goal or a breaking point tantamount to chasing a poltergeist into their neighbor's garden party.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;in direct pursuit of the Vigil&quot; is from the text. There's italics in it and it's a prerequisite for getting the chance to made the trade at all. I'm given to understand that the upload is generally <i>after</i> the hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155982#post1155982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say all their goals</div> </div> </div> </div>Your exact words were &quot;if you dismiss everything Network Zero does [\u2026]&quot; and &quot;apparently Network Zero never achieves anything.&quot; It is difficult not to read those as universal statements about the directed practices of Network Zero as a hunter compact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155965#post1155965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the breaking point isn't from some supernatural effect, just seeing supernatural things is meant to create breaking points in most people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you know how there's that statistic where text-based conversation has something like four percent of the communicative clarity of face-to-face conversation because of the lack of sensory data?<br /> <br /> Cutting out smell, taste, touch and proprioception from a genuine supernatural experience goes a long long way toward cutting out its ability to rattle your understanding of the world \u2014 seeing a video of a haunting is not nearly as traumatic as being present at the screening of a haunted video, because most of the unconscious cues the human mind/body/soul picks up on are not purely visual or auditory. If a changeling breaks into a warehouse and their Contracts are caught on security footage in the middle of a fight with a security guard, the guy watching the cameras is not a meaningful witness to add to a hypothetical case against the changeling compared to the guy the changeling fought or the evidence of the footage itself.<br /> <br /> A breaking point is an instant of psychological stress powerful enough that, for a normal person, success and failure are distinguished solely by whether the numerical rating of your Integrity goes down. As nofather points out, if a highly cut-down sensory recording of supernatural activity is enough to prompt that kind of reaction then fictional instances of the supernatural in horror films \u2014 or, for that matter, just regular instances of fictional violence \u2014 would have such a disastrous impact on the public consciousness that it would beggar belief for the medium to go without extreme regulations.<br /> <br /> No player operating in good faith is likely to answer <i>What has your character forgotten?</i> with <i>I saw a YouTube video of a person turning into a flock of tooth-eyed birds when I was seven</i> in a setting where monster hunters are active and relevant, especially not when <i>I saw a person turning into a flock of tooth-eyed birds</i> is both more visceral and more readily unexplainable. Watching a version of Paranormal Activity that happens to be footage of genuine supernatural events on Netflix in the comfort of my own home should not ever have a realistic chance of forming a lasting Chamber in a Beast game and it shouldn't be an outright source of trauma in a Hunter game, either. That is a <i>silly outcome</i> that doesn't even need a particularly convoluted setup to reveal it as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1155986#post1155986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if your core concept revolves directly around breaking a clause of the code you should modify it as a matter of principal regardless of how mechanically optimal it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your core concept revolves directly around breaking a clause of the Code then you <i>pick between dealing with the consequences of regularly hitting that breaking point or trading it out for the new breaking point and the Social penalty</i>, and <i>the former is just as valid an approach as the latter</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Also, why did you pick the Army of Truth as an example of a group who trigger a high Integrity Code Breaking Point if you're going to turn around and say they don't) </div> </div> </div>I didn't. I said that if I was going to play a member of a hardline faction of a compact built around circulating word of the supernatural, particularly when that faction is the most likely to engage in violence, then I would not be expecting to retain High Integrity in the first place, much less in a way where I would be worried about secondhand exposure as the biggest concern point of my actions in the <i>direct pursuit of the Vigil</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;tacitly&quot; is an odd word to use here. But what other clause in the code could it be referring too? State the actual breaking point you think it's referring to because right now it really looks like the document itself is saying I'm right about The Army of Truth modifying that part of The Code. </div> </div> </div>I could make a case for multiple, but &quot;expose the truth as blatantly as they dare&quot; is <i>really not</i> something that sounds like Do What Network Zero Does Anyway But With More Pageviews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They probably won't. But as a matter of principal, if The Code says your core goal is a breaking point you modify that part of the code. </div> </div> </div>No. Y'all're making this a harder line than it actually needs to be and then complaining when that results in nonsense. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1104161-why-do-you-think-beast-is-good-bad?p=1104738#post1104738\">I am axiomatically opposed to that as a form of argument about these games</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why I and others argue for the ability to make multiple changes to the code. So you aren't forced to choose between thematic consistency and a mechanically useful choice. </div> </div> </div>Thematic consistency is not &quot;members of compacts and conspiracies universally go all-in the moment they hit a relevant Code-based breaking point regardless of what it is&quot; and it's disingenuous in the extreme to characterize &quot;not trading out a High Integrity breaking point because you don't have plans to hunt at High Integrity often&quot; as &quot;just&quot; a mechanically useful choice when your position is then &quot;I need to be able to trade out three quarters of the universal High Integrity breaking points because what if I want to play at High Integrity and still do things that are core to my hunter group and can be stretched to be read as breaking points or do things that are breaking points and can be stretched to be read as core elements of my hunter group?&quot;* which is an argument based <i>entirely</i> in mechanical optimization. I'm not here for that.<br /> <br /> * Seriously? &quot;They hate VALKYRIE so they should get to trade out the other-hunters-in-need section&quot;? Their sharing information with other hunter organizations and tagging onto cells with non-netzo hunters is <i>in the corebook, under the auspices of &quot;Network Zero's members aren't stupid.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would the Army of Truth have a code that says getting innocents killed is acceptable? Their goal is to convince people, you can do that without killing anyone if all goes according to plan. And when things don't go according to plan you should risk breaking points. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that I said &quot;casualty,&quot; not &quot;death,&quot; Hunter as a gameline is filled to the brim with archetypes who treat collateral damage as an acceptable loss. &quot;Secret monster shreds three with slavering jaws in mass panic&quot; is more undeniable than &quot;man turns into living meat-thresher at pep rally, waves arms around for a bit, breaks volleyball net.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think anyone is arguing for unchallenged high integrity. I certainly am not. I'm arguing that if you follow your organisation's mission and modus operandi, and *everything goes according to plan* it should not cause a breaking point. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the argument I've made above about what kind of &quot;exposure&quot; can be reasonably said to count as a breaking point, the core nature of Integrity includes &quot;A breaking point is a breaking point even if the character thinks they're doing the right thing.&quot; That doesn't fall out of consideration just because you took up the Vigil and dedicated yourself to the creed of a hunter group, but it <i>does</i> fall out of consideration in tiered systems when the character is below the threshold for a given breaking point.<br /> <br /> Your argument is that the playtest's mechanics force you to spend the trade on the first breaking point you read in the list from top to bottom as soon as possible and that hunters should be expected to realistically execute plans perfectly and without internal consequence in a game based around a contentious archetype dealing with a class of phenomenon that damages the mortal psyche to confront. My point is that that's simply not how Integrity stats work in these games and the purpose of the trade-off is a combination of Werewolf's two free dots of Rites to allow every starting character to get Sacred Hunt if they want it and the exceptions Wisdom and Humanity lets you build in to emphasize that organized hunters can be strange and unsettling in their priorities.<br /> <br /> A vampire who takes on a bane and then strives constantly for high Humanity has his work cut out for him but can arrange a suitable environment for it if he twists and tilts his surroundings with every tool at his disposal, including proxies and other support networks; a mage who inures her most versatile spells and holds to high Wisdom does her best by living the life of a hermit, funneling Mana into her spells, containing Paradoxes, and culling Strong sympathetic connections she doesn't have immediate need of while leveraging front organizations toward her goals at a remove; hunters trying to maintain high Integrity with Code modifications <i>explicitly</i> benefit from connecting deeply and often with people they trust, and best practices for keeping that rating include contending with the known supernatural peacefully or indirectly wherever possible, not privileging the monsters over the mortals in the course of negotiating a workable outcome, and taking the time to harden themselves against as broad a variety of supernatural interaction as possible before they make this retreat/retirement in the event that they have to encounter or kill or torture a monster \u2014 a High-Integrity hunter who maintains that rating is an old hand and a living resource in a group that will allow him to operate in a manageable locale with competent associates.<br /> <br /> The mage and the vampire both have to <i>lose</i> their respective Integrity-alikes to get their bonuses; the hunter gets their trade offer the moment the opportunity for the roll <i>comes up</i>. Those aren't descents that reverse themselves quickly or easily, and being able to stabilize at 6 is tricky enough for the average hunter without a creed to fall back on, which is why I don't view the smash-myself-against-the-glass-breaker splat as particularly in need of a better exception clause than what they're presently given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T16:56:40-08:00","id":1156190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156176#post1156176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?<br /> <br /> The Covenants have its members deal in shady and bloody business that will shake a vampire's Humanity.<br /> The Tribes give direction on what and how its members should Hunt, but no guidelines on balancing a werewolf's Harmony amidst the Hunt.<br /> The Orders encourage Obsessions of certain kinds, and Obsessions are known to mar a mage's Wisdom.<br /> The Refinements, although they ultimately encourage a Promethean's Pilgrimage, are not without pitfalls thanks to Prometheans keep getting stuck in Roles.<br /> The Courts are ultimately support groups, but they're still fae affairs. And delving too deep into fae affairs was never good for a changeling's Clarity.<br /> A demon has no clear parallel to Integrity, but following their Agendas lead them vulnerable to many Cover compromises, Cover being the closest thing to Integrity they have.<br /> Likewise, Beasts have no direct equivalent of Integrity (other than high Satiety making them closer to human), but we know that their Hungers erode at what human morality they keep.<br /> Likewise, Deviant isn't out yet, but as for now it's clear that whatever a Renegade is up to won't be good for their &quot;higher&quot; calling/Integrity (their Loyalty, also doubling as their Virtue) in the long run.<br /> <br /> Organizations and objectives messing with its members' personal integrity (and Integrity) isn't new to the CofD. (And I daresay, even in real life) Even if, and sometimes especially if, everything does go according to their plan. Why should hunter Compacts and Conspiracies be the exception?</div> </div> </div> </div>You get more than a like sir-you get me personally thanking you for the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T17:20:58-08:00","id":1156196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Covenants have its members deal in shady and bloody business that will shake a vampire's Humanity.<br /> The Tribes give direction on what and how its members should Hunt, but no guidelines on balancing a werewolf's Harmony amidst the Hunt.<br /> The Orders encourage Obsessions of certain kinds, and Obsessions are known to mar a mage's Wisdom.<br /> The Refinements, although they ultimately encourage a Promethean's Pilgrimage, are not without pitfalls thanks to Prometheans keep getting stuck in Roles.<br /> The Courts are ultimately support groups, but they're still fae affairs. And delving too deep into fae affairs was never good for a changeling's Clarity.<br /> A demon has no clear parallel to Integrity, but following their Agendas lead them vulnerable to many Cover compromises, Cover being the closest thing to Integrity they have.<br /> Likewise, Beasts have no direct equivalent of Integrity (other than high Satiety making them closer to human), but we know that their Hungers erode at what human morality they keep.<br /> Likewise, Deviant isn't out yet, but as for now it's clear that whatever a Renegade is up to won't be good for their &quot;higher&quot; calling/Integrity (their Loyalty, also doubling as their Virtue) in the long run.<br /> <br /> Organizations and objectives messing with its members' personal integrity (and Integrity) isn't new to the CofD. (And I daresay, even in real life) Even if, and sometimes especially if, everything does go according to their plan. Why should hunter Compacts and Conspiracies be the exception? </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, and I dare say I think that was intentionally reinforced in 2E, since 1) They wanted the Integrity/Equivalent to play a bigger role than be a stat you can maintain high just by avoiding doing a few things you'd only do when you're an asshole anyway and 2) You get a Beat whenever you get a Breaking Point, so it has become a major way to gain Experience rather than just a negative point. I suspect this also was a factor in adding in Touchstones (to give a better chance for the Breaking point to succeed).<br /> <br /> But I think that in this case, the problem is more that the Code tells us something about your character's way of thinking, which you should have more freedom to decide.<br /> <br /> Things like Integrity, Humanity or Clarity are more like a state of mind not directly linked to your thought or belief (at least in 2E). They measure things like your sanity, how much you still are able to connect with humans despite being literally a walking corpse, or your ability to discern reality from fantasy. Traits like Hunger or Cover are even more alien, describing how hungry the nightmare you have as a soul is or how efficient your human disguise is.<br /> <br /> The Code, meanwhile, describe a code of conduct and philosophy of life your character alledgedly chose to follow of his own will and genuinely believes in. Even if he joined a group who believe something entirely different or if his player thinks this entire Code is bullshit. In other words, it limits the creative control you have over your character and what he/she thinks. And I think that's a problem.<br /> <br /> It makes sense for the Ordo Dracul and the Lancea Sanctum to lose humanity when doing their things because regardless of what they personally want or believe, it does distance them from humans. It makes sense for the Courts to lose Clarity when dealing with Fae because regardless of their goals, Fae will still mess with how they distinguish reality from fantasy. And it makes sense for Demons to risk their Covers when acting their Agenda because whatever they want doesn't factor on their ability to maintain a disguise.<br /> <br /> But it doesn't make sense for Compacts and Conspiracies to feel torn apart about not following rules their factions are explicilty stated <i>not</i> to care about. If the Lucifuge judge monsters on weither they are good or evil rather than on weither they are monsters or humans, they should not feel bad about defending some monsters against humans. If the Union just fight everyone messing up with their neightborhood supernatural or not with no discrimination, they shouldn't feel bothered about hurting humans when they are assholes. Granted, these aren't absolute (for exemple, the Cheiron Group might recruit people who believe in the Code forcefully), but the possibility of some of them not caring about this Code should still be real.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd like to get back on the exercise if nobody mind. Who's up for doing the next groups?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-05-2017, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T17:49:40-08:00","id":1156204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156196#post1156196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Code, meanwhile, describe a code of conduct and philosophy of life your character alledgedly chose to follow of his own will and genuinely believes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the Code is a set of survival instincts with an occasional in-universe name slapped on it. Werewolves who've never heard of the Oath of the Moon still lose their balance when they eat people, vampires making other vampires costs them their Humanity with or without the second Tradition, and so on up the chain. Your character can still be as deadened to the instinct that tells them <i>Don't leave that potential ally alone against the darkness!</i> as they are to the little voice that tells them to shy away from the supernatural as a mundane human, because <i>that is one of the benefits of having a tiered Integrity ladder whose middle section tops off at one point below the average starting character</i>.<br /> <br /> Seriously, <i>why</i> is becoming Vigilant being treated as a failure condition here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T18:06:49-08:00","id":1156208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, the Code is a set of survival instincts with an occasional in-universe name slapped on it. </div> </div> </div>You're saying the Lucifuge's survival instincts tell them to priorize mortal humans who are likely to hate them for being half-demons over supernatural beings who technically have much more in common with them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves who've never heard of the Oath of the Moon still lose their balance when they eat people </div> </div> </div>Actually, the 2E book is pretty explicit that violating an Oath of the Moon is a Breaking Point for the Forsaken, and ONLY the Forsaken (page 104 if you don't believe me). And eating people doesn't cause a Breaking point because of the Oath of the Moon (though that probably helps), but more because cannibalism is a spirit-like behaviour, making them act closer to spirits than humans and as such moving their Harmony toward Spirits (just like eating cooked food make their Harmony move to the other side because it's something <i>humans</i> would do), as explained in the sample Ivory Claw npc if I remember correct. It's still unrelated to their personal belief or moral code.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> vampires making other vampires costs them their Humanity with or without the second Tradition </div> </div> </div>Again, nothing to do with the Tradition, the Humanity loss is a natural effect of the Embrace. As explained in Blood and Smoke Page 61:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dissenters argue that this [the Second Tradition] is a law that needs no enforcement. Populations of predators take care of themselves, and the price of the Embrace is enough to control the numbers. There is a price. The Beast takes a toll for this transgression. The sire loses something, a bit of personality, or maybe a piece of the Man, sliced off on the altar of the Beast, where every vampire, sooner or later, sacrifices more and more of themselves. </div> </div> </div>Now, can we <i>please</i> get back on that exercise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-05-2017, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T19:17:41-08:00","id":1156222,"title":"","content":"I love how the work of Network Zero is been seen as limited to &quot;spooky videos&quot;. And yeah, you're right that seeing footage of a supernatural event in the middle of a movie wouldn't provoke any real response.... but that's not because it's &quot;spooky video&quot;, that's because it's been presented as being fake. No one thinks the things that happen in movies happen, because we know it's a movie. I'm sure no one in network zero would actively try to present the evidence they've collected as being fake, since that's the direct opposite of their vigil's mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T20:49:28-08:00","id":1156230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156208#post1156208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're saying the Lucifuge's survival instincts tell them to priorize mortal humans who are likely to hate them for being half-demons over supernatural beings who technically have much more in common with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that the Lucifuge are humans with the capacity to gain supernatural powers, are personally interesting to supernatural entities, and are culturally built around a practice that notionally draws a line between them and the monsters which they hunt and which they possess no especial natural resistance to in terms of exposure. As before, this attitude of &quot;assholes don't count&quot; is no more useful to Hunter than it is to Promethean.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that the Lucifuge run on Integrity and most of the monsters they &quot;technically have much more in common with&quot; either don't run on Integrity, run on Integrity <i>badly</i>, or are generally antithetical to Integrity. Trying to be like a mage exploring the depths of their Vice or a Promethean on the Refinement of Cobalt is going to have deleterious effects on your self-image, as is emulating the slasher who only kills perpetrators of child abuse or the demon who hasn't worried about tempting people to sin in thousands of years. Hunters are human and humans do not develop well under close relations with the supernatural in general and hunters have a <i>partial</i> hack to hold off the dread march of magical proximity on their self-image, which should not ever be confused with a hard lockout from human concerns.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that &quot;people are likely to hate you for being what you secretly are&quot; has historically led more frequently to people hiding what they secretly are than to throwing in their lot with an entropic cavalcade of unrestrained enablers without turning into a monster and that the Lucifuge having a semiunique antagonist type that is <i>specifically &quot;the type of people the Lucifuge recruits from, but they didn't get the call to become monster-hunters and got screwed up trucking with demons&quot;</i> is a point of tension that disappears from focus if you can just uniformly declare that the presence of exceptions on either end of the divide matters more than the fact that monsters mess up human lives unduly much when they interfere badly enough to get noticed by monster-hunters.<br /> <br /> Being part of a secret conspiracy of half-demon monster-hunters fighting against the temptations their wicked brethren gave into is not a <i>healthy</i> place to be stuck in, but spending time as a monster-hunter is spending time separating yourself from mundane humanity. Normal people aren't wired to look directly at the monsters doing monstrous things, and as a hunter you are <i>only barely</i> Not Normal People.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, the 2E book is pretty explicit that violating an Oath of the Moon is a Breaking Point for the Forsaken, and ONLY the Forsaken (page 104 if you don't believe me). </div> </div> </div>My dude I have read the books and it is just possible that this point had nothing to do with the &quot;violating the Oath of the Moon&quot; breaking point in 2e on account of how it's a valid observation even in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And eating people doesn't cause a Breaking point because of the Oath of the Moon (though that probably helps), but more because cannibalism is a spirit-like behaviour, making them act closer to spirits than humans and as such moving their Harmony toward Spirits (just like eating cooked food make their Harmony move to the other side because it's something <i>humans</i> would do), as explained in the sample Ivory Claw npc if I remember correct. It's still unrelated to their personal belief or moral code. </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm saying that, much like how the Oath of the Moon has tenets that happen to correspond to Harmony breaking points, <i>the Code's universal defaults are there with or without the explicit adoption of a formal belief system.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, nothing to do with the Tradition, the Humanity loss is a natural effect of the Embrace. </div> </div> </div>See above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Now, can we </span><i>please</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> get back on that exercise?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Is it remotely worth the time?</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156222#post1156222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love how the work of Network Zero is been seen as limited to &quot;spooky videos&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, did you have another thing that the compact is supposed to be doing in the course of the Vigil often enough to justify complaints about being forced to spend the freebie on getting rid of the one breaking point? Because that appears to have been the entirety of the focus in this discussion as it relates to Network Zero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah, you're right that seeing footage of a supernatural event in the middle of a movie wouldn't provoke any real response.... but that's not because it's &quot;spooky video&quot;, that's because it's been presented as being fake. </div> </div> </div>The reduced impact of using platforms like YouTube to circulate their footage is specifically brought up in Compacts and Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one thinks the things that happen in movies happen, because we know it's a movie. I'm sure no one in network zero would actively try to present the evidence they've collected as being fake, since that's the direct opposite of their vigil's mission. </div> </div> </div>I love how the implication you're making here is that a YouTube video with a completely sincere title like &quot;VAMPIRE CAUGHT ON FILM IN NEW BRUNSWICK&quot; is any more credibly &quot;real&quot; to a casual viewer than a creepy but mundane website that makes a strong case for its actually hosting the real legitimate video from The Ring.<br /> <br /> <i>The vast majority of Network Zero does not do what the Panoptic Cons do, and if they did then they would have bigger Integrity problems than inciting breaking points to worry about. The vast majority of Network Zero's major factions do not even focus on exposure as a positive thing.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T02:31:13-08:00","id":1156264,"title":"","content":"Fine for the Lucifuge. Then what about the Cheiron Group? Are you saying that when forced to chose between sacrificing their comrads to bring back the quarry to their boss who will probably execute them or use them as lab rats in case of failure or let said quarry go to save their fellow hunters, they will still pick the option that will clearly doom them because their survival instinct tell them to do so? Or that when the Union is confronted with a mundane serial killer/gang dealer harming their neightborhood, their &quot;survival instincts&quot; will tell them to spare him on the basis he is human and they might need him as an ally should supernatural beings who aren't even here at the moment suddenly show up? I could find many other examples.<br /> <br /> Yes, survival instincts can encourage humans to watch each other's back in period of need. But it can also push you to do do things such as betray other humans or harm them to save your own hide. I think it should be pretty obvious in the Horror genre this very game is based on. Survival instincts have no strict rules on how you'll react, it's just something compelling you to do whatever is necessary to survive, and will often (though not always) cause you to forget about your ethics and moral code. In other words, <i>it's not a Code</i> <i>and should not be referred as such</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My dude I have read the books and it is just possible that this point had nothing to do with the &quot;violating the Oath of the Moon&quot; breaking point in 2e on account of how it's a valid observation even in 1e. </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how that contradicts my statement above. And I just explained <i>why</i> eating people was a breaking point in 2E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. I'm saying that, much like how the Oath of the Moon has tenets that happen to correspond to Harmony breaking points, <i>the Code's universal defaults are there with or without the explicit adoption of a formal belief system.</i> </div> </div> </div>And that's kinda the problem here. Eating people of your own kind is something anyone somewhat healthy will agree is sick, and in the case of Werewolves will <i>always</i> result in you losing balance if done too much. The Code is suggesting that even without the Belief system, occasionally treating monsters like humans, or even judging them on their value as person rather than what they are (something <i>much more</i> subjective and that can even be seen as good) is just as dangerous for your mental health, even though while it can be, it can also be a good thing in the right context. <i>Yes</i>, trying to treat monster humanly can be a naive attitude resulting in you trusting the wrong person, becoming jaded or disabused or getting slowly lost due to how many shades of grey in the world of Darkness. But it can also result in you getting a better understanding of who deserves to die or not, recovering hope in the world and rebuilding friendships with people you thought were lost, all good things-- unlike eating human flesh which cannot result in good. The two aren't even comparable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Is it remotely worth the time?</span> </div> </div> </div>Definitely more than going back on that damn debate that hasn't been really moving since the beginning of this conversation. At least we would be seeing how restraining the Code truly is for each group gameplay-wise, and be able to judge if it's as much a problem as Raven and I thought. But if you don't want to take part, I won't keep you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-06-2017, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T03:45:54-08:00","id":1156278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156176#post1156176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Organizations and objectives messing with its members' personal integrity (and Integrity) isn't new to the CofD. (And I daresay, even in real life) Even if, and sometimes especially if, everything does go according to their plan. Why should hunter Compacts and Conspiracies be the exception?</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that modifying the Code is something we specifically know that membership in a hunter groups will be doing. Therefore the return question is that if there's a tenet diametrically opposite to their mission, why wouldn't that be the one they modify?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T04:08:01-08:00","id":1156280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156176#post1156176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Organizations and objectives messing with its members' personal integrity (and Integrity) isn't new to the CofD. (And I daresay, even in real life) Even if, and sometimes especially if, everything does go according to their plan. Why should hunter Compacts and Conspiracies be the exception?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean aside from the fact that it's already in the rules that Hunter organisations modify the code to prevent their goals and modus operandi directly causing breaking points and all anyone's asking for is a small tweak to the rules that increases the maximum number of shifts that would bring the number of Integrity protections in line with other gamelines such as Vampire's Banes?<br /> <br /> The answer is simple. I believe that a Breaking Point should be a significant moment in your character's character development. If Breaking Points turn up regularly as you go through your character's normal routine then they won't have the same amount of impact when your character betrays their selfhood or experiences a shocking event that's outside their daily grind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156188#post1156188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your argument is that the playtest's mechanics force you to spend the trade on the first breaking point you read in the list from top to bottom as soon as possible</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a completely inaccurate understanding of my views.<br /> <br /> I don't think anything forces you to spend the trade on the first breaking point you read going top to bottom, nor do I think there's any reason or principle that says you should pick the topmost one that applies.<br /> <br /> What I actually think is that you should spend the trade on breaking point that most strongly conflicts with the organization's/your charachter's methods and ideology. With Network Zero getting someone hurt or killed because you tried to expose them to the supernatural is a real risk, but exposing them to the supernatural is the goal in of itself and thus it has the strongest conflict.<br /> <br /> It's not about preserving high Integrity, it's about creating a Code that accurately reflects the character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156188#post1156188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that hunters should be expected to realistically execute plans perfectly and without internal consequence in a game based around a contentious archetype dealing with a class of phenomenon that damages the mortal psyche to confront</div> </div> </div> </div> Well that depends on what you're planning doesn't it. If your plan is to take a local journalist to the Goblin Market (the one held on Earth that you've visited before), walk around for the minimum time it takes for them to accept what they're seeing, then go home without buying anything then I'd say there's a fair chance that will go off without a hitch. You might need a roll to hold onto the journalist before he bolts or to clamp a hand over his mouth before he says something that could be taken as a promise. Perhaps a roll to resist a merchant with a very tempting offer. But it's reasonable for this plan to go perfectly.<br /> <br /> And having the occasional plan go right makes it more dramatic and impactful when a harder plan like trying to kill a powerful monster goes wrong, which it probably will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156188#post1156188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Seriously? &quot;They hate VALKYRIE so they should get to trade out the other-hunters-in-need section&quot;? Their sharing information with other hunter organizations and tagging onto cells with non-netzo hunters is <i>in the corebook, under the auspices of &quot;Network Zero's members aren't stupid.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div> You realize that you could trade &quot;help hunters in need&quot; for &quot;help hunters in need, unless they're VALKARIE&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156188#post1156188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the argument I've made above about what kind of &quot;exposure&quot; can be reasonably said to count as a breaking point, the core nature of Integrity includes &quot;A breaking point is a breaking point even if the character thinks they're doing the right thing.&quot; That doesn't fall out of consideration just because you took up the Vigil and dedicated yourself to the creed of a hunter group</div> </div> </div> </div> The playtest document explicitly says that dedicating yourself to the creed of a Compact/Conspiracy allows to modify your code to better reflect what you (and your peers) consider the right thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T04:59:16-08:00","id":1156286,"title":"","content":"Let's return to exercise - and focus on <b>Null Mysteriis</b> and playtest's Code:<br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - They do not seems to experiment on humans like Cherion is doing - So I think it's 'No'<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - MAYBE to test some hypothesis to save few hundred others. But do not seem thing on day to day business.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - Totally 'No' as they are <b>most friendly</b> of hunters groups.<br /> * Killing a person - Totally 'No', if they can miss it.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - MAYBE, as seeing once again 'my theory did not work'.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - MAYBE when they are <b>really</b> fascinated by supernatural phenomena at hand..<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Not likely to me.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Does not seems to be a case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2017, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:39:10-08:00","id":1156298,"title":"","content":"And let's do <b>Ashwood Abbey</b> also - mark, I just go with Abbey as 'looking for adrenaline gentelments club', not quasi-Slashers group.<br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - MAYBE - they do not seems to be 'kill, kill, kill' - but they look for new ways to explore pleasures. So going over hard BDSM can be certainly in their M.O.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - They mostly do harm to monsters, but I can certainly see situations like 'mistaken harm' on other people. Let's mark it as 'Yes'.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - Their 1E corebook write-up points they are misleading other hunters on Vigil - so I mark it as 'Yes'.<br /> * Killing a person - MAYBE - I can easily see them trying to kill Slasher. 'Just for fun!'<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - Totally 'Yes' - Ashwood Abbey is all about not being consistent with the consequences of their actions.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - MAYBE when they are <b>really</b> fascinated by supernatural phenomena at hand.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - I will said 'Yes' - 'It can be fun!'<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - 1E corebook points it's clearly 'Yes'.<br /> <br /> So on my count - we have 3 times 'Yes' and 3 times 'Maybe' on Abbey, contrasted to Code in Playtest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:59:26-08:00","id":1156311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156286#post1156286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's return to exercise - and focus on <b>Null Mysteriis</b> and playtest's Code:<br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - They do not seems to experiment on humans like Cherion is doing - So I think it's 'No'<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - MAYBE to test some hypothesis to save few hundred others. But do not seem thing on day to day business.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - Totally 'No' as they are <b>most friendly</b> of hunters groups.<br /> * Killing a person - Totally 'No', if they can miss it.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - MAYBE, as seeing once again 'my theory did not work'.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - MAYBE when they are <b>really</b> fascinated by supernatural phenomena at hand..<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Not likely to me.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Does not seems to be a case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter two sound like they could be <i>possible</i>. They could try to find a way to use supernatural energies for something, and they might thwart attempts to destroy a supernatural phenomenon that's interesting but seemingly harmless. On the other hand, both of those sound like they should be big deals that change a lot for the compact if they come to pass - which makes them good to keep as breaking points.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night:</b><br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - In relevant ways, definitely not.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Again, no.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - I could see this being possible. First, they may see themsleves as uniquely sanctioned. Second, I could see them regarding many hunters as too close to being monsters to count.<br /> * Killing a person - No.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - No.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - The closest I can see is shielding a repentent monster from vengeance.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Hell, no.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Unlikely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey:</b><br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - Maybe.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Absolutely. Hunting is an extreme sport to them, and they'll take this risk constantly in their fun and games.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - Probably not. Again, extreme sport, and they wouldn't pass up the chance to take part.<br /> * Killing a person - Maybe.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - Again, extreme sport, and a risk they take constantly.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - Unlikely. They draw their hunts out, but that's hardly championing a monster's autonomy.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Sure if it looks like fun.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - This is more likely to happen <i>to</i> them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Task Force VALKYRIE:</b><br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - The personnel of VALKYRIE would comprise people who are hardened to this if it's needful for the mission.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Likewise.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - Similarly to the Long Night, they might regard themselves as having a unique sanction that others might not have.<br /> * Killing a person - Again, they would likely be hardened to this.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - No.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - No.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - No.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - Refusing I can see, but if they've not done that, I don't think they'd do this later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aegis kai Doru:</b><br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - Robbing them probably doesn't count, so no.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Likewise.<br /> * Refusing aid to a fellow hunter in need - No.<br /> * Killing a person - No.<br /> * Learning that a monster harmed a person when you could have done something to stop it but didn\u2019t - No.<br /> * Putting the well-being or autonomy of a monster over that of a person - No.<br /> * Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source - Some of their relics count, though they lock the worst ones away rather than using them.<br /> * Betraying a fellow hunter - In this case, robbing them probably does count.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:37:37-08:00","id":1156341,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Wyrdhamster and Sunless Nick^^ Gotta point out though: Slashers aren't considered &quot;persons&quot; according to the new rules; they are classified as monsters. I know, that's stupid, but eh, let's not digress.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll try doing a brief recap of all the groups we did so far:<br /> <br /> * Malleus Maleficarum: One certainly, three maybe<br /> * Cheiron Group: Four certainly, one maybe<br /> * Lucifuge: Two certainly, two maybe<br /> * VALKYRIE: Three certainly<br /> * Ascending Ones: Two certainly, four maybe<br /> * Loyalists of Thule: Seven maybe yes<br /> * Null Mysterii: Three maybe<br /> * Ashwood Abbey: Three certainly, two maybe<br /> * Long Night: One maybe<br /> * Aegis Kai Doru: One maybe.<br /> <br /> Sooo, that's more than half the Core compacts and conspiracies, and already we can see many of them need more than 1 freebie.<br /> <br /> Now let's see what's remaining... I think that'd be the Union and Network Zero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-06-2017, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:04:05-08:00","id":1156349,"title":"","content":"I did Net0 a while back. I give them two certainlys and no maybe's<br /> <br /> * exposing the supernatural is replaced.<br /> * refusing to help other Hunters is modified to exclude VALKARIE or better yet: all government/big corporate spooks.<br /> <br /> As for The Union. I think they're just one maybe: Putting a monster above a human. I could see them doing that if said monster is part of their community and the human is an outsider. But that requires a monster whose in good standing in their community so most Union Hunters won't do it.<br /> <br /> All in all though it looks like one code modification simply isn't enough to accurately model the ideologies of the core groups<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156311#post1156311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Aegis kai Doru:</b><br /> <br /> * Causing significant harm to a person - Robbing them probably doesn't count, so no.<br /> * Allowing harm to come to a person in pursuit of your Vigil - Likewise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Robbing doesn't require harm, but if they fight back it could happen... normally I would say if they fight back and get hurt that should be a breaking point but the AKD always struck me as real fanatics about Relics. Add in that a lot of people Relics belong to Hunters who will fight back, and I'd say this is at least a maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-06-2017, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:14:48-08:00","id":1156351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did Net0 a while back. I give them two certainlys and no maybe's </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry then. I must have missed them when I scrolled back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> s for The Union. I think they're just one maybe: Putting a monster above a human. I could see them doing that if said monster is part of their community and the human is an outsider. But that requires a monster whose in good standing in their community so most Union Hunters won't do it. </div> </div> </div>So no Yes for killing a person? They <i>are </i>known to also hunt drug dealers and gangsters. I also remember Spirit Slayer had a story about how an Union Cell once made a deal with a Werewolf pack to leave them alone as long as they would focus their hunts only on criminals. It was one of my favourite parts in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:41:15-08:00","id":1156357,"title":"","content":"Doh, your right. My understanding of the Union is kinda frozen in the core book. The supplements had a different author who changed direction a little and I stuck with the original for the most part.<br /> <br /> I suspect though we'd see more kneecapping and less killing in 2E if they keep the criminal hunting at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:46:35-08:00","id":1156358,"title":"","content":"Ah. I didn't realize this had been added in later books. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T08:52:53-08:00","id":1156361,"title":"","content":"No worries, later books count of course. You were right on this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T10:17:10-08:00","id":1156387,"title":"","content":"It seems to be oriented so that you are supposed to get breaking points acting as a normal hunter, assuming you arn't completely jaded/absurdly careful. It isn't so much that they &quot;need freebies&quot;, its that &quot;you will get breaking points by being a normal member of this group&quot;. Being a member of the group means that you can ignore a few of them, but the system isn't designed so that you can get away with whatever because your group thinks it is OK. They are not meant to keep you at Integrity 7. They arn't even meant to slow your fall. They are meant to &quot;hunt&quot; monsters, each in their own way that may or may not involve literally hunting.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> KR is still putting way more weight to Breaking Points then the book does. The book's breaking points are basically &quot;incredibly stressful situations&quot;. Seeing a bloody corpse is a breaking point, but it probably isn't a significant point in your character's development (especially if this is the hundredth bloody corpse he has seen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 11-06-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T12:01:45-08:00","id":1156423,"title":"","content":"I think seeing a bloody corpse would be a significant point in your characters development. Remember that Breaking Points in the corebook are customised to your characters' psychology, at least to an extent. <br /> <br /> Seeing your 100th corpse wouldn't be a Breaking Point. Seeing your first would be the moment you realise you're not in Kansas anymore, that the situation you're in is more dangerous than anything you've been in before and you have to make a decision: Press on or run away from this situation with your tail between your legs.<br /> <br /> That is a significant moment in your character development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156387#post1156387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not meant to keep you at Integrity 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is saying they should keep you at 7. It's not about keeping Integrity high, it's about creating a Code that's consistent with your character. Take Network Zero the changes I would make is:<br /> <br /> * Replace the BP for exposing people to the supernatural with a BP for hiding the truth. This is probably going to trigger more Breaking Points than the original because the character will face situations where they're forced to hide the truth or alienate people in their mundane life by telling the truth - which is a breaking point in of itself.<br /> <br /> * Modify the BP that requires helping other Hunters to exclude VALKARIE and other spooks. Not really much of a difference in of itself, but it has drawbacks such as counting at lower integrity. (And I'm in favour of adding a Bane like mechanics that gives disadvantages for each modification)<br /> <br /> So it's not about keeping Integrity high, it's about the mechanics accurately modeling the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-06-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T12:27:13-08:00","id":1156433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156423#post1156423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think seeing a bloody corpse would be a significant point in your characters development. Remember that Breaking Points in the corebook are customised to your characters' psychology, at least to an extent.<br /> <br /> Seeing your 100th corpse wouldn't be a Breaking Point. Seeing your first would be the moment you realise you're not in Kansas anymore, that the situation you're in is more dangerous than anything you've been in before and you have to make a decision: Press on or run away from this situation with your tail between your legs.<br /> <br /> That is a significant moment in your character development.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was hyperbole. For an actual example, lets look at the breaking points that are the same for everyone to remove as much subjectivity as possible. A normal mortal investigator gets a breaking point for: killing something, witnessing the supernatural, and getting hit by a supernatural attack. Thus, a normal mortal investigator would suffer from three breaking points over the course of a normal fight with any type of supernatural creature. Would you seriously consider that each of these three things constitutes &quot;major character development&quot;, every single time they happen? Now lets say that you say &quot;witnessing the supernatural&quot; is something they do long enough to no longer constitute a breaking point, I'll point out this can't be the case for Awakened magic or Lunacy. Is it really a major changing point in your character's lives every time they see a careless Mage shoot a fireball out of their hands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T13:08:29-08:00","id":1156453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156433#post1156433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would you seriously consider that each of these three things constitutes &quot;major character development&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>As a matter of fact I would (but if all three happened at once it's only a single BP). A mortal investigator will be expecting his case to involve mortals, if he discovered it's actually pointing to the supernatural he'd have to choose between pressing on or quitting: a significant character development moment.<br /> <br /> Even if that's the last scene of the case and the game you could still have an epilogue about how he was affected by the discovery. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156433#post1156433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> every single time they happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>yes. In my opinion a character who does something that they know is likely to put them into conflict with the supernatural, like take a detective case after the last two led to the supernatural should either become a Hunter or see their integrity plummet. They clearly have a problem and are refusing to address it constructively.<br /> <br /> It would take good role playing to make each attack a significant milestone on the spiral of self-destruction but it's within the reach of any competent player.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156433#post1156433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is it really a major changing point in your character's lives every time they see a careless Mage shoot a fireball out of their hands?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now we're getting into crossover and I've always maintained that crossover usually requires tweaks here and there. If all the PCs are mortals I would adjust the rules that make careless fireballs no more and no less likely to trigger a breaking point as non supernal supernatural effects. If all the PCs are Awakened it doesn't matter if NPCs breaking points are significant character development moments or not.<br /> <br /> If there are mortal and awakened players... tough one, but I'd probably adjust the rule to inflict Conditions rather than Breaking Points","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-06-2017, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T13:49:44-08:00","id":1156465,"title":"","content":"I was using &quot;Mortal Investigator&quot; as the term for &quot;Blue book PC&quot;, not as an actual profession. I could see were that could be confusing. Maybe I should have capitalized it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a matter of fact I would (but if all three happened at once it's only a single BP). A mortal investigator will be expecting his case to involve mortals, if he discovered it's actually pointing to the supernatural he'd have to choose between pressing on or quitting: a significant character development moment.<br /> <br /> Even if that's the last scene of the case and the game you could still have an epilogue about how he was affected by the discovery. </div> </div> </div>Lets say it isn't someone with a choice. Someone is targeted by the supernatural constantly and fights it off, but would much rather live a quite life away from it all. Someone without the resolve to become a hunter, but who still ends up with a high supernatural body count anyways. Is it still a major character change after his fifth/six/fiftieth kill?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yes. In my opinion a character who does something that they know is likely to put them into conflict with the supernatural, like take a detective case after the last two led to the supernatural should either become a Hunter or see their integrity plummet.<br /> <br /> It would take good role playing to make each attack a significant milestone on the spiral of self-destruction but it's within the reach of any competent player. </div> </div> </div>But that isn't the question. The question is &quot;Does it lead to major character development every single time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Heck, lets remove the supernatural entirely from the example to sidestep the issue. Lets say that the character is a completely normal human hitman &quot;Johnny the Saint&quot;. Johnny is a stereotypical &quot;Hitman with a heart&quot;. No women, no children, 25% of all proceeds go to worthy charities. In game terms, he tries to keep his Integrity at 7+ despite his profession.<br /> <br /> Johnny is experienced. Before the game's start, he killed 10 men. In the course of the game, he kills another. Killing someone is always a breaking point, even for someone like Johnny. Kill 11 was a horrible person any vigilante would be happy to take out free of charge, and gives Johnny no reason to question his path. Then it goes on, is kill 12, 13, 14, ...30 etc all significant points of character development?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, now we're getting into crossover and I've always maintained that crossover usually requires tweaks here and there. If all the PCs are mortals I would adjust the rules that make careless fireballs auto-trigger breaking points. If all the PCs are Awakened it doesn't matter if NPCs breaking points are significant character development moments or not.<br /> <br /> If there are mortal and awakened players... tough one, but I'd probably adjust the rule to inflict Conditions rather than Breaking Points </div> </div> </div>I was using it as an example to point out that breaking points often don't have the weight you give them in the books. It was more &quot;this shows the authors' intent&quot; than &quot;what if this absurdly specific event just happens to happen&quot;.<br /> <br /> In my understanding, Integrity is basically &quot;Hit points of the soul&quot;. Breaking points can be-but by no means must be- major events in your character's lives. Johnny in the last example probably won't change much with each of his kills, but they will get to his head if he keeps it up without any attempts to stop himself from falling. He most likely won't change much if he randomly witnesses (then forgets) a Mage casting a spell, but the event isn't good for his mental health anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T16:56:05-08:00","id":1156514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156465#post1156465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say it isn't someone with a choice. Someone is targeted by the supernatural constantly and fights it off, but would much rather live a quite life away from it all. Someone without the resolve to become a hunter, but who still ends up with a high supernatural body count anyways. Is it still a major character change after his fifth/six/fiftieth kill?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would say any character who's got the sheer grit to survive 6+ combats with the supernatural would have to have the resolve to become a hunter. But rather than critiquing the example, lets work with it.<br /> <br /> I would say that yes, they should all be a significant point in his charachter development. You could play it as a gradual build up of the lack of sleep, the paranoia, just wearing him down day by day and treat the actual attacks as a convinient point to roll the dice on Integrity or you could just treat each attack as a signular Breaking Point. If I were playing that charachter I'd probably do both at once and have the charachter develop phobias based around each attack as an aid to roleplaying the more gradual day to day decline. I'd also ask the storyteller if we could work togeather to ensure there's unique and interesting traits in each attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156465#post1156465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that isn't the question. The question is &quot;Does it lead to major character development every single time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I think &quot;lead to&quot; is only part of the picture. If my charachter experiences a Breaking Point then I, as a player, will go out of my way to figure out how to create charachter development from that Breaking Point. <br /> <br /> It doesn't have to redirect the plot. If I'm playing a mortal private eye and discover evidence of supernatural involvement in my case I probably wont let the results decide if I drop the case there and then; especially not if the case is supposed to be the game. But if I roll badly I might have the PI start drinking (as is sterotypical) to gain the courage to go on. And if I roll well I might bring up a supernatural encounter he's forgotten/repressed/ignored from his backstory and ask the Storyteller if he could work in thematic parallels that could give my charachter a chance to find closure. <br /> <br /> But while I think that as a player I should be thinking up ways to create character development, I think the rules should meet me half way. Put Breaking Points in situations where it's easy(ier) to create character development and avoid throwing them around left right and center. I'm not asking for perfection, in a freeform system there's always going to be cases where a Breaking Point occurs at a time where it's hard to develop your character. But the blue book gives me a lot of flexibilty in saying what sort of things cause Breaking Points for my character which helps. I want Hunter to offer that same flexibility, mechanically I think you could get sufficient flexibility without a big change from the current playtest document. Just increase the number of modifications you're aloud from 1 to 3 or 5 and allow modifications at Tier 1. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156465#post1156465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Johnny is experienced. Before the game's start, he killed 10 men. In the course of the game, he kills another. Killing someone is always a breaking point, even for someone like Johnny. Kill 11 was a horrible person any vigilante would be happy to take out free of charge, and gives Johnny no reason to question his path. Then it goes on, is kill 12, 13, 14, ...30 etc all significant points of character development?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Johnny killing target 31 is unlikely to cause charachter development. Sure you can squeeze something out: This time it's personal, or this time the target's kid was watching. But that's a bit artifical. <br /> <br /> But I don't think this implies that the author's intent was that Breaking Points aren't supposed to be points of charachter development (distinct from &quot;major events in your charachter's lives&quot;). Rather I think that the authors had two conflicting intents: The first was that a Breaking Point is a moment of charachter development, that's why the blue book has you customise Breaking Points to your charachter. The second intent was that violence in the World of Darkness (at least for blue book mortals) is always a serious affair with reprocussions. <br /> <br /> I think both intents were good ideas. But there's a bit of weirdness when they collide.<br /> <br /> Mage incidentally introduced a third intent: Create a gnostic setting where the Lie is embedded into Sleeper's souls. This too can have a bit of weirdness when intents conflict, but if it's a typical mage game with no PC sleepers it won't come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T07:09:20-08:00","id":1156666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156387#post1156387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to be oriented so that you are supposed to get breaking points acting as a normal hunter, assuming you arn't completely jaded/absurdly careful. It isn't so much that they &quot;need freebies&quot;, its that &quot;you will get breaking points by being a normal member of this group&quot;. Being a member of the group means that you can ignore a few of them, but the system isn't designed so that you can get away with whatever because your group thinks it is OK.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, and I don't even disagree with it - except to the extent that the more uniform and/or rigid the Code is, the more one-tone-fits-all the game becomes. And the diversity of tones was one of the strongest elements of the first edition. I don't want to see it imperilled. But then I guess part of the point of this exercise is to test that.<br /> <br /> (Also I liked how the way the first edition Code functioned as a kind of z-splat for individual hunters).<br /> <br /> <br /> More generally: I think we've done all the core twelve now. Is it worth extending the exercise to the supplemental ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:32:12-08:00","id":1156692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get that, and I don't even disagree with it - except to the extent that the more uniform and/or rigid the Code is, the more one-tone-fits-all the game becomes. And the diversity of tones was one of the strongest elements of the first edition. I don't want to see it imperilled. But then I guess part of the point of this exercise is to test that. </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More generally: I think we've done all the core twelve now. Is it worth extending the exercise to the supplemental ones? </div> </div> </div>Don't think it is. As established sooner, the 12 core Conspiracies and Compacts will be the only ones listed in the 2E corebooks, so it's a bit early too start the supplemental ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:06:02-08:00","id":1156735,"title":"","content":"I wanted to share here a post from the PpB of the Playtest. It's an example of why assuming that the groups must always swap out the breaking points that conflict is not really a good assumption to make. (Also it's a good actual play in general and nice to see the playtest in practice rather than just theory.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1155285-ic-hunter-the-vigil-2e-playtest-the-lucifuge-s-doubting-souls?p=1156117#post1156117\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1155285-ic-hunter-the-vigil-2e-playtest-the-lucifuge-s-doubting-souls?p=1156117#post1156117\"> [IC] (Hunter: the Vigil 2e Playtest) The Lucifuge's Doubting Souls - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1155285-ic-hunter-the-vigil-2e-playtest-the-lucifuge-s-doubting-souls?p=1156117#post1156117\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1155285-ic-hunter-the-vigil-2e-playtest-the-lucifuge-s-doubting-souls?p=1156117#post1156117 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Scene 1: A Murder Most Foul Miskatonic Univeristy, Arkham, Massachusetts 1693 One Hour Ago Harvard may be the most prestigious university in the colonies, but </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T15:02:34-08:00","id":1156804,"title":"","content":".... Sorry, after reading this post, I fail to see how this post prove anything of the sort. I will admit it's well-transcribed, though.<br /> <br /> Feel free to explain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-07-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T15:45:13-08:00","id":1156817,"title":"","content":"It might have been better given the context all the way through, or maybe it is my bias already but I will try to illuminate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Micheal is not ready to acknowledge he is \u2018Son of Devil\u2019, </div> </div> </div>This point in particular is what struck me. Just because someone has agreed to be a Lucifuge does not mean that they are fully prepared for what that means in the long-term. In this case, despite the fact that getting powers from demonic sources is a core part of the Lucifuge, that doesn't mean that all members should immediately swap out the Breaking Point for a different one. It is good for the character and story that they continue to face this Breaking Point. Being a member of a Compact or Conspiracy is not a binary, one and done decision; it is something that the Hunter will have to deal with for their rest of their lives.<br /> <br /> As another example: Network 0. It has been said that they would HAVE to swap out the Breaking Point for 'causing a person to experience a breaking point for witnessing the supernatural', but I think that it is better to not swap it out and have the character come face to face with the realization that their ideology (&quot;we must expose the supernatural so people can be safe&quot;) is quite at odds with the reality of what doing those steps actually entails.<br /> <br /> By limiting the number of Tenet swaps (presumably one was chosen for a reason), it means that a given characters psyche can only cope with so much of what their ideology is making them do by simply ignoring it 'because their ideology says so'. Essentially, this is an argument against unrestrained swapping. Not that anyone was specifically calling for that, but I don't think specific numbers were discussed much. And once you agree that a limit makes sense at all, then it becomes a matter of figuring out what the limit should be based on what the stories you want the system to tell are and how much game complication you think can be handled for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 11-07-2017, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T15:56:34-08:00","id":1156819,"title":"","content":"Okay, now I <i>do</i> get your point. Thanks for clarifying^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T17:39:48-08:00","id":1156843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156817#post1156817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another example: Network 0. It has been said that they would HAVE to swap out the Breaking Point for 'causing a person to experience a breaking point for witnessing the supernatural', but I think that it is better to not swap it out and have the character come face to face with the realization that their ideology (&quot;we must expose the supernatural so people can be safe&quot;) is quite at odds with the reality of what doing those steps actually entails.</div> </div> </div> </div> To me that sounds like a character who's arc is supposed to result in them leaving Net0 (or becomes a reformer) because of moral differences. A perfectly good character, but I think anyone talking about Net0 characters in this thread had something very different in mind: A character who believes in and agrees with the Net0 ideology.<br /> <br /> Certainly, when I said it's a matter of principal that a Net0 character changes that breaking point I was doing so in the context of an Army of Truth hardliner, so someone who's already deep into Net0 and has already made up their mind about the ideology. <br /> <br /> The point I was making was mostly that you should change the parts of the code most at odds with your character's Compact backed ideology, not make the most mechanically optimal change. Not that all Net0 must do X.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156817#post1156817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think specific numbers were discussed much. And once you agree that a limit makes sense at all, then it becomes a matter of figuring out what the limit should be based on what the stories you want the system to tell are and how much game complication you think can be handled for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have been, the reason we went through all the core 12 too see which parts of the code we think they would change is to estimate a number. Personally I'd say 3 to 5. Though I've stated my support for a Bane/Tell drawback and would be ok with having no cap beyond the drawbacks building up.<br /> <br /> You said &quot;what stories you want to tell&quot;. To me Hunter doesn't have a central theme, each org has it's own theme, but the closest to a central theme would be that through numbers and teamwork mortals can play the same game as the supernatural.<br /> <br /> The loyalists of thule or the AKD can investigate the same mysteries as Mages. The Barret Commission can be as predatory as any Vampire. Les Mysteries have their own philosophy on flesh and spirit which they can argue for on equal terms to Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Your Net0 example works fine with 3 or 5 or unlimited changes, because he can choose not to modify his Code. But if you want the Code to accurately reflect, E.G. a typical Les Mysteries Hunter's mindset 1 change is not enough.<br /> <br /> In short, I want to tell lots of different kinds of story. So I want the rules to be flexible. Increasing the maximum changes provides that flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-07-2017, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T00:58:45-08:00","id":1156920,"title":"","content":"There is also to take into account that the variable hunter groups can all make for different kinds of stories individually. Task Force VALKYRIE allows you to do Men in Black/X-Files scifi stories. VASCU is for FBI/polar stories about agents hunting serial killers. The Cheiron Group if you wanna make stories \u00e0 la Resident Evil. And so on. And that's not even getting in what you can do with Cells including agents from multiple compacts and conspiracies.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, that game was never meant to tell a single type of Hunter story. Again, diversity is its strongest point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-08-2017, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T05:53:34-08:00","id":1156972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156692#post1156692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't think it is. As established sooner, the 12 core Conspiracies and Compacts will be the only ones listed in the 2E corebooks, so it's a bit early too start the supplemental ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core 12 minus one of the conspiracies,* plus Council of Bones, VASCU, and another compact.<br /> <br /> * We don't know which one, though my guess is either the Cheiron Group or Aegis kai Doru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156817#post1156817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This point in particular is what struck me. Just because someone has agreed to be a Lucifuge does not mean that they are fully prepared for what that means in the long-term. In this case, despite the fact that getting powers from demonic sources is a core part of the Lucifuge, that doesn't mean that all members should immediately swap out the Breaking Point for a different one. It is good for the character and story that they continue to face this Breaking Point. Being a member of a Compact or Conspiracy is not a binary, one and done decision; it is something that the Hunter will have to deal with for their rest of their lives.<br /> <br /> As another example: Network 0. It has been said that they would HAVE to swap out the Breaking Point for 'causing a person to experience a breaking point for witnessing the supernatural', but I think that it is better to not swap it out and have the character come face to face with the realization that their ideology (&quot;we must expose the supernatural so people can be safe&quot;) is quite at odds with the reality of what doing those steps actually entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good argument, but its logical upshot is that hunter groups shouldn't modify Code breaking points at all, since there will be no modifications that make <i>more</i> sense than those central to the group's mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T07:32:21-08:00","id":1156998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The core 12 minus one of the conspiracies,* plus Council of Bones, VASCU, and another compact.<br /> <br /> * We don't know which one, though my guess is either the Cheiron Group or Aegis kai Doru. </div> </div> </div>Oh? I didn't know about that.<br /> <br /> I sure as hell hope not, I absolutely love the Cheiron Group, and while the Aegis Kai Doru isn't my favourite per say, I do really like them conceptually. Then again, I pretty much love all of the 1e Conspiracies, so I guess no matter what, I'll be sad with the result. Are you sure it's not the Ashwood Abbey they are removing? They did say they were considering making them slashers.<br /> <br /> Also who are the Council of Bones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-08-2017, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T09:48:43-08:00","id":1157034,"title":"","content":"The Ashwood Abbey was confirmed to not get a full writeup in the Core, but they would have a short writeup (as is every group which is not a part of the core). They will not be presented as Slashers. The Council of Bones is the temporary name of a conspiracy of mediums and necromancers which speak with the dead, either helping them to move on or using them to find the monsters who killed them (I think- I don't remember the exact details). As for which of the groups is being removed from a full writeup (they should still get a short writeup), Monica has never clarified about the subject, but it is clear that if that is the case, it won't be a compact that they are removing. If I remember correctly, VASCU and another new Compact would be presented in the Slasher chapter, together with the Hunt Club as antagonists, and the Ashwood Abbey's place as &quot;core&quot; group would be replaced by another, new compact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T09:54:10-08:00","id":1157038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156843#post1156843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In short, I want to tell lots of different kinds of story. So I want the rules to be flexible. Increasing the maximum changes provides that flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1156920#post1156920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, that game was never meant to tell a single type of Hunter story. Again, diversity is its strongest point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be changing in 2e (the 2e lines have generally been about refocusing and refining the games already). It seems to me that the story that Hunter 2e is telling (generally) is &quot;How humans that have chosen to protect humanity in the face of the supernatural go about doing so, what that actually entails and how it affects them and their loved ones.&quot; That story is then told through the lens' of the various compacts and conspiracies to provide specific versions of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:17:26-08:00","id":1157045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ashwood Abbey was confirmed to not get a full writeup in the Core, but they would have a short writeup (as is every group which is not a part of the core). They will not be presented as Slashers. The Council of Bones is the temporary name of a conspiracy of mediums and necromancers which speak with the dead, either helping them to move on or using them to find the monsters who killed them (I think- I don't remember the exact details). As for which of the groups is being removed from a full writeup (they should still get a short writeup), Monica has never clarified about the subject, but it is clear that if that is the case, it won't be a compact that they are removing. If I remember correctly, VASCU and another new Compact would be presented in the Slasher chapter, together with the Hunt Club as antagonists, and the Ashwood Abbey's place as &quot;core&quot; group would be replaced by another, new compact. </div> </div> </div>Thank you Lostlight^^ Well, if none of the groups are gonna be removed from continuity, I am slightly less upset. There's at least still a chance they will be fleshed out in supplements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that might be changing in 2e (the 2e lines have generally been about refocusing and refining the games already). It seems to me that the story that Hunter 2e is telling (generally) is &quot;How humans that have chosen to protect humanity in the face of the supernatural go about doing so, what that actually entails and how it affects them and their loved ones.&quot; That story is then told through the lens' of the various compacts and conspiracies to provide specific versions of the story. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get that's what you think, and I still think it's not a good idea, because you lose the previously mentioned diversity then. I agree that the other 2e games have been refining the stories, but in this case, you'd really lost something to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-08-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T11:19:06-08:00","id":1157062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1157045#post1157045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you Lostlight^^ Well, if none of the groups are gonna be removed from continuity, I am slightly less upset. There's at least still a chance they will be fleshed out in supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monica has said that every hunter group released so far - not just those in the Hunter line, but those from Dark Eras too - will get some sort of write-up. I'd forgotten that Ashwood Abbey was getting swapped out as well - after being reminded, I think the compact replacing it is an existing one rather than a new one - if memory serves, there was a brief &quot;hope it's&quot; subthread (Maiden's Blood Sisterhood or Barrett Commission in my case, though the Bear Lodge would be a logical option, since they have similar motives to the Abbey).<br /> <br /> The reason I think it might be Cheiron that gets demoted is because the developers of Deviant want it for one of their conspiracies (though I don't know if Monica will sign off on that).<br /> <br /> The reason I think it might be Aegis kai Doru is that they've been somewhat overtaken by the rest of the ChroD in terms of what they best tie to - they make more sense as a Mummy-specific group now. Also, relics can be used by anyone, and are the Endowment most logical to find its way into the hands of multiple other groups - which diminishes Aegis's distinctiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T12:46:25-08:00","id":1157099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason I think it might be Cheiron that gets demoted is because the developers of Deviant want it for one of their conspiracies (though I don't know if Monica will sign off on that). </div> </div> </div>A reasonable assumption, I'll give you that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T02:14:24-08:00","id":1157483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1157038#post1157038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;How humans that have chosen to protect humanity in the face of the supernatural go about doing so, what that actually entails and how it affects them and their loved ones.&quot; That story is then told through the lens' of the various compacts and conspiracies to provide specific versions of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think that in order to tell that story Hunter will need more flexibility in it's mechanics and it will <i>definitely</i> need more flexibility in it's fluff (the Spade Sidebar). Werewolves are fictional, so you can say &quot;the wolf must hunt&quot; and players' suspension of disbelief will accept the idea that hunting is a universal psychological need for Werewolves.<br /> <br /> But Hunter's are human, and in the real world we know that humans have extremely diverse reactions to being put in identical situations. The game needs to be able to support all those different reactions if it's to tell the story of how the vigil affects Hunters and those they care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-10-2017, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T15:47:13-08:00","id":1157649,"title":"","content":"I haven't had a lot of time lately, and have been sick all morning and thus really fell behind on this thread &gt;_&gt;.<br /> <br /> As a final note, we should all remember that 1E Morality was much more limited then the current Code and Integrity system even taking into account the 1E Code and the optional &quot;Monsters Don't Count&quot; rule. I find it hard to believe that the 2E code- a flexible system- would be unable to do some of the same things the inflexible 1E system. In fact, most of the complaints relate to how similar it is is to 1E in many respects- such as &quot;applying the same ideology to everyone&quot;. There is no way that the current code would reduce ideological diversity compared to 1E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T16:13:04-08:00","id":1157653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1157649#post1157649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't had a lot of time lately, and have been sick all morning and thus really fell behind on this thread &gt;_&gt;.<br /> <br /> As a final note, we should all remember that 1E Morality was much more limited then the current Code and Integrity system even taking into account the 1E Code and the optional &quot;Monsters Don't Count&quot; rule. I find it hard to believe that the 2E code- a flexible system- would be unable to do some of the same things the inflexible 1E system. In fact, most of the complaints relate to how similar it is is to 1E in many respects- such as &quot;applying the same ideology to everyone&quot;. There is no way that the current code would reduce ideological diversity compared to 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>...yeaaaa honestly that's been my main issue with some of the views in this thread.<br /> <br /> For me, it sounds like people are coming from the perspective that what we've of the 2E Code is somehow the most complete and final version of the system, and are immediately assuming that HtV2e is going to be dead on arrival due to this iteration not living up to the themes on what made people like about HtV1e.<br /> <br /> Which I personally don't think so.<br /> <br /> I think what we've got right now is a deliberately bare-bones version of the Code that is still a work in progress. That Monica, via the playtest, just wanted to see how the most basic form of the Code would work in play, take in feedback and fix any issues that might have cropped up, and THEN start layering on more advanced rules and other complexities on the basic system. Which would include stuff like Compact and Conspiracy-exclusive Codes and breaking points.<br /> <br /> Can't have a good gameplay system unless if you're sure you have a strong foundation in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T16:24:35-08:00","id":1157656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1154066-hunter-2ed-the-code?p=1157653#post1157653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, it sounds like people are coming from the perspective that what we've of the 2E Code is somehow the most complete and final version of the system, and are immediately assuming that HtV2e is going to be dead on arrival due to this iteration not living up to the themes on what made people like about HtV1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's a single person in this thread who thinks it's going to be &quot;dead on arrival.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}